{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyWwvomB1Yus6C5rdpb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KASyMahPzvYJN6jLY2qeJq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd $HOME/.cache/plan-x193f88-research/hub/repo/lib/hub && ls -la examples; cat retrofit.md; head -60 session.js","description":"Read hub retrofit notes, examples list, and client header"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7491,"cache_read_input_tokens":91534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7491},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40","uuid":"2160a1c1-1409-48de-a516-dddd15a8ee04","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:55:06.814Z","request_id":"req_011CggyWwhuywBa2eRwQ6wTf","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01KASyMahPzvYJN6jLY2qeJq":{"command":"cd $HOME/.cache/plan-x193f88-research/hub/repo/lib/hub && ls -la examples; cat retrofit.md; head -60 session.js","description":"Read hub retrofit notes, examples list, and client header"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KASyMahPzvYJN6jLY2qeJq","type":"tool_result","content":"total 112\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 17:53 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 17:53 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 33330 Nov  3 17:53 arena.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 29231 Nov  3 17:53 ghost.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 33011 Nov  3 17:53 parallel.html\n# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n\n---\n\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\n\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\nagainst it:\n\n<protocol>\n{{contract}}\n</protocol>\n\nDo only this:\n\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\n   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press\n   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\n   `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })` once. In\n   `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current score at once if the run is\n   still going.\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\n\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\nlike). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the\ngame an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for\neither. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol\ndescribes; you need not run them, the hub does.\n\nIf the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one\nline: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.\n\nOtherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line\nyou changed.\n\n{{notes}}\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40","uuid":"98bcc293-aea6-4442-8f30-ff4e2c1d89b9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:55:07.117Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"total 112\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 17:53 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 17:53 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 33330 Nov  3 17:53 arena.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 29231 Nov  3 17:53 ghost.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 33011 Nov  3 17:53 parallel.html\n# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n\n---\n\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\n\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\nagainst it:\n\n<protocol>\n{{contract}}\n</protocol>\n\nDo only this:\n\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\n   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press\n   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\n   `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })` once. In\n   `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current score at once if the run is\n   still going.\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\n\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\nlike). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the\ngame an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for\neither. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol\ndescribes; you need not run them, the hub does.\n\nIf the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one\nline: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.\n\nOtherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line\nyou changed.\n\n{{notes}}\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174731__x326e4b/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":355,"oldLines":3,"newStart":355,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CggyZu9xBrxqg888gD8s7\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4722,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":163349,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":4722},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"bbb0a1ea-12f9-46f9-9677-d2d253a967c8\",\"uuid\":\"b226e59a-a043-48c6-a42a-84172f5da449\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T00:55:01.286Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CggyZtwZEtrwRf8Fcnz8N\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":5309,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CggyZu9xBrxqg888gD8s7\",\"type\"