{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CPDUzr1NKGkEEGBeNBji5t","type":"tool_result","content":"games/grand-theft-five-finger-drive-sd/docs/PLAN.md\ngames/grand-theft-five-finger-drive-sd/docs/PLAN.md:686:- `hub:type`: `Game`.\ngames/grand-theft-five-finger-drive-sd/docs/PLAN.md:687:- `hub:genre`: use the hub's existing suitable action-game value.\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40","uuid":"252e8df4-8477-460e-a753-7ed2523fa601","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:55:23.841Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"games/grand-theft-five-finger-drive-sd/docs/PLAN.md\ngames/grand-theft-five-finger-drive-sd/docs/PLAN.md:686:- `hub:type`: `Game`.\ngames/grand-theft-five-finger-drive-sd/docs/PLAN.md:687:- `hub:genre`: use the hub's existing suitable action-game value.","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174746__xe37f55/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":302,"oldLines":3,"newStart":302,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CggyandpSqZvZ9uBegsRu\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_016NMLKfwJ58cqXHdNe8x2zf\",\"name\":\"WebFetch\",\"input\":{\"url\":\"https://www.arcade-history.com/game/1887/\",\"prompt\":\"Extract all gameplay details about the arcade Operation Wolf: story text, stage list and what completing each stage does (bonuses to later stages: e.g. fewer enemies, health restored, ammo restored), items/power-ups and how they're obtained, enemy types, civilians and penalties, hostages, the ending and ranking, HUD elements, the cabinet's gun and recoil, music/sound notes, and any trivia (e.g. the main character's name, the interrogation scene). Give specifics.\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":623,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":156564,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":623},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"d128962a-bd2b-4da0-bea3-10df26a8e825\",\"uuid\":\"470b7b3d-111a-401b-8e6d-fcd2b6ed3032\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T00:55:08.146Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CggyanRRhRmnvaHbbBTEp\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_016NMLKfwJ58cqXHdNe8x2zf\":{\"url\":\"https://www.arcade-history.com/game/1887/\",\"prompt\":\"Extract all gameplay details about the arcade Operation Wolf: story text, stage list and what completing each stage does (bonuses to later stages: e.g. fewer enemies, health restored, ammo restored), items/power-ups and how they're obtained, enemy types, civilians and penalties, hostages, the ending and ranking, HUD elements, the cabinet's gun and recoil, music/sound notes, and any trivia (e.g. the main character's name, the interrogation scene). Give specifics.\"}}}"," {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_016NMLKfwJ58cqXHdNe8x2zf\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"**Story:** You play Special Forces operative 'Roy Adams', who must infiltrate and capture six heavily fortified bases and rescue five trapped hostages.\\n\\n**Stages (in order):** Communication Setup, Jungle, Village, Powder Magazine, Concentration Camp, Airport.\\n\\n**Stage rewards and effects:**\\n- **Powder Magazine:** Completing it refills ammo and grenades to maximum.\\n- **Village:** Completing it restores a large amount of damage (the tips say 20 points).\\n- **Other stages:** Completing each restores a small amount (the tips say 3 points).\\n- **Airport:** A bonus is awarded based on how many hostages board the plane.\\n- The page does not say that clearing stages reduces enemy counts in later stages.\\n\\n**Enemies:**\\n- Soldiers, who throw hand grenades and knives.\\n- Vehicles, which fire missiles and launch rockets.\\n- Helicopters, which can be shot down for points. The tips say they take many hits to destroy.\\n- Large blond soldiers with machine guns, who go down quickly if shot in the face (tips).\\n- Mortar crews behind sandbags (tips).\\n\\n**Civilians and hostages:**\\n- Shooting a civilian or hostage increases the damage bar.\\n- Hostages appear in the Concentration Camp stage, where the player must protect them while they run to safety.\\n- In the Airport stage, hostages run toward an airplane hatch while enemies attack.\\n\\n**Items and power-ups:**\\n- **Ammo and grenades:** Obtained by shooting barrels and crates. Both are limited.\\n- **High-powered machine gun:** Occasionally appears. It gives unlimited ammo and a faster rate of fire for 10 seconds.\\n- **Energy boost:** Appears randomly. Shooting it reduces damage by five points.\\n- **Power drinks:** Mentioned in the tips as items that can appear.\\n- **Farm animals:** Chickens and pigs occasionally cross the screen. Shooting them reveals bonuses such as health or ammo.\\n\\n**Penalties:** Getting hit, or shooting a civilian or hostage, raises the damage bar.\\n\\n**Game over:** The game ends if the damage bar fills completely or if you run out of both ammo and grenades.\\n\\n**Progression:** After completing the game, you return to the first mission at a higher difficulty.\\n\\n**HUD:** A damage bar appears to the right of the main play screen.\\n\\n**Ending and ranking:** The page does not describe an ending sequence or a ranking system. It lists Mark Twitty as the official record holder with 212,350 points.\\n\\n**Cabinet and controls:** One player, a lightgun control, and two buttons. The page does not mention gun recoil.\\n\\n**Music and sound:**\\n- Music by Hiroshi Tuda.\\n- Sound chips: Yamaha YM2151 and two OKI MSM5205 chips.\\n- Pony Canyon / Scitron released a limited-edition soundtrack album on June 21, 1988.\\n\\n**Trivia:**\\n- Released November 1987; developed by East Technology.\\n- A bootleg is known as Operation Bear.\\n- The page does not mention an interrogation scene.\\n\\n**Discrepancies:** The tips refer to the \\\"Ammo Dump\\\" as stage four and the first stage as \\\"enemy radar,\\\" while the main text names the stages Powder Magazine and Communication Setup.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"d128962a-bd2b-4da0-bea3-10df26a8e825\",\"uuid\":\"85be676f-e053-4a73-b1fa-579b7f562da9\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T00:55:20.928Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"bytes\":63256,\"code\":200,\"codeText\":\"OK\",\"result\":\"**Story:** You play Special Forces operative 'Roy Adams', who must infiltrate and capture six heavily fortified bases and rescue five trapped hostages.\\n\\n**Stages (in order):** Communication Setup, Jungle, Village, Powder Magazine, Concentration Camp, Airport.\\n\\n**Stage rewards and effects:**\\n- **Powder Magazine:** Completing it refills ammo and grenades to maximum.\\n- **Village:** Completing it restores a large amount of damage (the tips say 20 points).\\n- **Other stages:** Completing each restores a small amount (the tips say 3 points).\\n- **Airport:** A bonus is awarded based on how many hostages board the plane.\\n- The page does not say that clearing stages reduces enemy counts in later stages.\\n\\n**Enemies:**\\n- Soldiers, who throw hand grenades and knives.\\n- Vehicles, which fire missiles and launch rockets.\\n- Helicopters, which can be shot down for points. The tips say they take many hits to destroy.\\n- Large blond soldiers with machine guns, who go down quickly if shot in the face (tips).\\n- Mortar crews behind sandbags (tips).\\n\\n**Civilians and hostages:**\\n- Shooting a civilian or hostage increases the damage bar.\\n- Hostages appear in the Concentration Camp stage, where the player must protect them while they run to safety.\\n- In the Airport stage, hostages run toward an airplane hatch while enemies attack.\\n\\n**Items and power-ups:**\\n- **Ammo and grenades:** Obtained by shooting barrels and crates. Both are limited.\\n- **High-powered machine gun:** Occasionally appears. It gives unlimited ammo and a faster rate of fire for 10 seconds.\\n- **Energy boost:** Appears randomly. Shooting it reduces damage by five points.\\n- **Power drinks:** Mentioned in the tips as items that can appear.\\n- **Farm animals:** Chickens and pigs occasionally cross the screen. Shooting them reveals bonuses such as health or ammo.\\n\\n**Penalties:** Getting hit, or shooting a civilian or hostage, raises the damage bar.\\n\\n**Game over:** The game ends if the damage bar fills completely or if you run out of both ammo and grenades.\\n\\n**Progression:** After completing the game, you return to the first mission at a higher difficulty.\\n\\n**HUD:** A damage bar appears to the right of the main play screen.\\n\\n**Ending and ranking:** The page does not describe an ending sequence or a ranking system. It lists Mark Twitty as the official record holder with 212,350 points.\\n\\n**Cabinet and controls:** One player, a lightgun control, and two buttons. The page does not mention gun recoil.\\n\\n**Music and sound:**\\n- Music by Hiroshi Tuda.\\n- Sound chips: Yamaha YM2151 and two OKI MSM5205 chips.\\n- Pony Canyon / Scitron released a limited-edition soundtrack album on June 21, 1988.\\n\\n**Trivia:**\\n- Released November 1987; developed by East Technology.\\n- A bootleg is known as Operation Bear.\\n- The page does not mention an interrogation scene.\\n\\n**Discrepancies:** The tips refer to the \\\"Ammo Dump\\\" as stage four and the first stage as \\\"enemy radar,\\\" while the main text names the stages Powder Magazine and Communication Setup.\",\"durationMs\":12779,\"url\":\"https://www.arcade-history.com/game/1887/\"},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_016NMLKfwJ58cqXHdNe8x2zf\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"d128962a-bd2b-4da0-bea3-10df26a8e825\",\"uuid\":\"bb661910-d87a-40f2-a7ff-90c7000b4e22\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":150,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"d128962a-bd2b-4da0-bea3-10df26a8e825\",\"uuid\":\"d450714c-cbc0-447b-99f3-d2670091f313\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":273,"oldLines":3,"newStart":273,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":950,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619\",\"uuid\":\"991c8bcb-b956-47fa-8db3-17841ab4cb65\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1100,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619\",\"uuid\":\"8cfd2df1-4e35-4818-804b-76703407fcf9\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1200,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619\",\"uuid\":\"58c42cab-fb37-4c11-b557-b94dbf05cdc1\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1300,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619\",\"uuid\":\"8e8a35c8-ead2-4306-a012-15c1cfb68666\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":365,"oldLines":3,"newStart":365,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":8350,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941\",\"uuid\":\"4da3f2ba-5e1f-425c-ad1c-35149ed6f8eb\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":8450,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941\",\"uuid\":\"1c7663b5-69fd-41ac-9e9f-36a43655c98a\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":8550,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941\",\"uuid\":\"b454dac4-fbef-4481-81d7-6565047e1702\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":8700,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"67077d04-87f0-4158-a4f5-843d0a0e9941\",\"uuid\":\"79cb8919-73f0-47c6-a00a-67cc70b77efa\"}"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174746__xe37f55/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174813__x2e02c0/agent.out"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CPDUzr1NKGkEEGBeNBji5t","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
