{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyoqYodYPpBmeLwAWoN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N2zXsDpzgXrob3iH2qjQdD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd $HOME/.cache/plan-x193f88-research/hub/repo && sed -n 1,40p docs/curation-2026-09-28.md; sed -n 235,260p README.md","description":"Read hub curation notes about CDN bundles and README limits"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1666,"cache_read_input_tokens":160737,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1666},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40","uuid":"4c67436b-08b0-4220-8f4a-c880df6e2d31","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:58:03.224Z","request_id":"req_011CggyoqL9TVm7RGKPmGKf9","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01N2zXsDpzgXrob3iH2qjQdD":{"command":"cd $HOME/.cache/plan-x193f88-research/hub/repo && sed -n 1,40p docs/curation-2026-09-28.md; sed -n 235,260p README.md","description":"Read hub curation notes about CDN bundles and README limits"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N2zXsDpzgXrob3iH2qjQdD","type":"tool_result","content":"# Library import — 28 Sep 2026\n\n`C:\\dev\\GPT-games` held 336 game pages and 4 source zips, already renamed by\nsource (its own `SOURCE-REVIEW.md` explains the source guesses). The wall held\n245 games. Every file on both sides was compared, and each game now appears\nonce, in its newest version, under the library's naming convention\n(`Source-Title-YYYY-MM-DD-model.html`, see the README).\n\n**342** games in the catalogue · **104** new (98 on the wall, 6 hidden) · **244** kept and renamed · **7** left out\n\n## How the two sides were matched\n\n1. **Byte-identical** (SHA-256): 149 files. The wall's file was renamed to the folder's name.\n2. **Same title, same game code**: 74 files. The folder's copy is an offline\n   bundle of the same build: the libraries a page loads from a CDN (three.js,\n   Babylon.js, React) are inlined as base64, and the code is re-emitted by a\n   bundler. The bundle adds no game text of its own, only library code, so they\n   are one version of one game. The wall keeps its lean build, renamed:\n   *HOT TREADS* is 115 KB on the wall and 22.8 MB bundled.\n   Project folders (Aetherfall, Pennywing, Runeclash…) stay folders.\n3. **Same title, the wall's build is newer**: kept the wall's build, renamed.\n   - Little World — Sing, play, grow — hub build is newer (voice storage schema v2 vs v1)\n   - Plus One — A life of your own — hub build has session content the GPT copy lacks\n   - Singularity Tycoon — A history of intelligence — hub build has lessons and win conditions the GPT copy lacks\n4. **Different titles, one lineage**: text shared between files (with library\n   strings discounted) found the few renamed iterations; each was read to see\n   which is newer.\n5. **Everything else is a separate game** — including same-idea attempts whose\n   code is unrelated (the two BLACKWELLs, Kinetic and Kinetic Studio, Form and\n   Form Lab, the Endless Sky and Final Fantasy sets), as in the first curation.\n\n## Left out\n\n| File | Why |\n|---|---|\n| `Daytona-USA-Days-of-Daytona-USA-Rival-Battle-II-2026-09-07-model-unknown.html` | older build (v5.0) of Days of Daytona USA; the wall keeps v12.0, the audited build |\n| `Out-Run-RUNOUT-The-coast-is-calling-2026-09-07-model-unknown.html` | older iteration of SUPER RUNOUT (2026-09-11), which is on the wall |\n| `Star-Fox-Vanguard-Wing-2026-09-10-model-unknown.html` | a \"Boot page ready.\" placeholder (Milestone 0), not a game |\n| `original-Hudson-s-little-kitchen-Learn-together-2026-09-17-model-unknown.html` | superseded by Hudson's little home, which is the kitchen plus a family room |\n| `original-Mandel-A-voxel-fractal-explorer-Attempt-01-2026-09-12-model-unknown.html` | earlier build of Mandel 3D (same code, before the orbit camera) |\nin and hitting reload is the whole loop. (It remembers each file's parsed head\nuntil the file changes, so that stays instant at four hundred games.)\n\n```bash\npnpm test         # parsers, layout rules, zip reading, search and filters, Couch and Catalogue logic\npnpm scan         # rebuild data/games.json by hand; --list prints every game\npnpm dev --host 0.0.0.0   # reach it from your phone on the same wifi\n```\n\nThe scan's output is worth a glance after a big import. Past forty games it\nprints a summary instead of every title, followed by anything that needs you:\nfiles too large for GitHub, projects that still load files from the site root,\nproject folders whose extra pages might really be separate games.\n\n## Playing\n\nClicking a cabinet runs the game **inside** the hub, so leaving it puts you back\non the wall with your scroll position, search and filters exactly as you left\nthem. Nothing is written into a game file to make that work — the hub only\nattaches listeners to the game's document, which it is allowed to do because\nthe games are served from the same origin.\n\nThe bar in the corner has three buttons: **←** back to the wall, **🎲** roll\nanother random game from what the wall was showing, and **✕**. A tap of ✕\nfolds the bar down to just the ✕ (tap again to bring it back); holding it\nremoves the bar entirely until the hub is reloaded. The browser's Back button\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40","uuid":"da6c38cf-a66a-4e13-b55c-968f8744eb70","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:58:03.596Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Library import — 28 Sep 2026\n\n`C:\\dev\\GPT-games` held 336 game pages and 4 source zips, already renamed by\nsource (its own `SOURCE-REVIEW.md` explains the source guesses). The wall held\n245 games. Every file on both sides was compared, and each game now appears\nonce, in its newest version, under the library's naming convention\n(`Source-Title-YYYY-MM-DD-model.html`, see the README).\n\n**342** games in the catalogue · **104** new (98 on the wall, 6 hidden) · **244** kept and renamed · **7** left out\n\n## How the two sides were matched\n\n1. **Byte-identical** (SHA-256): 149 files. The wall's file was renamed to the folder's name.\n2. **Same title, same game code**: 74 files. The folder's copy is an offline\n   bundle of the same build: the libraries a page loads from a CDN (three.js,\n   Babylon.js, React) are inlined as base64, and the code is re-emitted by a\n   bundler. The bundle adds no game text of its own, only library code, so they\n   are one version of one game. The wall keeps its lean build, renamed:\n   *HOT TREADS* is 115 KB on the wall and 22.8 MB bundled.\n   Project folders (Aetherfall, Pennywing, Runeclash…) stay folders.\n3. **Same title, the wall's build is newer**: kept the wall's build, renamed.\n   - Little World — Sing, play, grow — hub build is newer (voice storage schema v2 vs v1)\n   - Plus One — A life of your own — hub build has session content the GPT copy lacks\n   - Singularity Tycoon — A history of intelligence — hub build has lessons and win conditions the GPT copy lacks\n4. **Different titles, one lineage**: text shared between files (with library\n   strings discounted) found the few renamed iterations; each was read to see\n   which is newer.\n5. **Everything else is a separate game** — including same-idea attempts whose\n   code is unrelated (the two BLACKWELLs, Kinetic and Kinetic Studio, Form and\n   Form Lab, the Endless Sky and Final Fantasy sets), as in the first curation.\n\n## Left out\n\n| File | Why |\n|---|---|\n| `Daytona-USA-Days-of-Daytona-USA-Rival-Battle-II-2026-09-07-model-unknown.html` | older build (v5.0) of Days of Daytona USA; the wall keeps v12.0, the audited build |\n| `Out-Run-RUNOUT-The-coast-is-calling-2026-09-07-model-unknown.html` | older iteration of SUPER RUNOUT (2026-09-11), which is on the wall |\n| `Star-Fox-Vanguard-Wing-2026-09-10-model-unknown.html` | a \"Boot page ready.\" placeholder (Milestone 0), not a game |\n| `original-Hudson-s-little-kitchen-Learn-together-2026-09-17-model-unknown.html` | superseded by Hudson's little home, which is the kitchen plus a family room |\n| `original-Mandel-A-voxel-fractal-explorer-Attempt-01-2026-09-12-model-unknown.html` | earlier build of Mandel 3D (same code, before the orbit camera) |\nin and hitting reload is the whole loop. (It remembers each file's parsed head\nuntil the file changes, so that stays instant at four hundred games.)\n\n```bash\npnpm test         # parsers, layout rules, zip reading, search and filters, Couch and Catalogue logic\npnpm scan         # rebuild data/games.json by hand; --list prints every game\npnpm dev --host 0.0.0.0   # reach it from your phone on the same wifi\n```\n\nThe scan's output is worth a glance after a big import. Past forty games it\nprints a summary instead of every title, followed by anything that needs you:\nfiles too large for GitHub, projects that still load files from the site root,\nproject folders whose extra pages might really be separate games.\n\n## Playing\n\nClicking a cabinet runs the game **inside** the hub, so leaving it puts you back\non the wall with your scroll position, search and filters exactly as you left\nthem. Nothing is written into a game file to make that work — the hub only\nattaches listeners to the game's document, which it is allowed to do because\nthe games are served from the same origin.\n\nThe bar in the corner has three buttons: **←** back to the wall, **🎲** roll\nanother random game from what the wall was showing, and **✕**. A tap of ✕\nfolds the bar down to just the ✕ (tap again to bring it back); holding it\nremoves the bar entirely until the hub is reloaded. The browser's Back button","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174743__x8534bd/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":279,"oldLines":3,"newStart":279,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":69,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":1,\"session_id\":\"6ff8a465-a3dc-4463-ad61-3d7e016e47ef\",\"uuid\":\"8da4e565-d3f4-4036-a46e-5079b454667e\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":230,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":161,\"session_id\":\"6ff8a465-a3dc-4463-ad61-3d7e016e47ef\",\"uuid\":\"91556616-f9d7-458b-b72c-3f527fe4a43d\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cggyjo6MJ6txyWEdgVjpo\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"I've got the source's rules (30-second clock, half and full points, double counter points, time-out decisions, senpai practice, bonus stages, and rank tiers), and I'm reading the engine gui