n: `node tools/cmu.mjs ledger kick` searches it, or grep `src/mocap/catalogs/cmu-takes.tsv`.\nAI_GUIDE.md:636:- **Take** the clips you want into a small set of your own: `node tools/anim-set.mjs src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js examples/cmu-lib/CMU_10.js --clips Idle_Loop,10_01 --name MINE --out mine.js` (the curated sets are `src/mocap/sets/<set>.js`; take `NN_xx` is in `examples/cmu-lib/CMU_<NN>.js`). A clip copied by hand also needs its set's preamble (its `sources`, the bodies it was measured on), so use the tool when you can run commands.\nAI_GUIDE.md:637:- **Play** it: load `src/mocap/readable.js`, `src/mocap/mocap.js` and the set after the engine, then `const lib = Mocap.load(MOCAP.MINE); Mocap.drive(rig, lib);` once, and each step `rig.mocap = lib.sample(lib.clip('Idle_Loop'), t)` before `rig.update`. `rig.mocapW` (0 to 1) fades a clip in and out over the rig's own animation, `rig.mocapMask = 'upper'` plays only the chest, head and arms over the rig's own walk, and `lib.moveAt(clip, t)` says how far a travelling clip has carried the body.\nAPI-INDEX.md:91:- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\nAPI-INDEX.md:496:- `game.script(fn, o)` †: run a coroutine on game time, in the update step: game.script(function* (game) { yield .5; yield E.until(() => door.open); yield game.tween(cam, { y: 0 }, 1); yield E.all([a, b]); ... }, { keep }). Each yield waits: a number (seconds), nothing (one step), a condition (a function, or E.until(fn)), a tween or script (until it is done), a generator (run as a script of its own, and waited for), E.all([...]) or E.any([...]) (each of these). It runs at once to its first yield. Cutscenes, boss patterns, wave timelines, tutorials, attract modes. Returns the Script\nAPI-INDEX.md:645:- `slash.start(canCancel = false)`: begin a swing if idle (or when canCancel and already recovering). Returns true if it started\nAPI-INDEX.md:646:- `slash.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\nAPI-INDEX.md:650:- `slash.phase = null`: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', or null when idle\nAPI-INDEX.md:660:- `combo.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\nAPI-INDEX.md:662:- `combo.idle = 99`: seconds since the last hit ended\nAPI-INDEX.md:700:- `rig.t`: seconds of its own clock (idle breathing, blinks)\nAPI-INDEX.md:1220:## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\nAPI-INDEX.md:1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\nAPI-INDEX.md:1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\nAPI-INDEX.md:1233:- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\nAPI-INDEX.md:1234:- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\nAPI.md:130:With no code: a **pause menu** on pausable scenes (Resume, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title; keys, mouse, gamepad and touch), **settings** saved per game (`game.settings`: volume, music, effects, mute, reduce motion, screen shake and flashes, pixel scaling, a screen filter: clean, scanlines or CRT, the frame rate: Auto, 60 or Full, and its readout), **controls** the player rebinds (conflicts said first; dead zone, invert aim, button symbols, vibration; touch button side, size, opacity), **full screen** (a phone's first tap and each game started by a tap, a top-right button, the menu; turning it off is remembered), a **menu button** at the top right (on a touch screen it stays in play: it is the touch START), a **way out** of every menu screen (close, back, a sideways swipe), the **back gesture** stepping back in the game (`game.back()`: a menu screen closes, play pauses) before it leaves the page, **pausing** when the page is hidden or the controller unplugs, and a page set up for phones (safe areas, no scrolling, zooming or pull to refresh on the canvas).\nAPI.md:158:- Font (5x7 proportional with lower case; `font: 'tiny'` for 3x5): `E.font.text(g, str, x, y, color, { outline, shadow, gradient, scale, align, wrap, font })`, `E.font.title(g, str, x, y, { scale, colors, outline, depth, depthColor, align })`, `E.font.width(str, opts)`, `E.font.lineHeight(opts)`, `E.font.wrap(str, maxW, opts)`. Glyphs: ASCII plus `♥ ★ ← → ↑ ↓ • × ♪ ▸ ©`.\nAPI-INDEX.md:283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\nAPI-INDEX.md:297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\nAPI-INDEX.md:326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\nAPI-INDEX.md:360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":488,"oldLines":3,"newStart":488,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3750,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d\",\"uuid\":\"6228d1c8-1083-4f7c-8a74-425b96db2063\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3850,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d\",\"uuid\":\"4a40adfc-a374-4e71-bbd8-25a02c7dc93d\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3950,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d\",\"uuid\":\"2e447c0c-72f2-44bb-a3b4-b0045ed493b9\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":4050,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"5176bdbd-8f33-407b-b89e-9fc1c745933d\",\"uuid\":\"895adc7a-bff5-4a63-91be-ab572365c907\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174755__x531263/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":429,"oldLines":3,"newStart":429,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_014hDJjTPnAV6t6WQXJHVvHe\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"// my-3D2dge game checker: loads a game in a headless browser, presses start, plays it for a\\n// moment, switches through the game's camera views, and reports errors, warnings, frame rate,\\n// how much of the window the picture covers (covers: 1 = no black bars), how much is actually on screen, and screenshots.\\n//\\n// Setup (once):   npm install          (installs Playwright)\\n//                 npx playwright install chromium\\n// Usage:          node tools/check.mjs path/to/game.html[#scene] [--seconds 4] [--out check-output] [--size 390x844@3]\\n//                 (--size: the window in CSS pixels and its pixel density; @2 and up is a phone or tablet, with touch)\\n// Exit code is 1 if the page threw any error or never drew anything, so agents and CI can rely on it.\\n// A game that sets game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} } } gets its snapshot printed after play (its own state:\\n// the hero, the objective, what an agent needs to see the game is where it should be).\\nimport { chromium } from 'playwright';\\nimport { mkdirSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { resolve, join } from 'node:path';\\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\\n\\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\\nconst file = args.find(a => !a.startsWith('--') && !/^\\\\d+(\\\\.\\\\d+)?$/.test(a));\\nconst opt = (name, def) => { const i = args.indexOf('--' + name); return i >= 0 ? args[i + 1] : def; };\\nif (!file) { console.error('Usage: node tools/check.mjs path/to/game.html [--seconds 4] [--out check-output]'); process.exit(2); }\\nconst seconds = +opt('seconds', 4), out = resolve(opt('out', 'check-output'));\\nconst [, sw, sh, sd] = (opt('size', '1280x720') || '').match(/^(\\\\d+)x(\\\\d+)(?:@(\\\\d+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?))?$/) || [0, 1280, 720];\\nconst dpr = +(sd || 1), size = { viewport: { width: +sw, height: +sh }, deviceScaleFactor: dpr, ...(dpr >= 2 && { isMobile: true, hasTouch: true }) };\\nmkdirSync(out, { recursive: true });\\n\\nconst browser = await chromium.launch({ executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined, args: ['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'] });\\nconst page = await browser.newPage(size);\\nconst errors = [], warnings = [], engineWarnings = [], external = new Set();\\npage.on('pageerror', e => errors.push(String(e && e.stack || e)));\\npage.on('console', m => {\\n=====\\n// A headless test of the genre kits: each kit's game runs in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where there is no\\n// DOM) after the scripts its page loads before it (the engine, an asset set), starts its slice (the page's deep link,\\n// #<id>), plays two seconds, then runs the slice's proof twice: run(600), scripted play from a seed, gives a hash of how\\n// it went, the same every time. Run it: node kits/test.mjs [id ...] (every kit without one; exit code 1 on a failure).\\n// A game copied from a kit tests the same way: a kit's code reads three of the page's globals, given stand-ins here\\n// (window, addEventListener, location); drive it with game.advance and input.tap / hold, as game/test.mjs does.\\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\\nimport { readFileSync, readdirSync } from 'node:fs';\\n\\nconst here = new URL('./', import.meta.url), read = f => readFileSync(new URL(f, here), 'utf8');\\nconst ids = process.argv.slice(2).length ? process.argv.slice(2) : readdirSync(here).filter(f => f.endsWith('.html')).map(f => f.slice(0, -5)).sort();\\nlet failed = 0;\\nfor (const id of ids) {\\n  const ctx = { console: { log() {}, info() {}, warn() {}, error: console.error }, addEventListener() {}, location: { hash: '#' + id } };\\n  ctx.window = ctx; vm.createContext(ctx);\\n  try {\\n    // the page's scripts, in its order: ../my-3d2dge.js, any asset set, then the kit's game\\n    for (const [, src] of read(id + '.html').matchAll(/<script src=\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\"><\\\\/script>/g)) vm.runInContext(read(src), ctx, { filename: src });\\n    const game = ctx.My3D2dge.current, slice = ctx.__game.scenes[id];\\n    game.advance(2);\\n    const scene = game.sceneName, a = slice.run(600), b = slice.run(600), errors = game.errors.map(e => e.message), ok = a === b && !errors.length;\\n    console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + id + ': ' + scene + ' plays; its proof twice ' + (a === b ? 'the same (' + a + ')' : a + ', then ' + b) + (errors.length ? '; errors: ' + errors.join(' | ') : ''));\\n    if (!ok) failed++;\\n  } catch (e) { console.log('FAIL ' + id + ': ' + (e && e.stack || e).toString().split('\\\\n').slice(0, 3).join(' / ')); failed++; }\\n}\\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} of ${ids.length} kit(s) failed` : `all ${ids.length} kit(s) passed`);\\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174755__x531263/work\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f93111a9-5060-4eb2-b5bf-6a1585c61e13\",\"uuid\":\"b0db1eb4-37dc-48a8-934d-32e1f8dd5eda\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T00:58:33.933Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"// my-3D2dge game checker: loads a game in a headless browser, presses start, plays it for a\\n// moment, switches through the game's camera views, and reports errors, warnings, frame rate,\\n// how much of the window the picture covers (covers: 1 = no black bars), how much is actually on screen, and screenshots.\\n//\\n// Setup (once):   npm install          (installs Playwright)\\n//                 npx playwright install chromium\\n// Usage:          node tools/check.mjs path/to/game.html[#scene] [--seconds 4] [--out check-output] [--size 390x844@3]\\n//                 (--size: the window in CSS pixels and its pixel density; @2 and up is a phone or tablet, with touch)\\n// Exit code is 1 if the page threw any error or never drew anything, so agents and CI can rely on it.\\n// A game that sets game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} } } gets its snapshot printed after play (its own state:\\n// the hero, the objective, what an agent needs to see the game is where it should be).\\nimport { chromium } from 'playwright';\\nimport { mkdirSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { resolve, join } from 'node:path';\\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\\n\\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\\nconst file = args.find(a => !a.startsWith('--') && !/^\\\\d+(\\\\.\\\\d+)?$/.test(a));\\nconst opt = (name, def) => { const i = args.indexOf('--' + name); return i >= 0 ? args[i + 1] : def; };\\nif (!file) { console.error('Usage: node tools/check.mjs path/to/game.html [--seconds 4] [--out check-output]'); process.exit(2); }\\nconst seconds = +opt('seconds', 4), out = resolve(opt('out', 'check-output'));\\nconst [, sw, sh, sd] = (opt('size', '1280x720') || '').match(/^(\\\\d+)x(\\\\d+)(?:@(\\\\d+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?))?$/) || [0, 1280, 720];\\nconst dpr = +(sd || 1), size = { viewport: { width: +sw, height: +sh }, deviceScaleFactor: dpr, ...(dpr >= 2 && { isMobile: true, hasTouch: true }) };\\nmkdirSync(out, { recursive: true });\\n\\nconst browser = await chromium.launch({ executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined, args: ['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'] });\\nconst page = await browser.newPage(size);\\nconst errors = [], warnings = [], engineWarnings = [], external = new Set();\\npage.on('pageerror', e => errors.push(String(e && e.stack || e)));\\npage.on('console', m => {\\n=====\\n// A headless test of the genre kits: each kit's game runs in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where there is no\\n// DOM) after the scripts its page loads before it (the engine, an asset set), starts its slice (the page's deep link,\\n// #<id>), plays two seconds, then runs the slice's proof twice: run(600), scripted play from a seed, gives a hash of how\\n// it went, the same every time. Run it: node kits/test.mjs [id ...] (every kit without one; exit code 1 on a failure).\\n// A game copied from a kit tests the same way: a kit's code reads three of the page's globals, given stand-ins here\\n// (window, addEventListener, location); drive it with game.advance and input.tap / hold, as game/test.mjs does.\\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\\nimport { readFileSync, readdirSync } from 'node:fs';\\n\\nconst here = new URL('./', import.meta.url), read = f => readFileSync(new URL(f, here), 'utf8');\\nconst ids = process.argv.slice(2).length ? process.argv.slice(2) : readdirSync(here).filter(f => f.endsWith('.html')).map(f => f.slice(0, -5)).sort();\\nlet failed = 0;\\nfor (const id of ids) {\\n  const ctx = { console: { log() {}, info() {}, warn() {}, error: console.error }, addEventListener() {}, location: { hash: '#' + id } };\\n  ctx.window = ctx; vm.createContext(ctx);\\n  try {\\n    // the page's scripts, in its order: ../my-3d2dge.js, any asset set, then the kit's game\\n    for (const [, src] of read(id + '.html').matchAll(/<script src=\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\"><\\\\/script>/g)) vm.runInContext(read(src), ctx, { filename: src });\\n    const game = ctx.My3D2dge.current, slice = ctx.__game.scenes[id];\\n    game.advance(2);\\n    const scene = game.sceneName, a = slice.run(600), b = slice.run(600), errors = game.errors.map(e => e.message), ok = a === b && !errors.length;\\n    console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + id + ': ' + scene + ' plays; its proof twice ' + (a === b ? 'the same (' + a + ')' : a + ', then ' + b) + (errors.length ? '; errors: ' + errors.join(' | ') : ''));\\n    if (!ok) failed++;\\n  } catch (e) { console.log('FAIL ' + id + ': ' + (e && e.stack || e).toString().split('\\\\n').slice(0, 3).join(' / ')); failed++; }\\n}\\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} of ${ids.length} kit(s) failed` : `all ${ids.length} kit(s) passed`);\\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\",\"stderr\":\"\\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174755__x531263/work\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_014hDJjTPnAV6t6WQXJHVvHe\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"f93111a9-5060-4eb2-b5bf-6a1585c61e13\",\"uuid\":\"35790aec-9d2c-4680-b3d2-4f37662258a2\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":100,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"f93111a9-5060-4eb2-b5bf-6a1585c61e13\",\"uuid\":\"754e261d-0d85-40c7-87df-9bb4c5cabc57\"}","+{\"type\":\