{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0179ywD4nsYHspfxKPW6UbFA","type":"tool_result","content":"867 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work/PLAN.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40","uuid":"07fed3da-fbe8-4080-83a1-4ae09bfe2674","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:33.482Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"867 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work/PLAN.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":730,"oldLines":3,"newStart":730,"newLines":138,"lines":["   | Hints | on / off | on |","   | Level up | At once / On rest | At once |","   | Voices volume | slider | 0.8 |","+","+---","+","+## 5. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller-first","+","+### 5.1 Principles","+","+- **Resolution.** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true`. The HUD is laid out for **320×240 (4:3) up to about 427×240 (16:9)** in game pixels and anchored to `r.W` and `r.H`.","+  - At 1080p one game pixel is about 4.5 screen pixels, so the 5×7 font reads at about 31 px from the sofa.","+  - Body text is the normal 5×7 font; headings use `scale: 2`; nothing interactive uses the tiny 3×5 font.","+- **Few, big things.** At most about 12 focusable things per screen region. Every screen shows ○ Back at the bottom right. Cut density before you shrink anything.","+- **One look: \"lockwork brass.\"**","+  - Panels: `bg ['#1c1813', '#0e0c0a']`, border `#b8924a`, focus `#ffd36a` (double border plus a slow pulse), text `#f0e6d0`.","+  - Stat colours: HP `#e0463c`, spell slots `#4a8aff`, food `#c8a040`.","+  - Rivets: 2×2 dots `#e8c878` in the panel corners.","+  - Title text: `E.font.title` with `colors ['#fff6d8', '#ffd36a', '#c8923a', '#6a4a1a']` and `depthColor '#2a1a08'`.","+- **Keyboard and mouse are native, not stand-ins.** The same screens, with hover moving the focus, click acting, drag and drop in the Party screen, the mouse wheel scrolling lists and the Hand following the cursor (§5.4).","+- **Prompts always follow `input.lastDevice`** (§5.5).","+","+### 5.2 The play HUD (over the full-screen 3D view)","+","+| Element | Where (game pixels) | Content |","+|---|---|---|","+| Compass | top centre, 64×16 | \"W  **N**  E\", with the facing letter at scale 2. It changes instantly on spinners: the only clue. |","+| Floor toast | top left | the floor's name for 3 s on arrival |","+| Party bar | bottom, `H−50` to `H−2` | one card per member in formation order. Row groups are 4 px apart, with tiny labels FRONT, MID and BACK above them. |","+| Card (about 66×46) | — | live portrait 30×30 (`drawPortrait`, wince when hurt, grey when Down, bones when Dead); the name (cut to 7 letters); HP bar and `hp/max`; a 2-px food strip under the portrait; **two hand slots** 15×15 with the item icon, a cooldown wipe (dark, sweeping), a \"ready\" glint and MISS or damage pops; status icons in a row of 6×6 (poison drop, chain, Zz, shield, bowl) |","+| Selected card | — | brass double frame; the L2 and R2 glyph badges under its hand slots |","+| Log | above the bar, left | 3 lines, newest at the bottom, with a shadow |","+| Prompts | above the bar, right | up to 4 `[glyph] Verb`, e.g. `✕ Pull lever · □ Strike · △ Party · Create Map` |","+| Hand | above the bar, centre | held item icon and its name (unless the mouse cursor carries it) |","+| Hit chevrons | screen edges | red chevrons on the left, right or bottom edge for 0.6 s on flank or rear hits; a red vignette on front-row hits |","+| Mouse helpers | top right under the engine corner | small icons for Map, Camp, Party and Journal, mouse only; hidden for the pad |","+| Boss bar | under the compass | THE BOLT-HOLDER, 200×6, with 3 lock pips (turned or locked) |","+| Race HUD | top left | timer `02:13.4`, checkpoint label, crowns, and in a session the standings in seat colours |","+","+Keep clear of `game.cornerArea()`, the engine's top-right menu button.","+","+### 5.3 Screens","+","+Every screen is drawn over the dimmed 3D view, takes focus navigation (§5.4) and shows its prompts.","+","+- **Party (△, I).**","+  - **Top:** member tabs, one 32-px portrait each (L1 and R1 switch).","+  - **Left:** the paperdoll, a large live rig portrait framed by 20×20 slots: Head, Neck, Body, Arms, Main, Off, Ring, Ring, Feet, Quiver.","+  - **Centre:** the backpack, 4×3 slots of 22×22.","+  - **Right:** details: a 32×32 icon, the name, a type line, stats (damage, speed, Defense, classes) and the description (§7.7 tone).","+  - **Bottom:** `HP 11/11 · Defense 14 · Lv 2 Fighter · XP 140/250 · Food ███░`.","+  - **Actions:** ✕ takes or places (it carries the item into the Hand, or swaps), □ Use, △ Drop at your feet, R2 Sheet. ○ returns a carried item, then closes the screen.","+  - **The Sheet tab** shows the stats and their modifiers, class abilities, resistances and the spellbook or the prayers. Dismiss (NPCs) is here, behind a confirm.","+- **Cast.** Opened by a caster's book or symbol hand.","+  - A centred panel of about 260×150, with level tabs L1, L2, L3 (shoulders switch them).","+  - Rows read \"Spark Dart ×2\", with a description and the target type.","+  - ✕ casts. A `member` target then moves the highlight across the cards (◀ ▶, ✕). A `line`, `front`, `door` or `party` spell fires at once. ○ cancels.","+- **Camp (L3, C).** The view darkens and a small campfire light glows in the cell. Tiles in 2 rows of 5 (§4.9).","+  - **Rest** shows a rest panel: the hours counting, HP ticking up on the cards and ○ Stop.","+  - **Memorize** and **Pray**: known spells on the left (grouped by level, with descriptions) and slots on the right. ✕ on a spell fills the next free slot of its level, ✕ on a slot empties it, △ \"Same as before\".","+  - **Scribe**: scrolls in the party's packs that the mage doesn't know; ✕ learns one.","+  - **Formation**: the 2×3 places; ✕ twice swaps two members.","+  - **Eat**: a confirm, then a summary of who ate what.","+  - **Save** and **Load** open the engine's slot screens (`saves.show`).","+  - **Settings** opens `game.menu('settings')`.","+- **Map (Create, M).**","+  - A parchment-coloured panel with the floor's explored cells at 8 to 10 px per cell, and a legend row at the bottom.","+  - L1 and R1 switch between visited floors; the d-pad or stick pans a map larger than the screen; ○ closes.","+  - Dev *reveal* shows everything.","+- **Journal (J, or the tab from Party or Map).** Quests, Notes, Deeds and Log. Notes open the **Reader**, a parchment page with the note's text at the normal size, paged with the d-pad.","+- **Dialogue.** `E.Dialog` at the bottom: portrait on the left, name in brass and 3 lines a page. ✕ finishes the line, then turns the page; ○ fast-forwards; choices are a vertical list.","+- **Title, creation, About and Credits, game over, ending, floor card and touch notice:** §7.3, §11, §5.7.","+","+### 5.4 Focus navigation and the mouse","+","+- **One focus system** (`61-ui-kit.js`) for every screen.","+  - Each screen registers its widgets as rects with an id, an action and optional explicit neighbours.","+  - The d-pad and the left stick (menus use the engine's `up/down/left/right`, which include the stick) move to the nearest widget in that direction, by geometry; explicit neighbours override.","+  - Holding a direction repeats (`input.repeat`, 0.35 s, then 0.1 s).","+- **The mouse.**","+  - Moving the pointer over a widget focuses it; a left click acts as ✕; a right click on a slot acts as □; the wheel scrolls lists.","+  - Party screen drag and drop: mouse-down carries the item, mouse-up places it.","+- **Mouse in the 3D view.** Each frame, project the interactables in front with `world.project`: the front wall's feature, the items in the front and own cells, doors, the monsters in front and alcoves. Each gets a screen hotspot.","+  - Hovering one outlines it (a soft brass rim drawn with the pen around the thing) and shows a tooltip, e.g. \"Lever — click to pull\".","+  - A left click on a hotspot uses it. With an item in the Hand, a left click on the lower view puts it down and a left click on the upper view throws it, as in the source.","+  - A right click anywhere in the view is **Party Strike**.","+- **Party cards.** A click on a hand slot uses that hand (the source's core gesture); a click on a portrait selects; a right click on a portrait opens that member in the Party screen.","+","+### 5.5 Prompts and glyphs","+","+- **One painter, `glyph(g, x, y, action)`**, draws a badge for the action's binding on the last device:","+","+  | Device | Badge |","+  |---|---|","+  | Pad, PlayStation (default) | ✕ blue, ○ red, □ pink, △ green, drawn as shapes on a dark disc; L1, R1, L2, R2, L3, R3, Options and Create as rounded labels; D-pad and stick icons |","+  | Pad, Xbox (Settings → Controls → Button symbols) | A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow letters; LB, RB, LT, RT, View, Menu |","+  | Keyboard | a keycap with the bound key (`input.codeLabel`) |","+  | Mouse | a mouse icon with the left or right button lit |","+","+  Never print raw codes. Build every prompt string from `input.label(action)` through the painter, so rebinding just works.","+- **When the prompts change.** They switch the moment `lastDevice` changes: a pad button or a stick past the dead zone, a key, or a mouse move of more than 4 px or a click.","+","+### 5.6 Input map (all rebindable except the menu actions)","+","+| Action | Gamepad (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Mouse |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| Step forward / back | Left stick ↑ ↓, D-pad ↑ ↓ | W / S, ↑ / ↓, Numpad 8 / 5 or 2 | — |","+| Strafe left / right | Left stick ← → | A / D, Numpad 4 / 6 | — |","+| Turn left / right | D-pad ← →, right stick ← → (a flick, repeating every 0.35 s while held) | Q / E, ← / →, Numpad 7 / 9 | — |","+| Use / interact / take / place / stow | ✕ (tap) | F | left click on a thing in the view |","+| Put the Hand's item down | ✕ (hold 0.4 s) | H | left click on the lower view |","+| Throw the Hand's item | ○ | G | left click on the upper view |","+| Party Strike | □ | Space | right click in the view |","+| Select member previous / next | L1 / R1 | Tab / Shift+Tab, or 1–6 | click a portrait |","+| Selected member's main / off hand | R2 / L2 | 1–6 main hand (and select); Shift+1–6 off hand | click a hand slot |","+| Party screen | △ | I | portrait right click, HUD icon |","+| Camp | L3 | C | HUD icon |","+| Examine ahead | R3 | X | middle click |","+| Automap | Create (acts on release; ignored when Options was pressed while Create was held) | M | HUD icon |","+| Journal | (from the Party or Map tabs, or the pause menu) | J | HUD icon |","+| Pause menu | Options | Esc, P | the engine's corner button |","+| Menus | D-pad / stick, ✕ confirm, ○ back, L1 / R1 tabs | arrows, Enter, Backspace or Esc | hover, click, wheel |","+","+**Implementation notes.**","+- Define your own play actions (`fwd, back, strafeL, strafeR, turnL, turnR, use, strike, selPrev, selNext, handMain, handOff, party, camp, examine, map, journal, throw, putDown`) in the play scene's `input` map, as the kit did.","+- **Don't use the engine's merged `left/right` in play**: they merge the d-pad and the stick, and here they mean different things.","+  - Read the left stick from `input.padAxes[0]` and `[1]`, with the dead zone and a 0.5 threshold, for move and strafe.","+  - Read the right stick X from `padAxes[2]`, as a flick with re-arm, for turning.","+  - The d-pad codes are `Pad12` to `Pad15`.","+- **Hub rule.** While Create (`Pad8`) is held, ignore Options (`Pad9`), and don't toggle the map on Create's release if Options went down in between.","+- **Idle detection** (attract mode): any action pressed, any `input.held` code, a stick past 0.3, a pointer move over 4 px or a click.","+","+### 5.7 Touch-only devices","+","+- **Detection.** `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` with no `(hover: hover)`, and no keyboard or gamepad input seen yet. On such devices `input.touchEnabled = false`: no touch buttons and no stick.","+- **The title** shows a panel: \"**Controller or keyboard required.** Connect a controller or a keyboard to play.\" The engine's top-right menu button stays and opens Settings.","+- **The attract mode runs** after the same 10 s idle. A touch exits it to the title, which shows the notice again.","+- **The notice hides** the moment a key or a pad button arrives, and play works normally from then on."]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1781,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1781,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01Mv5AXhLu859bfwXN9VbkJn\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1655\\t- Hoshino in the fog: \\\"When you can't see, the signals see for you.\\\"\\n1656\\t- Hoshino at Sato's flash: \\\"That's Sato. Thirty years. He's flashing for me... Answer him.\\\"\\n1657\\t- **Finale:**\\n1658\\t  - Ota: \\\"Hoshino-san. Thirty-eight years. The whole station is here.\\\"\\n1659\\t  - Hoshino: \\\"...And the last stop was yours, Rookie.\\\"\\n1660\\t  - Hoshino: \\\"Here. My watch. It runs two seconds fast. I never told anyone.\\\"\\n1661\\t  - Hoshino: \\\"A loop has no last station. Every ending is the next departure.\\\"\\n1662\\t  - Mika: \\\"Welcome to the Halo Line, Driver!\\\"\\n1663\\t  - Haro-kun: \\\"Harooo!\\\"\\n1664\\t\\n1665\\t**Results** (Hoshino, by rank; one line per stage per rank, varied):\\n1666\\t\\n1667\\t| rank | S1 line |\\n1668\\t|---|---|\\n1669\\t| S | \\\"...Exactly there. Exactly then.\\\" |\\n1670\\t| A | \\\"Good. Now do it four hundred more times.\\\" |\\n1671\\t| B | \\\"Acceptable. Your brakes are nervous.\\\" |\\n1672\\t| C | \\\"You drove. That is all I will say.\\\" |\\n1673\\t| D | \\\"We will talk about this at the depot.\\\" |\\n1674\\t\\n1675\\t- Game over: \\\"That's enough. Hand me the key.\\\"\\n1676\\t- Write the other stages' lines in the same voice.\\n1677\\t\\n1678\\t### 5.6 Art assets\\n1679\\t\\n1680\\tAll art follows the engine's native look: PS1-era pixel art drawn with `E.px` primitives and `E.font`, shaded with `E.tones` (`deep`, `sh`, `base`,\\n1681\\t`lt`, `hi`), lit by palette per time of day. Every world drawer has 3 levels of detail by k (§4.1).\\n1682\\t\\n1683\\t**New (made for this game; these make it feel like the source):**\\n1684\\t\\n1685\\t| Group | Items | Technique |\\n1686\\t|---|---|---|\\n1687\\t| Trains | Halo 8000 / 3000 / Sky Liner / freight loco plus containers; body pattern (windows, doors, stripe, skirt, bogies, pantograph); front faces (headlights, tail lights, LED destination, cab windows, driver silhouette) | strips plus a front-face thing |\\n1688\\t| Cab | 8000 modern panel, 3000 classic panel, windshield frame, visor, wipers, glass droplets, master controllers, the gloved hand (4 poses: on handle, point, press button, horn), pocket watch, timetable card | screen overlay |\\n1689\\t| Line-side | 4-lamp signal (lit states, glow), shunting signal, ATS beacon, limit and END boards, horn board, stop approach and PASS boards, stop markers \\\"6\\\" / \\\"10\\\", km posts, slow-order boards, special emitter, catenary masts (lattice, concrete), wires | things / per-segment lines |\\n1690\\t| Stations | platform slab patterns, canopy, columns, name boards, vending machines, bins, clock, LED board, stairs, fence, door marks, Haro-kun poster | strips plus things |\\n1691\\t| Town (parametric) | `building({ w, d, h, floors, roof: 'flat'|'gable'|'hip', facade: 'office'|'apartment'|'house'|'shop'|'konbini'|'warehouse'|'machiya', palette, lit })` drawn as boxes (front, side, roof), windows lit at night | strips |\\n1692\\t| Landmarks | terminal clock tower, greenhouses, whale-arch bridge, gantry cranes, container stacks, ferry, lighthouse (beam at night), pagoda, temple gate, torii, observatory dome, clock tower, Ferris wheel (turning), sakura trees | things |\\n1693\\t| Crossings | road band, crossbuck, flashing lamps, gate arm (tweened), kei cars, bikes | band plus things |\\n1694\\t| People | outfits per §4.10 and §5.4; briefcase, umbrella, flag, camera attachments at `rig.hand()` | Humanoid rigs |\\n1695\\t| UI | logo plus halo ring, halo map, glyph badges, Halo Time ring, notch display, stop gauge, judgment titles, hanko rank stamps, postcards, weather and time icons, DEMO badge | overlay |\\n1696\\t\\n1697\\t**From the engine's library** (generic props; bake once at boot with `E.shapeSprite(id, { view, facing, size })` into things):\\n1698\\t- `tree`, `pine`, `bush`, `rock`, `fence`, `bench`, `lamppost`, `crate`, `barrel`, `sign`;\\n1699\\t- `kenney-fantasy-town:hedge*`, `kenney-pirate:boat-row-large`, `kenney-holiday:bench` (load their sets per `src/assets/README.md`);\\n1700\\t- `E.prop('tree' | 'pine' | 'bush' | 'flowers' | 'grass' | 'lamp' | 'streetlamp' | 'trashcan' | 'hydrant').frames[0]`.\\n1701\\t\\n1702\\tSearch for more with `node tools/asset-find.mjs \\\"<words>\\\"`, and cut what you use into a set of your own (`tools/asset-set.mjs`) so the bundle\\n1703\\tstays lean.\\n1704\\t\\n1705\\t### 5.7 Animations (new, on top of the engine's rigs)\\n1706\\t\\n1707\\t- **Gloved hand:** rides the handle (an 80 ms tween per notch), point-and-call (raise, point at the target, return), press ATS, press the horn.\\n1708\\t- **Controls:** handle tweens, needles (a critically damped spring), lamp blinks, wiper sweeps, droplets that gather and are wiped away, the visor\\n1709\\t  dropping.\\n1710\\t- **Train:** doors sliding (exterior and platform cam), the pantograph bobbing with sparks at night, the S5 headlight flash, the back-up crawl.\\n1711\\t- **World:** crossing gates and lamps, the obstruction emitter flashing, the lighthouse beam turning, the Ferris wheel turning, falling sakura petals,\\n1712\\t  seagulls flapping, festival lanterns swaying.\\n1713\\t- **People:** idle and gait (built in); `wave` (kids); `cheer` (festival, the duel winner); new `bow`, `point` and `flag` poses (§3.8 #6) for staff,\\n1714\\t  workers and the finale; boarding and alighting walks; umbrellas.\\n1715\\t- **Haro-kun:** squash-and-stretch bounce, the halo spinning and glowing, wing flaps, a hop on PERFECT, waving on the title.\\n1716\\t- **UI:** the stamp slam, the halo ring cracking (particles), the postcard flip, the halo map's selection glow travelling the ring, the title train\\n1717\\t  arriving.\\n1718\\t- Check every rig animation with `node tools/filmstrip.mjs index.html#gallery --steps \\\"...\\\" --seed 1`.\\n1719\\t\\n1720\\t### 5.8 Audio assets\\n1721\\t\\n1722\\tEverything in §4.16 and §4.17. Departure melodies, one per station:\\n1723\\t\\n1724\\t| station | melody id | character |\\n1725\\t|---|---|---|\\n1726\\t| akari | `akari` | stately and bright: a 4-bar bell fanfare |\\n1727\\t| hanabatake | `hanabatake` | skipping, pastoral |\\n1728\\t| kujira | `kujira` | rolling, wave-like |\\n1729\\t| minato | `minato` | jaunty, ends with a ship-horn note |\\n1730\\t| todai | `todai` | airy (used when stopping in Free Run) |\\n1731\\t| okiku | `okiku` | pentatonic, koto-like |\\n1732\\t| yuhi | `yuhi` | warm, falling |\\n1733\\t| shotengai | `shotengai` | busy, syncopated |\\n1734\\t| daigaku | `daigaku` | a school-bell quote |\\n1735\\t| koen | `koen` | light and lilting |\\n1736\\t| hoshimi | `hoshimi` | twinkling and high |\\n1737\\t| kawasemi | `kawasemi` | quick, bird-like |\\n1738\\t\\n1739\\t---\\n1740\\t\\n1741\\t## 6. Build order and milestones\\n1742\\t\\n1743\\tEach milestone ends **playable** and **green** (`node test/run.mjs`). Don't start the next until the acceptance checks pass. Cut nothing silently.\\n1744\\tIf time runs short, use the cut order in §7, removing whole features (never stubbing them).\\n1745\\t\\n1746\\t| # | Milestone | Build | Acceptance |\\n1747\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n1748\\t| **M0** | Setup | the dev folder; engine copied; `index.html` (session.js first); `src/00-core.js`, a placeholder-free blank title scene; `test/run.mjs` with lib.mjs loading engine plus src in a vm; `tools/bundle.mjs`; ENGINE-CHANGES.md | page opens from file:// with no errors; `node test/run.mjs` prints `N passed, 0 failed`; bundle builds and opens |\\n1749\\t| **M1** | **Rail renderer** | `rail.js`: segments, square-pixel projection, ground, ballast, sleepers, rails, catenary, strips (platform, canopy, wall, overpass, tunnel, bridge truss), things (signal, boards, masts, trees via shapeSprite), crest clipping, tint, fog, rear view, `project`, `pick`; a small test route; `#gallery` | the §4.1 tests; the 13 gallery screenshots reviewed (§8.5): rails converge cleanly, platforms read as raised, nothing squashed on 16:9 |\\n1750\\t| **M2** | Train and cab core | `30-train.js`; lever and input map; the cab overlay (speedo, notch, gauges, handle, glove); the HUD skeleton; camera sway; the continuous sound (VVVF, rolling, joints, brakes); one station stop with judgment and Stop Cam on the test route | §4.3 check values; drive and stop by keyboard and pad; judgment shown; sounds respond to v and notch |\\n1751\\t| **M3** | Rules: full S1 | route compiler and the S1 route; signals and blocks; ATS; limits; stations with dwell and departure sequence; timetable and clock; calls and horn; Halo Time, score, ranks; comfort; briefing and results; minimal title → S1 → results flow; story data for S1; first Babble voices | S1 playable end to end by a human; §4.4–4.10 tests |\\n1752\\t| **M4** | Autopilot and Dev Mode | `35-autopilot.js`; `DH.proof`; Dev Mode (tools, sliders, Reset, debug overlay, sound board); engine changes §3.8 #3; `tools/calibrate.mjs` | the autopilot ranks S on S1; slider tests; the proof hash is stable; Dev Mode works by pad and mouse |\\n1753\\t| **M5** | Multiplayer | PR stage and the quad-track route section; train actors as ghosts; `63-hub.js` with our card; `64-duel.js`; hub harness script | mock-hub tests; **harness passes** with 2p, with 4p plus latency, jitter and loss, and with host-leave; the duel finishes with two autopilots |\\n1754\\t| **M6** | Career content | the whole halo route and depot; zones and scenery sets; stations and landmarks; S0–S5 data, events, rival, freight, crossings, workers, obstruction, fog, glare, rain, night; crowds and characters; all story lines; postcards; calibrated timetables | **full playthrough test** (autopilot skill 1 and 0.6 over S0–S5 and PR) passes; every event fires; gallery shots per zone reviewed |\\n1755\\t| **M7** | Front end and attract | boot steps and splash; title (touch-only branch); halo map; Free Run; Duel lobby; Driver's Log; How to Drive; About & Credits; game over; ending and credits; **attract mode**; glyph badges everywhere; settings additions | §4.15, 4.20, 4.22, 4.25, 4.26 tests; attract loop screenshots; every screen at 1080p and 720p readable at 10 ft (§8.5) |\\n1756\\t| **M8** | Audio and polish | the full soundscape, 12 melodies, all music, all Babble voices; rumble; animation polish (filmstrips); a balance pass with the sliders (a human drives each stage on Normal: an S is hard but possible, a C is easy); accessibility review | sound board audition; node-leak test; no look notes left from `tools/check.mjs` that matter |\\n1757\\t| **M9** | Ship | final bundle; About/Credits text; exit-interview.json; the full suite on the **bundle** (headless plus browser plus harness) | §9 checklist all ticked |\\n1758\\t\\n1759\\t**First playable target (end of M3):** S1 driven by a human, start to finish, with real feedback. That's where the fun gets proven or fixed. Tune the\\n1760\\tphysics and judgment windows there before any content work.\\n1761\\t\\n1762\\t---\\n1763\\t\\n1764\\t## 7. Risks and how to de-risk them\\n1765\\t\\n1766\\t| Risk | Why it's risky | De-risk |\\n1767\\t|---|---|---|\\n1768\\t| **Rail renderer quality** | It is the whole look; pseudo-3D strips (platforms, trains, buildings) and the rear view are new code | Build it first (M1) on a test route; projection unit tests; the gallery with screenshots before anything else; keep strip faces simple (flat colour plus pattern), add detail later |\\n1769\\t| **Stopping feel and precision** | If precise stops feel random, the game fails | The lag model plus the stop gauge's fine scale plus the braking guide; MPC autopilot as proof it can be done; tune in M3 with telemetry (debug overlay); sliders for lag, windows, brake scale; record human sessions (`?record=1`) and replay them |\\n1770\\t| **Babble and VVVF synthesis** | They can sound harsh or leak WebAudio nodes | Fixed node graph for the continuous layers; a capped node pool for syllables; the sound board for auditions; master limiter (a DynamicsCompressor on our bus); the leak test |\\n1771\\t| **Hub compliance** | Easy to miss a rule (ready without input, one result, stopping on end) | Copy `examples/ghost.html`'s flow; mock-hub tests in M5; run the real harness early, and again on the final bundle |\\n1772\\t| **Content volume** | 12 stations, 13 zones, 6 stages | Data-driven scripts; a parametric building generator; seeded scenery per zone; hand-draw only the landmarks; stations from one kit |\\n1773\\t| **Determinism** | Tests and hub copies must agree | `DH.rng` streams only; fixed steps; proof hash twice; no wall clock |\\n1774\\t| **10-foot legibility** | 320×240 pixels on a TV | Font-size rules (§4.14); screenshots at 1920×1080 and 1280×720 viewed scaled down; at most 6 HUD elements |\\n1775\\t| **Engine edits** | Could break standard features | Minimal patches (§3.8); rerun the handoff tests; log them |\\n1776\\t| **Disk and /tmp** | /tmp was full on this machine | `TMPDIR` inside the dev folder; clean `_src` clones after copying |\\n1777\\t| **Time** | A big scope | Milestone gates; the cut order below |\\n1778\\t\\n1779\\t**Cut order if time runs out** (each cut removes the feature cleanly, including its menu entries and tests):\\n1780\\t1. postcards 7–8;\\n1781\\t2. the Halo 3000 cab art (it keeps its physics and sound and uses the 8000 cab);\\n1782\\t3. the `trackside` camera;\\n1783\\t4. the Stats page in the Log;\\n1784\\t5. Free Run's train choice.\\n1785\\t\\n1786\\t**Never cut:** any TASK.md requirement (dev mode with sliders, attract, the hub, the 10-foot UI and glyphs, touch-only handling, About/Credits, the exit\\n1787\\tinterview) or any stage S0–S5 or PR.\\n1788\\t\\n1789\\t---\\n1790\\t\\n1791\\t## 8. Testing\\n1792\\t\\n1793\\t### 8.1 One command\\n1794\\t\\n1795\\t`node test/run.mjs` (from the dev folder; also `npm test`).\\n1796\\t- It runs every headless suite and prints **only failures**, each as `FAIL <suite>: <what> (<detail>)`, then **one line**: `57 passed, 0 failed`.\\n1797\\t- Exit code 1 on any failure.\\n1798\\t- `node test/run.mjs physics stations` runs a subset. Rerun only the suites that cover the code you changed, and the whole run before each milestone\\n1799\\t  gate.\\n1800\\t- `--browser` adds the Playwright checks (§8.3). `--hub` adds the harness (§8.4). Both need `TMPDIR` set (§0).\\n1801\\t\\n1802\\t`test/lib.mjs`:\\n1803\\t- creates a vm context with stand-ins: `window`, `addEventListener`, `removeEventListener`, `location {hash, search}`,\\n1804\\t  `navigator {maxTouchPoints, getGamepads}`, `matchMedia`, and optionally a mock `AIHub` (§4.23);\\n1805\\t- loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, `engine/modules/rail.js`, then `src/*.js` in order;\\n1806\\t- returns `{ E, DH, game, I }`.\\n1807\\t- Each test drives the game with `game.advance()`, `I.tap/hold/press/feed`, and `game.debug`.\\n1808\\t\\n1809\\t### 8.2 Headless suites (what each asserts)\\n1810\\t\\n1811\\t| suite | asserts (see each §'s Tests) |\\n1812\\t|---|---|\\n1813\\t| `rail` | projection, square pixels, rear mirror, crest clipping, strip faces, project/pick (§4.1) |\\n1814\\t| `route` | compiling, segments, curves, grades, spans, validation good and bad (§4.2) |\\n1815\\t| `physics` | check values, lever rules, slip, determinism (§4.3) |\\n1816\\t| `signals` | aspects, starting signals, ATS ring/confirm/EB, SPAD, S2 freight (§4.4) |\\n1817\\t| `limits` | tolerance, once per section, rear clears (§4.5) |\\n1818\\t| `stations` | judgment table, re-stops, on time/late/early, smooth, dwell order, pilot interlock, missed and wrong stops (§4.6) |\\n1819\\t| `calls` | windows, GREAT vs OK, sighting, departure call, auto calls, horn zone (§4.7) |\\n1820\\t| `timetable` | clock, pause, card, calibrated par early by 6–12 s (§4.8) |\\n1821\\t| `score` | Halo Time cap and 0, Max, ranks, difficulty (§4.9) |\\n1822\\t| `crowds` | queues, doors, boarding, comfort, LOD (§4.10) |\\n1823\\t| `events` | each event fires once and does its effect (§4.11) |\\n1824\\t| `tod` | grade continuity, rain adhesion, fog sighting (§4.12) |\\n1825\\t| `cameras` | placements, the view cycle, the director (§4.13) |\\n1826\\t| `hud` | state builder, hit boxes, element count, layouts at 3 sizes (§4.14) |\\n1827\\t| `input` | glyph families, lever flip, wheel, touch-only (§4.15) |\\n1828\\t| `sound` | parameter function, names exist (§4.16) |\\n1829\\t| `babble` | determinism, contour, voices, Dialog hook (§4.17) |\\n1830\\t| `story` | briefings and results lines exist, queueing, tips once, wrap length (§4.18) |\\n1831\\t| `autopilot` | skill 1 → S on every stage; skill 0.6 → no game over; proof stable (§4.19) |\\n1832\\t| `attract` | 10 s trigger, order, loop, every exit input, no records, touch-only (§4.20) |\\n1833\\t| `dev` | sliders live, Reset, hidden from Settings and from sessions, tools (§4.21) |\\n1834\\t| `progress` | postcards, store round-trip, unlock order (§4.22) |\\n1835\\t| `hub` | the mock-hub contract (§4.23) |\\n1836\\t| `duel` | two players, viewports, winner and tie (§4.24) |\\n1837\\t| `settings` | each setting applies and persists (§4.25) |\\n1838\\t| `screens` | every screen's open, close and routes; About has every label (§4.26) |\\n1839\\t| **`playthrough`** | **the scripted whole game:** boot → title → (wait 10 s → attract → input → title) → Career S0…S5 via the menus, driven by the autopilot at skill 1 → results after each → the ending and credits → title; then PR via Duel (2 autopilots) and via the mock hub; asserts no errors (`game.errors` empty), S0 passed, every service stage (S1–S5) rank S, every postcard 1–8 unlocked, every event id fired, and the same proof hash when run twice |\\n1840\\t\\n1841\\t### 8.3 Browser checks (`--browser`; Playwright 1.63.0, file:// first)\\n1842\\t\\n1843\\t1. `node engine/tools/check.mjs <bundle.html>`, plus `#gallery`, `#stage=S2`, `#attract`: no errors; act on its look notes (fill, colour count,\\n1844\\t   contrast).\\n1845\\t2. A Playwright script on the bundle:\\n1846\\t   - the page loads; the title is drawn; after 10.5 s of no input, attract is on (`__dh.snapshot().attract.active`); a key press returns to the\\n1847\\t     title;\\n1848\\t   - keyboard drive: Enter, then CAREER, then S1 via the menus; hold W for 3 s and the speed is above 0;\\n1849\\t   - mouse: hover over the title menu moves the focus, and a click picks;\\n1850\\t   - **touch emulation** (`hasTouch`, `isMobile`, with no keyboard events sent): the message and the Settings button show; attract still runs.\\n1851\\t3. Audio node count after 60 s of autopilot driving stays bounded.\\n1852\\t\\n1853\\t### 8.4 AI Hub harness (`--hub`)\\n1854\\t\\n1855\\t- Copy `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` and the bundle (as `game.html`) into `test/.serve/`.\\n1856\\t- Start `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory test/.serve`, read the port from stdout, and confirm that `GET /game.html` is our\\n1857\\t  page (its `<title>`).\\n1858\\t- In Playwright, open in turn:\\n1859\\t  1. `harness.html?game=game.html&players=2&auto=1`;\\n1860\\t  2. `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`;\\n1861\\t  3. the same with `&scenario=host-leave`.\\n1862\\t- Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and assert `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. On failure, print the failed checklist items.\\n1863\\t- Stop the server **by its PID**.\\n1864\\t- Also open the bundle outside the harness to confirm the normal game still runs (the hub's own `hub-check` does this too).\\n1865\\t\\n1866\\t### 8.5 Screenshots (only for what scripts can't judge)\\n1867\\t\\n1868\\tSave them to `shots/` at 1920×1080 and 1280×720:\\n1869\\t- the 13 gallery shots;\\n1870\\t- each zone at its stage's time of day;\\n1871\\t- a station dwell with the crowd boarding;\\n1872\\t- the crossing with gates down;\\n1873\\t- the obstruction;\\n1874\\t- rain wipers;\\n1875\\t- fog;\\n1876\\t- the rival alongside;\\n1877\\t- the S5 finale bow;\\n1878\\t- the title, the halo map, a briefing, results with the stamp, game over;\\n1879\\t- Driver's Log;\\n1880\\t- About;\\n1881\\t- the attract DEMO overlay;\\n1882\\t- the duel split screen;\\n1883\\t- the hub card (from the harness).\\n1884\\t\\n1885\\tJudge each: does it read from 10 feet (view at 25% size)? Does it look like a PS1-era pixel game, not an Atari one? Is any colour flat or muddy?\\n1886\\t\\n1887\\tFilmstrips: the glove's point-and-call, the staff bow and flag, the stamp slam, the crossing gate.\\n1888\\t\\n1889\\t---\\n1890\\t\\n1891\\t## 9. Ship checklist\\n1892\\t\\n1893\\t1. `node tools/bundle.mjs` writes `../DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-<model>-<ts>.html`:\\n1894\\t   - `<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">`, then the **unmodified** `session.js` `<script>` as the first script;\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619\",\"uuid\":\"47e985e0-b9c0-47f4-8cc2-83310f82c9ff\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:34:26.022Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/work/PLAN.md\",\"content\":\"- Hoshino in the fog: \\\"When you can't see, the signals see for you.\\\"\\n- Hoshino at Sato's flash: \\\"That's Sato. Thirty years. He's flashing for me... Answer him.\\\"\\n- **Finale:**\\n  - Ota: \\\"Hoshino-san. Thirty-eight years. The whole station is here.\\\"\\n  - Hoshino: \\\"...And the last stop was yours, Rookie.\\\"\\n  - Hoshino: \\\"Here. My watch. It runs two seconds fast. I never told anyone.\\\"\\n  - Hoshino: \\\"A loop has no last station. Every ending is the next departure.\\\"\\n  - Mika: \\\"Welcome to the Halo Line, Driver!\\\"\\n  - Haro-kun: \\\"Harooo!\\\"\\n\\n**Results** (Hoshino, by rank; one line per stage per rank, varied):\\n\\n| rank | S1 line |\\n|---|---|\\n| S | \\\"...Exactly there. Exactly then.\\\" |\\n| A | \\\"Good. Now do it four hundred more times.\\\" |\\n| B | \\\"Acceptable. Your brakes are nervous.\\\" |\\n| C | \\\"You drove. That is all I will say.\\\" |\\n| D | \\\"We will talk about this at the depot.\\\" |\\n\\n- Game over: \\\"That's enough. Hand me the key.\\\"\\n- Write the other stages' lines in the same voice.\\n\\n### 5.6 Art assets\\n\\nAll art follows the engine's native look: PS1-era pixel art drawn with `E.px` primitives and `E.font`, shaded with `E.tones` (`deep`, `sh`, `base`,\\n`lt`, `hi`), lit by palette per time of day. Every world drawer has 3 levels of detail by k (§4.1).\\n\\n**New (made for this game; these make it feel like the source):**\\n\\n| Group | Items | Technique |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Trains | Halo 8000 / 3000 / Sky Liner / freight loco plus containers; body pattern (windows, doors, stripe, skirt, bogies, pantograph); front faces (headlights, tail lights, LED destination, cab windows, driver silhouette) | strips plus a front-face thing |\\n| Cab | 8000 modern panel, 3000 classic panel, windshield frame, visor, wipers, glass droplets, master controllers, the gloved hand (4 poses: on handle, point, press button, horn), pocket watch, timetable card | screen overlay |\\n| Line-side | 4-lamp signal (lit states, glow), shunting signal, ATS beacon, limit and END boards, horn board, stop approach and PASS boards, stop markers \\\"6\\\" / \\\"10\\\", km posts, slow-order boards, special emitter, catenary masts (lattice, concrete), wires | things / per-segment lines |\\n| Stations | platform slab patterns, canopy, columns, name boards, vending machines, bins, clock, LED board, stairs, fence, door marks, Haro-kun poster | strips plus things |\\n| Town (parametric) | `building({ w, d, h, floors, roof: 'flat'|'gable'|'hip', facade: 'office'|'apartment'|'house'|'shop'|'konbini'|'warehouse'|'machiya', palette, lit })` drawn as boxes (front, side, roof), windows lit at night | strips |\\n| Landmarks | terminal clock tower, greenhouses, whale-arch bridge, gantry cranes, container stacks, ferry, lighthouse (beam at night), pagoda, temple gate, torii, observatory dome, clock tower, Ferris wheel (turning), sakura trees | things |\\n| Crossings | road band, crossbuck, flashing lamps, gate arm (tweened), kei cars, bikes | band plus things |\\n| People | outfits per §4.10 and §5.4; briefcase, umbrella, flag, camera attachments at `rig.hand()` | Humanoid rigs |\\n| UI | logo plus halo ring, halo map, glyph badges, Halo Time ring, notch display, stop gauge, judgment titles, hanko rank stamps, postcards, weather and time icons, DEMO badge | overlay |\\n\\n**From the engine's library** (generic props; bake once at boot with `E.shapeSprite(id, { view, facing, size })` into things):\\n- `tree`, `pine`, `bush`, `rock`, `fence`, `bench`, `lamppost`, `crate`, `barrel`, `sign`;\\n- `kenney-fantasy-town:hedge*`, `kenney-pirate:boat-row-large`, `kenney-holiday:bench` (load their sets per `src/assets/README.md`);\\n- `E.prop('tree' | 'pine' | 'bush' | 'flowers' | 'grass' | 'lamp' | 'streetlamp' | 'trashcan' | 'hydrant').frames[0]`.\\n\\nSearch for more with `node tools/asset-find.mjs \\\"<words>\\\"`, and cut what you use into a set of your own (`tools/asset-set.mjs`) so the bundle\\nstays lean.\\n\\n### 5.7 Animations (new, on top of the engine's rigs)\\n\\n- **Gloved hand:** rides the handle (an 80 ms tween per notch), point-and-call (raise, point at the target, return), press ATS, press the horn.\\n- **Controls:** handle tweens, needles (a critically damped spring), lamp blinks, wiper sweeps, droplets that gather and are wiped away, the visor\\n  dropping.\\n- **Train:** doors sliding (exterior and platform cam), the pantograph bobbing with sparks at night, the S5 headlight flash, the back-up crawl.\\n- **World:** crossing gates and lamps, the obstruction emitter flashing, the lighthouse beam turning, the Ferris wheel turning, falling sakura petals,\\n  seagulls flapping, festival lanterns swaying.\\n- **People:** idle and gait (built in); `wave` (kids); `cheer` (festival, the duel winner); new `bow`, `point` and `flag` poses (§3.8 #6) for staff,\\n  workers and the finale; boarding and alighting walks; umbrellas.\\n- **Haro-kun:** squash-and-stretch bounce, the halo spinning and glowing, wing flaps, a hop on PERFECT, waving on the title.\\n- **UI:** the stamp slam, the halo ring cracking (particles), the postcard flip, the halo map's selection glow travelling the ring, the title train\\n  arriving.\\n- Check every rig animation with `node tools/filmstrip.mjs index.html#gallery --steps \\\"...\\\" --seed 1`.\\n\\n### 5.8 Audio assets\\n\\nEverything in §4.16 and §4.17. Departure melodies, one per station:\\n\\n| station | melody id | character |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| akari | `akari` | stately and bright: a 4-bar bell fanfare |\\n| hanabatake | `hanabatake` | skipping, pastoral |\\n| kujira | `kujira` | rolling, wave-like |\\n| minato | `minato` | jaunty, ends with a ship-horn note |\\n| todai | `todai` | airy (used when stopping in Free Run) |\\n| okiku | `okiku` | pentatonic, koto-like |\\n| yuhi | `yuhi` | warm, falling |\\n| shotengai | `shotengai` | busy, syncopated |\\n| daigaku | `daigaku` | a school-bell quote |\\n| koen | `koen` | light and lilting |\\n| hoshimi | `hoshimi` | twinkling and high |\\n| kawasemi | `kawasemi` | quick, bird-like |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Build order and milestones\\n\\nEach milestone ends **playable** and **green** (`node test/run.mjs`). Don't start the next until the acceptance checks pass. Cut nothing silently.\\nIf time runs short, use the cut order in §7, removing whole features (never stubbing them).\\n\\n| # | Milestone | Build | Acceptance |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **M0** | Setup | the dev folder; engine copied; `index.html` (session.js first); `src/00-core.js`, a placeholder-free blank title scene; `test/run.mjs` with lib.mjs loading engine plus src in a vm; `tools/bundle.mjs`; ENGINE-CHANGES.md | page opens from file:// with no errors; `node test/run.mjs` prints `N passed, 0 failed`; bundle builds and opens |\\n| **M1** | **Rail renderer** | `rail.js`: segments, square-pixel projection, ground, ballast, sleepers, rails, catenary, strips (platform, canopy, wall, overpass, tunnel, bridge truss), things (signal, boards, masts, trees via shapeSprite), crest clipping, tint, fog, rear view, `project`, `pick`; a small test route; `#gallery` | the §4.1 tests; the 13 gallery screenshots reviewed (§8.5): rails converge cleanly, platforms read as raised, nothing squashed on 16:9 |\\n| **M2** | Train and cab core | `30-train.js`; lever and input map; the cab overlay (speedo, notch, gauges, handle, glove); the HUD skeleton; camera sway; the continuous sound (VVVF, rolling, joints, brakes); one station stop with judgment and Stop Cam on the test route | §4.3 check values; drive and stop by keyboard and pad; judgment shown; sounds respond to v and notch |\\n| **M3** | Rules: full S1 | route compiler and the S1 route; signals and blocks; ATS; limits; stations with dwell and departure sequence; timetable and clock; calls and horn; Halo Time, score, ranks; comfort; briefing and results; minimal title → S1 → results flow; story data for S1; first Babble voices | S1 playable end to end by a human; §4.4–4.10 tests |\\n| **M4** | Autopilot and Dev Mode | `35-autopilot.js`; `DH.proof`; Dev Mode (tools, sliders, Reset, debug overlay, sound board); engine changes §3.8 #3; `tools/calibrate.mjs` | the autopilot ranks S on S1; slider tests; the proof hash is stable; Dev Mode works by pad and mouse |\\n| **M5** | Multiplayer | PR stage and the quad-track route section; train actors as ghosts; `63-hub.js` with our card; `64-duel.js`; hub harness script | mock-hub tests; **harness passes** with 2p, with 4p plus latency, jitter and loss, and with host-leave; the duel finishes with two autopilots |\\n| **M6** | Career content | the whole halo route and depot; zones and scenery sets; stations and landmarks; S0–S5 data, events, rival, freight, crossings, workers, obstruction, fog, glare, rain, night; crowds and characters; all story lines; postcards; calibrated timetables | **full playthrough test** (autopilot skill 1 and 0.6 over S0–S5 and PR) passes; every event fires; gallery shots per zone reviewed |\\n| **M7** | Front end and attract | boot steps and splash; title (touch-only branch); halo map; Free Run; Duel lobby; Driver's Log; How to Drive; About & Credits; game over; ending and credits; **attract mode**; glyph badges everywhere; settings additions | §4.15, 4.20, 4.22, 4.25, 4.26 tests; attract loop screenshots; every screen at 1080p and 720p readable at 10 ft (§8.5) |\\n| **M8** | Audio and polish | the full soundscape, 12 melodies, all music, all Babble voices; rumble; animation polish (filmstrips); a balance pass with the sliders (a human drives each stage on Normal: an S is hard but possible, a C is easy); accessibility review | sound board audition; node-leak test; no look notes left from `tools/check.mjs` that matter |\\n| **M9** | Ship | final bundle; About/Credits text; exit-interview.json; the full suite on the **bundle** (headless plus browser plus harness) | §9 checklist all ticked |\\n\\n**First playable target (end of M3):** S1 driven by a human, start to finish, with real feedback. That's where the fun gets proven or fixed. Tune the\\nphysics and judgment windows there before any content work.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Risks and how to de-risk them\\n\\n| Risk | Why it's risky | De-risk |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **Rail renderer quality** | It is the whole look; pseudo-3D strips (platforms, trains, buildings) and the rear view are new code | Build it first (M1) on a test route; projection unit tests; the gallery with screenshots before anything else; keep strip faces simple (flat colour plus pattern), add detail later |\\n| **Stopping feel and precision** | If precise stops feel random, the game fails | The lag model plus the stop gauge's fine scale plus the braking guide; MPC autopilot as proof it can be done; tune in M3 with telemetry (debug overlay); sliders for lag, windows, brake scale; record human sessions (`?record=1`) and replay them |\\n| **Babble and VVVF synthesis** | They can sound harsh or leak WebAudio nodes | Fixed node graph for the continuous layers; a capped node pool for syllables; the sound board for auditions; master limiter (a DynamicsCompressor on our bus); the leak test |\\n| **Hub compliance** | Easy to miss a rule (ready without input, one result, stopping on end) | Copy `examples/ghost.html`'s flow; mock-hub tests in M5; run the real harness early, and again on the final bundle |\\n| **Content volume** | 12 stations, 13 zones, 6 stages | Data-driven scripts; a parametric building generator; seeded scenery per zone; hand-draw only the landmarks; stations from one kit |\\n| **Determinism** | Tests and hub copies must agree | `DH.rng` streams only; fixed steps; proof hash twice; no wall clock |\\n| **10-foot legibility** | 320×240 pixels on a TV | Font-size rules (§4.14); screenshots at 1920×1080 and 1280×720 viewed scaled down; at most 6 HUD elements |\\n| **Engine edits** | Could break standard features | Minimal patches (§3.8); rerun the handoff tests; log them |\\n| **Disk and /tmp** | /tmp was full on this machine | `TMPDIR` inside the dev folder; clean `_src` clones after copying |\\n| **Time** | A big scope | Milestone gates; the cut order below |\\n\\n**Cut order if time runs out** (each cut removes the feature cleanly, including its menu entries and tests):\\n1. postcards 7–8;\\n2. the Halo 3000 cab art (it keeps its physics and sound and uses the 8000 cab);\\n3. the `trackside` camera;\\n4. the Stats page in the Log;\\n5. Free Run's train choice.\\n\\n**Never cut:** any TASK.md requirement (dev mode with sliders, attract, the hub, the 10-foot UI and glyphs, touch-only handling, About/Credits, the exit\\ninterview) or any stage S0–S5 or PR.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Testing\\n\\n### 8.1 One command\\n\\n`node test/run.mjs` (from the dev folder; also `npm test`).\\n- It runs every headless suite and prints **only failures**, each as `FAIL <suite>: <what> (<detail>)`, then **one line**: `57 passed, 0 failed`.\\n- Exit code 1 on any failure.\\n- `node test/run.mjs physics stations` runs a subset. Rerun only the suites that cover the code you changed, and the whole run before each milestone\\n  gate.\\n- `--browser` adds the Playwright checks (§8.3). `--hub` adds the harness (§8.4). Both need `TMPDIR` set (§0).\\n\\n`test/lib.mjs`:\\n- creates a vm context with stand-ins: `window`, `addEventListener`, `removeEventListener`, `location {hash, search}`,\\n  `navigator {maxTouchPoints, getGamepads}`, `matchMedia`, and optionally a mock `AIHub` (§4.23);\\n- loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, `engine/modules/rail.js`, then `src/*.js` in order;\\n- returns `{ E, DH, game, I }`.\\n- Each test drives the game with `game.advance()`, `I.tap/hold/press/feed`, and `game.debug`.\\n\\n### 8.2 Headless suites (what each asserts)\\n\\n| suite | asserts (see each §'s Tests) |\\n|---|---|\\n| `rail` | projection, square pixels, rear mirror, crest clipping, strip faces, project/pick (§4.1) |\\n| `route` | compiling, segments, curves, grades, spans, validation good and bad (§4.2) |\\n| `physics` | check values, lever rules, slip, determinism (§4.3) |\\n| `signals` | aspects, starting signals, ATS ring/confirm/EB, SPAD, S2 freight (§4.4) |\\n| `limits` | tolerance, once per section, rear clears (§4.5) |\\n| `stations` | judgment table, re-stops, on time/late/early, smooth, dwell order, pilot interlock, missed and wrong stops (§4.6) |\\n| `calls` | windows, GREAT vs OK, sighting, departure call, auto calls, horn zone (§4.7) |\\n| `timetable` | clock, pause, card, calibrated par early by 6–12 s (§4.8) |\\n| `score` | Halo Time cap and 0, Max, ranks, difficulty (§4.9) |\\n| `crowds` | queues, doors, boarding, comfort, LOD (§4.10) |\\n| `events` | each event fires once and does its effect (§4.11) |\\n| `tod` | grade continuity, rain adhesion, fog sighting (§4.12) |\\n| `cameras` | placements, the view cycle, the director (§4.13) |\\n| `hud` | state builder, hit boxes, element count, layouts at 3 sizes (§4.14) |\\n| `input` | glyph families, lever flip, wheel, touch-only (§4.15) |\\n| `sound` | parameter function, names exist (§4.16) |\\n| `babble` | determinism, contour, voices, Dialog hook (§4.17) |\\n| `story` | briefings and results lines exist, queueing, tips once, wrap length (§4.18) |\\n| `autopilot` | skill 1 → S on every stage; skill 0.6 → no game over; proof stable (§4.19) |\\n| `attract` | 10 s trigger, order, loop, every exit input, no records, touch-only (§4.20) |\\n| `dev` | sliders live, Reset, hidden from Settings and from sessions, tools (§4.21) |\\n| `progress` | postcards, store round-trip, unlock order (§4.22) |\\n| `hub` | the mock-hub contract (§4.23) |\\n| `duel` | two players, viewports, winner and tie (§4.24) |\\n| `settings` | each setting applies and persists (§4.25) |\\n| `screens` | every screen's open, close and routes; About has every label (§4.26) |\\n| **`playthrough`** | **the scripted whole game:** boot → title → (wait 10 s → attract → input → title) → Career S0…S5 via the menus, driven by the autopilot at skill 1 → results after each → the ending and credits → title; then PR via Duel (2 autopilots) and via the mock hub; asserts no errors (`game.errors` empty), S0 passed, every service stage (S1–S5) rank S, every postcard 1–8 unlocked, every event id fired, and the same proof hash when run twice |\\n\\n### 8.3 Browser checks (`--browser`; Playwright 1.63.0, file:// first)\\n\\n1. `node engine/tools/check.mjs <bundle.html>`, plus `#gallery`, `#stage=S2`, `#attract`: no errors; act on its look notes (fill, colour count,\\n   contrast).\\n2. A Playwright script on the bundle:\\n   - the page loads; the title is drawn; after 10.5 s of no input, attract is on (`__dh.snapshot().attract.active`); a key press returns to the\\n     title;\\n   - keyboard drive: Enter, then CAREER, then S1 via the menus; hold W for 3 s and the speed is above 0;\\n   - mouse: hover over the title menu moves the focus, and a click picks;\\n   - **touch emulation** (`hasTouch`, `isMobile`, with no keyboard events sent): the message and the Settings button show; attract still runs.\\n3. Audio node count after 60 s of autopilot driving stays bounded.\\n\\n### 8.4 AI Hub harness (`--hub`)\\n\\n- Copy `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` and the bundle (as `game.html`) into `test/.serve/`.\\n- Start `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory test/.serve`, read the port from stdout, and confirm that `GET /game.html` is our\\n  page (its `<title>`).\\n- In Playwright, open in turn:\\n  1. `harness.html?game=game.html&players=2&auto=1`;\\n  2. `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`;\\n  3. the same with `&scenario=host-leave`.\\n- Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and assert `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. On failure, print the failed checklist items.\\n- Stop the server **by its PID**.\\n- Also open the bundle outside the harness to confirm the normal game still runs (the hub's own `hub-check` does this too).\\n\\n### 8.5 Screenshots (only for what scripts can't judge)\\n\\nSave them to `shots/` at 1920×1080 and 1280×720:\\n- the 13 gallery shots;\\n- each zone at its stage's time of day;\\n- a station dwell with the crowd boarding;\\n- the crossing with gates down;\\n- the obstruction;\\n- rain wipers;\\n- fog;\\n- the rival alongside;\\n- the S5 finale bow;\\n- the title, the halo map, a briefing, results with the stamp, game over;\\n- Driver's Log;\\n- About;\\n- the attract DEMO overlay;\\n- the duel split screen;\\n- the hub card (from the harness).\\n\\nJudge each: does it read from 10 feet (view at 25% size)? Does it look like a PS1-era pixel game, not an Atari one? Is any colour flat or muddy?\\n\\nFilmstrips: the glove's point-and-call, the staff bow and flag, the stamp slam, the crossing gate.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Ship checklist\\n\\n1. `node tools/bundle.mjs` writes `../DenshaDeHalo-DenshaDeGo-<model>-<ts>.html`:\\n   - `<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">`, then the **unmodified** `session.js` `<script>` as the first script;\",\"numLines\":240,\"startLine\":1655,\"totalLines\":1947}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01Mv5AXhLu859bfwXN9VbkJn\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619\",\"uuid\":\"b0094ea8-0444-42fe-83a7-adcbf7e6990b\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":150,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619\",\"uuid\":\"7bc63702-729f-4eca-9ef1-6ed2725e2dad\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":300,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"a6a22e8e-f9ad-4c1e-b19f-6f268b0ad619\",\"uuid\":\"3f322afc-9f97-4d12-9783-6c9131af293e\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174807__x5c5240/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2026,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2026,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":9850,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"cd9cfc19-7963-45d1-a23a-cb789e1689ad\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":9950,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"88dfba03-bceb-4cd9-b7d9-13b3db44c2a4\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":10050,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"e245c1c9-7fc4-48ed-90d9-1aeb26c306cf\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":10200,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"72da779b-b7c4-4942-9731-c58e2fe147ce\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1936,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1936,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":2700,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800\",\"uuid\":\"76aafd3b-0211-495c-a953-9081a2329378\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":2800,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800\",\"uuid\":\"a14ed040-ae2d-4861-a21b-c0a62f9db7b7\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":2950,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800\",\"uuid\":\"e8b6b565-1a90-424d-9d9b-66fface4c607\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3100,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800\",\"uuid\":\"5cfbc9d0-1848-45bb-a325-32dd4e7759c8\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174822__x21985c/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1772,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1772,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":39700,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":250,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"dfcf0191-4aca-4d8f-b521-00f680c81fe7\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":39950,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":250,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"694207c9-7955-4025-b220-ad4c88833f9a\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":40100,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"6ba65c7c-d8ef-4ca4-b01f-0b57f90d4a68\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":40350,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":250,\"session_id\":\"5ddd0aea-0d8f-48ab-8f8a-03ad6fdbf27a\",\"uuid\":\"b0f08d97-2f3b-417a-96f6-b6e9b9ea8f32\"}"]}]}],"moreFiles":2,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work/PLAN.md","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174801__xc8e150/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174807__x5c5240/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174822__x21985c/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174831__x898ed5/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174837__x7ac903/agent.out"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0179ywD4nsYHspfxKPW6UbFA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
