{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013zg5cufcRtVEiuBFYXUr5n","type":"tool_result","content":"1034 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work/PLAN.md\n[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: PLAN.md. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40","uuid":"d2440dff-3f63-4f31-943a-5ae6f9428701","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:56.097Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1034 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work/PLAN.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: PLAN.md. Call Read before editing.]","bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":865,"oldLines":3,"newStart":865,"newLines":170,"lines":[" - **The title** shows a panel: \"**Controller or keyboard required.** Connect a controller or a keyboard to play.\" The engine's top-right menu button stays and opens Settings."," - **The attract mode runs** after the same 10 s idle. A touch exits it to the title, which shows the notice again."," - **The notice hides** the moment a key or a pad button arrives, and play works normally from then on.","+","+---","+","+## 6. Presentation: art, animation and audio","+","+### 6.1 Art direction","+","+- **The base is the engine's native 3D look,** the one the spike showed: code-drawn textures, `world.res = 'pixels'` (chunky low-res pixels), toon light, outlines on, characters as **cards** (`world.look = 'card'`: the rigs drawn as pixel art from the camera's own angle) and fog for the source's distance falloff.","+- **Lighting.** `torchShadows: 2`, `torchLights: 6`, the party's lantern as a `world.light` at the eyes, and `glowLights: 4` for spells.","+- **New art** wherever the source's feel needs it: wall features, doors, floor items, the creatures in §6.3, the boss, the brass UI, item icons and the stages for the title and the cutscenes.","+- **Props.** For generic set dressing (bones, barrels, crates, chains, cobwebs, banners, candles, tables), search the store first with `node tools/asset-find.mjs \"bones\"`, using `kaykit-dungeon-remastered`, `kenney-mini-dungeon` and `kenney-graveyard`. Cut a set with `tools/asset-set.mjs`, load it with `E.addAssets`, and place props with `world.shape(id, …)` or `{ shape }` in the legend.","+","+| Floor | Ground (`level.ground`, `colors`) | Walls (`side`, `color`) | Fog | Ambient `[sky, ground, power]` | Signature dressing |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| 1 The Hasp Drains | flagstone `#3e4a44 / #2a332f / #55615a`; a floor colour function paints dark-green **water channels** (6 units wide) down the Rat Channel and Cistern cells | brick `#4a5048` | `#06080a`, 24 → 150 | `#4a5a5a, #1a201e, 2.6` | floor drains (grates), dripping pipes (pen tubes), slime streaks, rusty chains, rat bones, sluice wheels |","+| 2 The Tumbler Halls | tiles `#5a4a3a / #3e3228 / #7a6450` | block `#6a5a48` | `#0a0806`, 40 → 220 | `#7a6048, #2a2018, 3.0` | turning **wall gears** (pen rings of teeth, slowly rotating), anvils, workbenches, cogs on the floor, forge glow (orange lights) in the Workshop |","+| 3 The Gloam Deeps | plain `#2a2434 / #1a1622 / #3a3248` | block `#2e2838` | `#040306`, 20 → 130 | `#3a3a5a, #141220, 2.2` | carved **eye reliefs** on walls (pen), shut-eye banners, bone piles, pale blue candles in the Chapel (lights) |","+| 4 The Eye's Vault | tiles `#3a3e46`; the arena floor colour function adds faint cyan rune lines | block `#30343c` | `#020204`, 30 → 200 | `#2a3040, #0c0e14, 2.0` | the boss's amber light, cyan lightning flashes, the 3 Great Locks' rune lights going out as they turn |","+","+- **Item icons.** Make about 60 of them as `E.sprite` strings, designed at 12×12 and drawn at ×1 on the cards and ×2 in the Party screen. Shade them with `E.tones`.","+- **Item models.** Each floor item also gets a tiny **3D model drawn with the pen**, lying flat at its quadrant spot:","+  - blade (sword, dagger): a thin box with a cross-guard;","+  - axe or mace: a head on a haft;","+  - crossbow; bolts or arrows: thin tubes;","+  - potion: a ball and a neck, in its colour;","+  - scroll: a tube; book: a box;","+  - key: a ring plus a shaft with teeth, in the key's colour;","+  - rock: a grey lump of balls; ration: a wrapped box;","+  - gear: a ring of boxes; ward: a toothed disc.","+","+### 6.2 The 3D presenter (`40–44`)","+","+- **Building a floor.**","+  - Map each cell to 2×2 level tiles (`#` → `##`, open → `..`). A torch wall feature turns the tile on its open side into `t`, the kit's NICHE trick.","+  - Make `new E.World3D(game, { level, look: 'card', res: 'pixels', torchLights: 6, torchShadows: 2, torchPower: 18, ambient, fog, sky: fogColour, camera: { mode: 'fixed' }, overlay: { fov: 60 }, onDraw })`.","+  - Create all of the floor's lights at build time (lantern, candles, forge glows, the boss), as the engine requires.","+  - Build every floor's world at boot and `prepare()` it, so a floor change never compiles a shader mid-game. On a floor change, swap the active world.","+- **Each frame,** from the sim state:","+  - **Camera:** `world.camera.fixed = { x, y, z: EYE + bob, yaw, pitch: −0.04, fov: 74 }`, from the party's tween (the kit's `place()`). A bump adds the lurch, a hit adds `game.shake`, a pit fall drops z by 40 and fades.","+  - **Doors and gates:** `world.thing('door', …, { w: 32, h: 46, swing })`; set `t.open` toward the sim's state and call `world.setSolid` when it opens.","+  - **Secret walls** (and **illusory walls**): a movable wall block that is **indistinguishable from the level's walls**. Try `world.box({ fixed: true, side: <the floor's side style>, color })` first; if it doesn't match, add a `wallBlock` helper to the 3D engine that reuses the level's wall material (risk 3, §13). A secret block sinks into the floor when opened; an illusory one never moves (the party's step through it is masked by the dissolve).","+  - **Wall features:** custom `E.World3D.THINGS`, drawn with the pen on the wall face (local +y out of the wall, as the kit's `wallLever`).","+","+    | THING | How to draw it |","+    |---|---|","+    | `wallLever` | the kit's |","+    | `wallButton` | a square stone and a brass boss that presses in |","+    | `catch` | a slightly proud stone with a crack, or a brass rivet plate; glints under Seeing |","+    | `alcove` | a dark recessed box that draws its items inside |","+    | `keyhole` | per key shape: iron round, warded cross, gear toothed, bone skull, ward discs |","+    | `plaque` | a stone tablet with dark glyph dashes |","+    | `grate`, `pipe`, `chain`, `gearWall` (rotating), `eyeRelief` | decor |","+    | `candle` | a holder, a wax stick and a flame glow when lit, paired with its light |","+    | `greatLock` | a big wheel with rune glow, spun over 2 s |","+    | `undergate` | a great door with 3 keyholes and 7 bolt bars that slide when a ward goes in |","+    | `cage` | bars |","+    | `shrine` | a ring of tiny rat statues |","+    | `clockFace` | a dial with 4 gear sockets and hands that move once the clock is whole |","+    | `altarSlab` | a floor slab |","+    | `stairs` | the kit's `stair` (down), plus `stairUp` |","+    | `pitEdge` | a dark hole with a lip; a bridge slab when bridged |","+    | `plate` | the kit's |","+    | `teleporterField` | a soft swirl glow, only when not silent |","+","+  - **Floor items:** pen models at the quadrant spots of the visible cells (`onDraw`).","+  - **Monsters:** cards (`world.mob` with `rig`, `blob` or `orb`) are steered toward their slot's position with `vx`/`vy` as the kit does (`fly: true` for fliers). Their `anim` comes from the sim: attack phase, hurt flash, `die` pose, sink. Pen-drawn creatures are drawn in `onDraw` from their sim state and a local animation clock (§6.3).","+  - **Projectiles and FX:** `world.glow` for bolts and orbs, pen bars for lightning, `game.particles` for sparks, embers, smoke and damage `text`, and `world.arc` for floor telegraphs (Bolt Rain).","+  - **First-person overlay:** with `world.overlay.pen`, draw the striking member's weapon swinging across its side of the view: left for places 1, 3 and 5, right for 2, 4 and 6. The crossbow rises and kicks; a caster's hand glows in the spell's colour.","+  - **Hover outlines and name tags:** project with `world.project`, then draw them in the HUD.","+- **NullView** implements the same interface (`enter(floor)`, `frame(r)`, `event(e)`, `pick(sx, sy)`) as no-ops for Node.","+","+### 6.3 Creature recipes","+","+The sizes follow the engine's guidance (heroes `size` 1.2 to 1.4, bosses larger). Every rig gets a real palette.","+","+| Creature | Build | Recipe | Animation notes |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| Drain Rat | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 3.6, ears: 'cat', tail: true, feet: true, mouth: 'fangs', colors: { base: '#6a5a50', dk: '#3e342e', lt: '#9a8a7a', eye: '#ff6a4a' } }` | fast squash scurry; the wind-up is a rear-back squash |","+| Bloat Leech | pen | 5 balls (r 4 → 2.5) along a sine curve on the floor, `#b89a9a` with `#7a5a5a` rings; a mouth ring of 6 small balls; a wet glint | the body undulates; it lunges out 6 units on the strike |","+| Latchkin | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: .85, build: 'chibi', hunch: .5, hood: true, outfit: 'tunic', bladeLen: 5, eyeGlow: '#ffd24a', colors: { skin: '#7a8a5a', hair: '#4a3a2a', cloth: '#6a4a32', pants: '#3a2e22', metal: '#9a9aa8' } }`, plus a pen ring of keys at the belt | the `thrust` move; it stays in a crouch-run while fleeing |","+| Drain Ooze | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 8, face: 'front', mouth: true, colors: { base: '#5a8a3a', dk: '#2e5a22', lt: '#9ad06a', spec: '#e8ffd0' } }` | a slow wobble; it slams by squashing down; it splashes green particles |","+| Rat Knot | pen | 6 rat-body balls in a ring with ear cones, tails as tubes knotted at the middle | the ring wobbles and turns; two bites a strike |","+| Snick, the Latch-Boss | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.0, build: 'bulky', hunch: .3, hat: { style: 'crown', color: '#c8a040' }, armor: true, outfit: 'coat', bladeLen: 9, eyeGlow: '#ffd24a', colors: { skin: '#7a8a5a', cloth: '#5a3a2a', plate: '#a08040' } }`, plus a pen cape of hanging keys | the `overhead` move; it rattles its keys at 50% when it calls for help |","+| Tinker Skeleton | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.2, build: 'skeleton', outfit: 'coat', bladeLen: 7, colors: { bone: '#d8cfb4', cloth: '#5a4030', metal: '#8a8a90' } }`, plus a pen hammer head on the blade | the `overhead` and `slash` moves; it collapses into bones on death |","+| Rustling | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 4.2, horns: true, feet: true, mouth: true, colors: { base: '#b8642a', dk: '#7a3a18', lt: '#e8a060' } }` | the horns twitch; it throws rust-flake particles when it hits |","+| Brass Spider | pen | abdomen ball r 7 and cephalothorax r 4.5 in `#b8923a`; 8 legs of 2 tubes each with procedural tetrapod gait (sine phase lifts); 4 red eye glows | legs step; it lunges on the strike; it falls apart into parts on death |","+| Clockwork Sentinel | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.6, build: 'bulky', armor: true, hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#8a6a3a' }, bladeLen: 14, eyeGlow: '#ff8a3a', colors: { cloth: '#6a4a2a', plate: '#b08a4a', metal: '#c8a868', skin: '#5a4a3a' } }`, plus a pen wind-up key turning on its back | the `twohand` move with a 0.8 s wind-up; the key spins faster during it |","+| Lidless Hound | pen | a quadruped (adapt the 3D horror kit's dogs, `src/starter3d/40-horror.js`): pale `#c8b8b0`, smooth eyeless head, long jaw | run, leap and bite |","+| Gloam Seer | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', outfit: 'robe', hood: true, weapon: 'staff', eyeGlow: '#8ae0ff', colors: { cloth: '#d8d0e8', hair: '#3a2a4a', skin: '#b8b0c8', trim: '#6a4a9a' } }`, plus an eye-sigil glow over the staff | the `cast` pose while charging a Locking Bolt (cyan glow growing) |","+| Gloam Warden | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.35, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#2a2434' }, weapon: 'staff', eyeGlow: '#e8e8ff', colors: { cloth: '#2a2434', plate: '#4a4458', metal: '#9a98a8', skin: '#b8b0c8' } }`, plus a pen halberd blade on the staff | the `thrust` move (reaches two cells) |","+| Gazer | card orb plus pen | an orb `{ color: '#e8a040', r: 4 }`; pen iris (a flattened ball `#3a8a6a`), pupil, two lid slabs, 3 fin cones | blinks; the pupil tracks the party; it glows before Spark Gaze |","+| Lockjaw Golem | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.9, build: 'bulky', armor: true, weapon: null, eyeGlow: '#7ad8ff', colors: { cloth: '#3a3e46', plate: '#5a606a', skin: '#4a4e56' } }`, plus a pen **padlock head** (box body and shackle tube) instead of a hat | the `haymaker` move; heavy footstep shakes |","+| **The Bolt-Holder** | pen | an eye ball r 14 (sclera `#e8e0c8` with red vein bars); a flattened amber iris r 7 (`#e8a030`) facing the party; a black pupil r 3.5 that dilates; upper and lower lid slabs that blink and narrow for the Gaze; **7 radial iron bolts** (bars 22 long and 2.5 thick, with 5×5×3 heads) that slide out 2 per Great Lock (the 7th, the keystone, never moves); cyan lightning arcs (jagged pen bars) between neighbouring bolt heads; a ±3 bob; an amber `world.light`; red tint and crack lines in phase 3 | it must not read as a beholder: no eyestalks, no mouth, no tentacles. It reads as a caged iron lantern-eye. |","+| Ghosts (race) | card, `E.Humanoid` | a hooded cloak in the player's seat colour, `fade 0.45`, a lantern glow in the seat colour, and the hub name as a HUD tag | they glide between the cells they report |","+","+**People** (portraits and cutscenes):","+- the party (§7.9);","+- Keywarden Imelda Strake: heroic, band crown, coat, navy and silver;","+- Magister Abel Lintel: robe, pointed hat, long white hair;","+- Ysolde Vane: robe, long hair, ghost blue, drawn translucent;","+- Tamsin: size 0.9, ponytail, green hood;","+- Durgan: bulky, braided beard, iron helmet;","+- Veil: robe, hood, eyes shut (draw them closed).","+","+### 6.4 Animation list (new, on the engine's rigs, tweens and pen)","+","+- **Party view.** Step glide with bob; turn ease; bump lurch; pit fall (drop and fade); teleport (a cut or a swirl); spinner (a short wobble only when *visible*: none for silent spinners); hit shake; level-up glow on the card; KO slump (the portrait tinted grey); death toll (the card turns to bones); first-person weapon swings for each weapon family (blade, axe, blunt, spear thrust, crossbow, bow, sling, throw, punch); casting hand glows.","+- **World.** Gates rising with a chain rattle and wooden doors swinging; levers flipping and buttons and catches pressing in; plates sinking; secret walls sinking; the trapdoor dropping open; the pit bridge rising; teleporter swirl; gears turning; candles lighting and guttering; the Great Locks spinning; the Undergate's 7 bolts drawing back one by one; the clock's hands moving once it is whole; the boss's bolts sliding, lids blinking, iris dilating and lightning arcing.","+- **Monsters.** Idle, move glide, wind-up telegraph (the move's `wind` phase, at least 0.5 s), strike, hurt flash and recoil, death (the `die` pose, then sink; blobs squash flat; constructs fall apart into pen parts; the leech curls).","+- **UI.** Cooldown wipes; damage pops; card shake; chevrons; focus pulse; toast slides; the title logo shimmer.","+","+### 6.5 Audio: code only, no files","+","+- **The music director.** It plays a song per floor through `game.audio.music(song, { fade: 1 })`. Every dungeon song carries a `fight` track (drums and bass, `on: false`) that comes in with `audio.layer('fight', 1, .5)` when any monster engages and goes out 4 s after the last one. Stings use `audio.sting`. All songs are original, in the step-sequencer format (`{ bpm, steps, tracks: [{ wave, vol, notes }] }`).","+","+  | Song | Feel | Seed motif (original) |","+  |---|---|---|","+  | `title`, \"The City of a Thousand Locks\" | 76 bpm, D minor, bell pulses over a low triangle | `D4 - F4 A4 G4 - F4 E4 \\| D4 - - - C4 E4 G4 F4 \\| E4 - D4 C#4 D4 - - -` |","+  | `drains` | 60 bpm, a sparse drone, a lonely pulse every 8 bars, drips as sfx | low `A1` drone; a `pulse25` figure `A3 . C4 . E4 . . . \\| D4 . C4 . B3 . . .` |","+  | `tumbler` | 96 bpm in 6/8, ticking percussion | `drums` `h . h c . h` over `E2 . B2 E2 . B2` |","+  | `gloam` | 54 bpm, sine pads, a tritone colour | `C3` plus `F#3` pads, a choir-like sine line in long notes |","+  | `vault` / `boss` | 138 bpm, saw bass, lightning arpeggios | `A2 A2 . A2 C3 . A2 . \\| G2 G2 . G2 Bb2 . G2 .`, arps `A4 E5 A5 E5` |","+  | `camp` | 70 bpm, a lullaby | the title motif in a major key, triangle |","+  | `ending` | 84 bpm, D major | the title motif resolved |","+  | stings | — | `levelUp`, `deed`, `secret`, `wardFound`, `gameOver`, `victory`, `npcJoin` |","+","+- **Sound effects** (`audio.define`, the engine's voice format; the kit's `SOUNDS` are the template). Define every one of these:","+  - steps per floor: wet stone, metal grating, dust, stone;","+  - turn, bump, door open and close, gate grind, lever clank, button click, catch click, plate thunk, secret-wall grind, illusion shimmer, trapdoor, fall and land;","+  - teleporter whoosh (visible ones only), spinner grind, dart volley;","+  - key turn, lock fail, lockpick scratch and snap, alcove place and take;","+  - item pickup, drop and throw whoosh, land clatter, eat crunch, drink glug, scroll unroll, wand zap;","+  - swings (blade, axe, blunt), crossbow and bow twangs, sling whirr;","+  - hits (flesh, metal, bone, ooze), miss whiff, crit clang, party hurt;","+  - level up, death toll, raise;","+  - each spell: cast, travel loop and impact;","+  - monster voices for each type (squeak, slurp, chitter, rattle, clank, growl, chant, gaze hum);","+  - boss: roar, lightning crack, bolt slam, lock turn and shriek;","+  - UI: move, confirm, back, error, tab;","+  - ambience loops per floor: drips, distant gears, whispers, a low hum.","+","+  Pan by bearing with the patched `{ pan }` (§3.9).","+- **Voices: the babble synth** (`50-audio.js`, on `game.audio.ctx` and routed to the voice bus).","+  - **Per-speaker profile:** `{ base: Hz, range: semitones, rate: syllables/s, wave, formant: ×, breath: 0..1, vib: [Hz, depth], echo: 0..1 }`. The profiles:","+","+    | Speaker | base Hz | range | rate | wave | other |","+    |---|---|---|---|---|---|","+    | Narrator | 95 | 3 | 9 | triangle | echo 0.2 |","+    | Keywarden | 170 | 4 | 12 | square | |","+    | Lintel | 120 | 5 | 10 | saw | |","+    | Tamsin | 300 | 7 | 15 | pulse | |","+    | Durgan | 105 | 4 | 11 | square | |","+    | Ysolde | 220 | 5 | 9 | sine | echo 0.4 |","+    | Veil | 240 | 3 | 10 | triangle | breath 0.5 |","+    | Snick | 260 | 8 | 16 | square | |","+    | Bolt-Holder | 70 | 6 | 8 | saw | ring mod 30 Hz, echo 0.5 |","+","+    The party members also get profiles from their race and sex.","+  - **Driving it.** Set `talk.voice = null`. Each update, read `talk.shown`; for every two new letters (and on every vowel), emit a syllable.","+  - **The syllable:**","+    - The vowel picks a formant pair (F1/F2): a 800/1200, e 400/2000, i 300/2300, o 450/800, u 325/700, × `formant`.","+    - The letter's code picks the pitch inside `range`, so a word always sounds the same.","+    - Plosives (b d g k p t) add a 10 ms noise click; fricatives (f s v z h) add a 40 ms high-passed noise; nasals (m n) add a low hum.","+    - `?` rises at the end, `!` is louder and higher, `.` pauses 0.15 s and `,` pauses 0.08 s.","+  - **The voice:** an oscillator into two parallel band-pass filters (Q 8) into a gain envelope (5 ms attack, 0.6× hold, 30 ms release), then the bus.","+  - **Barks:** short babble for party pain (\"Oof!\"), effort (\"Hah!\"), level-up (\"Yes!\") and casting, and for monster taunts.","+  - **Test it in Node.** `babble.plan(text, profile)` returns syllable events (time, pitch, F1, F2, noise) and must be deterministic (§14). In Node there is no AudioContext, so the synth is a no-op."]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2037,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2037,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh2hEJvV5XcsSN4zciQc\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4856,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":484119,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":4856},\"output_tokens\":5,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714\",\"uuid\":\"7b0a89f0-1fd4-443e-a459-8518d4f15bcd\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:35:53.201Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh2hE4YH11votUt7XmuM\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":906,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh2hEJvV5XcsSN4zciQc\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01GuJWvM6HGdJ1fbf9rF34fW\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":140,\"limit\":200},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4856,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":484119,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":4856},\"output_tokens\":5,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714\",\"uuid\":\"f698d97f-a682-41e2-9689-96ae0c6c6c0f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:35:54.404Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh2hE4YH11votUt7XmuM\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01GuJWvM6HGdJ1fbf9rF34fW\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":140,\"limit\":200}}}"," {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01GuJWvM6HGdJ1fbf9rF34fW\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"140\\t- **Tooling:** Node ≥ 20 (24 is installed); Playwright **1.63.0** (the handoff pins it) and Chromium for browser checks;\\n141\\t  the handoff's `tools/check.mjs`, `filmstrip.mjs` and `replay.mjs`; Python 3 for the hub harness's local server.\\n142\\t- **Rules:** no other runtime libraries and no network at runtime. The hub client only talks to its parent frame.\\n143\\t- **Machine note:** `/tmp` was almost full when this was planned. If npm or Playwright fail with ENOSPC, set\\n144\\t  `TMPDIR=DEV/.tmp`.\\n145\\t\\n146\\t**Fetching the sources** (M0):\\n147\\t\\n148\\t```sh\\n149\\tgit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git DEV/.src/my-3d2dge\\n150\\tcd DEV/.src/my-3d2dge && git sparse-checkout set --no-cone /dist/handoff/ /src/mocap/mocap.js /src/mocap/readable.js \\\\\\n151\\t  /src/mocap/sets/ /src/mocap/catalogs/ /tools/anim-set.mjs /docs/MOCAP.md\\n152\\t# (add any file anim-set.mjs imports if it complains)\\n153\\tcurl -fsSL -o DEV/vendor/aihub-session.js https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\\n154\\tfor f in harness.html bridge.js round.js README.md; do curl -fsSL -o DEV/hub/$f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done\\n155\\t```\\n156\\t\\n157\\t### 3.2 Engine patches\\n158\\t\\n159\\tAll patches go in `DEV/engine/my-3d2dge.js`. Mark each with `// AOA:`, list it in `DEV/ENGINE-CHANGES.md` with what\\n160\\tchanged and why, give it a headless test, and mention it in the About screen's Engine Feedback.\\n161\\t\\n162\\t1. **PlayStation symbols in the pixel font.** The 5×7 font table `G57` (around line 1322) lacks ✕ ○ □ △, which\\n163\\t   `input.label()` returns for PlayStation pads. Add them, plus ◀ ▶ for steppers.\\n164\\t2. **Button symbols setting.** Change the standard `glyphs` setting (around line 2999) to `{ group: 'Game', label:\\n165\\t   'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation ✕ ○ □ △'], ['xbox',\\n166\\t   'Xbox A B X Y']] }`. That way it appears on the Settings screen and defaults to PlayStation, as TASK.md requires.\\n167\\t3. **Per-letter dialog voice.** In `Dialog`'s typing (around line 8956, `if (this.voice && …) this.game.audio.sfx(this.voice)`),\\n168\\t   when `typeof this.voice === 'function'`, call `this.voice(ch, index, pageText, this)` for **every** newly shown\\n169\\t   letter. Do not skip every other letter, and do not call sfx. This drives the Animalese voices (§4.24.3).\\n170\\t4. **Audio.**\\n171\\t   - (a) Add a third bus `_voxBus` under `_master`, with `audio.voiceVolume` and a standard setting `voices` (Sound\\n172\\t     group, slider, default .8). Add `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')`, which returns the GainNode, or null\\n173\\t     headless.\\n174\\t   - (b) New options for a music track:\\n175\\t     - `decay` (seconds): an exponential pluck envelope instead of a held note;\\n176\\t     - `filter: 'lowpass'` with `cutoff` (Hz);\\n177\\t     - `detune` (cents): a second detuned oscillator;\\n178\\t     - `wave`: may name an entry in `audio.instruments`, a registry of PeriodicWave partial tables `{ real: [], imag: [] }`,\\n179\\t       so songs can use `steel`, `marimba`, `pluck`, `bell`, `organ` and `pad` (§4.24.1).\\n180\\t5. **Humanoid** (the art patch, §4.25.2):\\n181\\t   - (a) an `athletic` entry in `BUILDS`;\\n182\\t   - (b) `outfit: 'swim'` with `swim: { cut, pattern, colors: { main, accent, trim }, brief }`. Also allow\\n183\\t     `o.pattern` on the `shirt` outfit, for Sonny's loud shirt.\\n184\\t   - (c) hair styles `twinbuns`, `bun`, `braid`, `bob`, `puff` and `curly`;\\n185\\t   - (d) hat styles `sunhat` and `visor`;\\n186\\t   - (e) an `extras` hook: `rig.extras = [{ at: 'head' | 'face' | 'neck' | 'hair' | 'wristL' | 'wristR', draw(g, P,\\n187\\t     rig, view) }]`. It is called inside `draw` with the projected anchor point and depth-sorted with the head and torso.\\n188\\t     Sunglasses, flowers, necklaces, masks, glasses and wristbands use it.\\n189\\t   - (f) bare feet: when `colors.boot === colors.skin`, draw simple feet with no boot cuff; also an optional sandal strap\\n190\\t     color.\\n191\\t   - (g) new held poses: `vready`, `bump`, `set`, `block`, `toss`, `highfive`, `clap`, `facepalm`, `peace`, `lookback`,\\n192\\t     `stretch`, `sit`, `sunbathe`. Build them as `cheer`, `cast` and `kneel` are built in `solvePose`: joint targets,\\n193\\t     arms solved with `E.ik3`, blended by `poseW`.\\n194\\t6. **Session combo.** Add `game.input.reserveCombo = [8, 9]`: while pad button 8 (Create/View) is held, button 9\\n195\\t   (Options/Menu) presses reach no action. This is an AI Hub rule.\\n196\\t7. **Touch-off mode.** `new E.Game({ touch: 'never' })` hides touch buttons and the touch stick for good and hides the\\n197\\t   Touch settings group, but keeps the corner's menu button. Touch-only devices use it (§4.1.5).\\n198\\t8. Register the `court` and `servecam` views. Adding them to `E.VIEWS`, or making them in game code with `new E.View`,\\n199\\t   are both fine.\\n200\\t\\n201\\t### 3.3 Folder layout\\n202\\t\\n203\\t```\\n204\\t./PLAN.md                    this plan\\n205\\t./<GAME>.html                the deliverable (built; never edited by hand)\\n206\\t./exit-interview.json\\n207\\tDEV/\\n208\\t  package.json               { \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\", \\\"scripts\\\": { \\\"build\\\": \\\"node tools/build.mjs\\\", \\\"test\\\": \\\"node test/run.mjs\\\" },\\n209\\t                               \\\"devDependencies\\\": { \\\"playwright\\\": \\\"1.63.0\\\" } }\\n210\\t  README-DEV.md              how to build, run and test; conventions\\n211\\t  ENGINE-CHANGES.md          every engine patch: what and why\\n212\\t  .src/                      sparse clone of the engine repository (reference only; never bundled)\\n213\\t  engine/my-3d2dge.js        the patched engine\\n214\\t  vendor/aihub-session.js    unmodified hub client\\n215\\t  vendor/mocap/readable.js, mocap.js, aoa-clips.js     (the cut clip set, name AOA)\\n216\\t  hub/harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md      (tests only; never bundled)\\n217\\t  src/*.js                   game modules (§3.6), concatenated in name order\\n218\\t  build/game.js              generated: every src file inside one IIFE\\n219\\t  build/dev.html             generated: engine, vendor and build/game.js as separate <script src>, for quick looks\\n220\\t  tools/build.mjs            builds build/ and the deliverable\\n221\\t  tools/rigsheet.mjs         every fighter × suit × facing × view to test-output/rigsheet/*.png (Playwright)\\n222\\t  tools/check.mjs, filmstrip.mjs, replay.mjs, asset-sheet.mjs, asset-find.mjs, asset-set.mjs   (copied from the handoff)\\n223\\t  test/run.mjs               THE test command (§9)\\n224\\t  test/lib/load.mjs, fakehub.mjs, bots.mjs, assert.mjs\\n225\\t  test/suites/*.test.mjs\\n226\\t  test-output/               screenshots, filmstrips, rig sheets (never bundled)\\n227\\t```\\n228\\t\\n229\\t### 3.4 Build (`node tools/build.mjs`, also `npm run build`)\\n230\\t\\n231\\t1. Concatenate `src/*.js` in lexical order into `build/game.js`, wrapped as\\n232\\t   `(() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge, G = {}; window.AOA = G; /* files */ })();`. Each src file is plain code\\n233\\t   that adds to `G`: no import or export.\\n234\\t2. Write `build/dev.html`.\\n235\\t3. Write the deliverable html. Order matters:\\n236\\t   ```html\\n237\\t   <!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n238\\t   <script>/* vendor/aihub-session.js, verbatim */</script>        <!-- first script, right after meta charset (hub rule) -->\\n239\\t   <meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"> … (the tags of §4.23)\\n240\\t   <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\">\\n241\\t   <title>Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball</title>\\n242\\t   <style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}</style>\\n243\\t   </head><body>\\n244\\t   <!-- the handoff template's #e3-boot splash div, retitled AHEAD OR ALIVE -->\\n245\\t   <canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas>\\n246\\t   <script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script>\\n247\\t   <script>/* vendor/mocap/readable.js + mocap.js + aoa-clips.js */</script>\\n248\\t   <script>/* build/game.js */</script>\\n249\\t   </body></html>\\n250\\t   ```\\n251\\t4. Escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\\\/script`. Add no external URL. Print the file size.\\n252\\t5. The build never edits the vendor client.\\n253\\t\\n254\\t### 3.5 Runtime architecture\\n255\\t\\n256\\t- **One game.**\\n257\\t  ```js\\n258\\t  G.game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'court', id: 'ahead-or-alive', bg: '#0a2d3d',\\n259\\t    menu: hub ? false : { items, settings, quit: 'title' },\\n260\\t    autoPause: !hub, corner: !hub, fullscreen: hub ? false : true, touch: touchOnly ? 'never' : 'auto' })\\n261\\t  ```\\n262\\t  Here `hub = window.AIHub && AIHub.active` is known on the first line, and `items` are the pause actions of §4.2.\\n263\\t  Add `G.ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme })` for themed standard screens, toasts and tutorial cards. If the Shell's pause\\n264\\t  screen doesn't list the `menu.items`, pass them again as `screens: { pause: { actions } }`. A headless test checks the\\n265\\t  pause screen lists them.\\n266\\t- **Scenes** (`game.start({ scenes, scene, boot })`): `title`, `menu`, `attract`, `charselect`, `cutscene` (runs story\\n267\\t  scripts), `map`, `location` (every walkable place, entered with `{ loc }`), `match`, `poolhop`, `shop`, `wardrobe`,\\n268\\t  `journal`, `album`, `casino` (cashier, slots, blackjack and roulette as sub-states), `dayend`, `results`, `credits`,\\n269\\t  `about`, `howto`, `exhibition` (setup and join), `hub` (AI Hub card and match). Gameplay scenes are `pausable: true`;\\n270\\t  title, menu, attract, about, credits and the hub scene are not.\\n271\\t- **Overlays.** `G.overlay` is a stack for the dev panel, photo mode, toasts, the touch-only notice and the attract\\n272\\t  watcher. Wrap every scene with `G.wrapScene(scene)`: its `update` first calls `G.overlay.update(dt)`, which returns\\n273\\t  true when an overlay took the input, and its `draw` ends with `G.overlay.draw(r)`.\\n274\\t- **State.** `G.state` is the vacation save object (§4.19), or null outside a vacation. `G.session` is the\\n275\\t  exhibition/hub match config. `G.unlocks` lives in `E.store('aoa-unlocks')`.\\n276\\t- **Tuning.** `G.T` is the live object every system reads every step. It is built from `G.TUNING` defaults (§4.22.2),\\n277\\t  with dev overrides from `E.store('aoa-dev-tuning')`.\\n278\\t- **Randomness.** Gameplay never calls `Math.random`; use `G.rng(stream)`:\\n279\\t  - `world`: schedules, moods, weather and stock (seeded per save);\\n280\\t  - `match`: AI rolls, net cords (seeded per match);\\n281\\t  - `casino`;\\n282\\t  - `cosmetic`: crowd, particles, voices (never affects state).\\n283\\t  In a hub shared world the host seeds `match` from `AIHub.rng('match')`. A test greps `src/` for `Math.random(`.\\n284\\t- **Event bus.** `G.bus.on/off/emit` carries `point`, `touch`, `fault`, `matchEnd`, `gift`, `affinity`, `purchase`,\\n285\\t  `slotEnd`, `dayEnd`, `photo` and `story`. Commentary, stats, tests and the attract director listen to it.\\n286\\t- **Debug handle.** `game.debug = { snapshot(), tools }` (§9.2). The dev panel's buttons call the same `tools`.\\n287\\t\\n288\\t### 3.6 Source modules (`DEV/src/`)\\n289\\t\\n290\\t| File | Holds |\\n291\\t| --- | --- |\\n292\\t| `00-core.js` | G namespace, constants, rng streams, event bus, scene wrapper, overlay stack, helpers (`G.fmtMoney` → `S$12,500`) |\\n293\\t| `01-tuning.js` | `G.TUNING` (every slider: default, min, max, step, group, label, unit) and difficulty presets |\\n294\\t| `02-data-cast.js` | fighters, hosts and staff: looks, stats, tastes, likes, voice profiles, schedules, celebration clips |\\n295\\t| `03-data-items.js` | swimsuits, accessories, gifts, shops and stock rotation |\\n296\\t| `04-data-world.js` | location maps (rows, legends, props, spots, interactables), island map, calendar, weather, events |\\n297\\t| `05-data-text.js` | all dialogue as `E.Story` nodes, commentary lines, UI strings, How to Play and About texts |\\n298\\t| `06-data-music.js` | songs (step notation), jingles, instrument tables |\\n299\\t| `10-input.js` | action maps per context, devices, glyph icons, prompt drawing, the touch-only gate, mouse helpers |\\n300\\t| `11-ui.js` | the 10-foot canvas UI kit (§4.2) |\\n301\\t| `12-audio.js` | SFX defines, music control and layers, ambience loops, the Animalese voice synth |\\n302\\t| `13-rigs.js` | the rig factory (cast + suit + accessories), extras drawers, portraits |\\n303\\t| `14-world-art.js` | resort `E.SHAPES` and `E.MATERIALS`, backdrops and lighting by time of day, water, effects helpers |\\n304\\t| `15-anim.js` | move timelines, the arm-IK overlay, celebrations and emotes, mocap glue |\\n305\\t| `20-ball.js` | closed-form ball flight, launches, aiming, prediction, net and ground events |\\n306\\t| `21-rules.js` | the referee: touches, faults, scoring, serve rotation, match end, stats |\\n307\\t| `22-players.js` | player entity: movement, actions, the timing judge, the human controller |\\n308\\t| `23-ai.js` | volleyball AI: assignment, positioning, decisions, error model, chemistry, spectacle mode |\\n309\\t| `24-match.js` | the Match: phases, cameras, HUD, crowd, commentary, celebrations, replay, results |\\n310\\t| `25-netplay.js` | AI Hub shared-world host and client sync, the card, reporting |\\n311\\t| `30-vacation.js` | calendar, slots, weather, schedules, moods, affinity, partners, money, events, saves |\\n312\\t| `31-map.js` | the island map scene |\\n313\\t| `32-location.js` | the walkable location scene, NPC spots, talk menu, interactables |\\n314\\t| `33-shop.js` | shops, wardrobe, gift bag, journal |\\n315\\t| `34-story.js` | `E.Story` wiring, cutscene scripts, portraits and voices, prologue, party, endings |\\n316\\t| `40-poolhop.js` | Pool Hop |\\n317\\t| `41-casino.js` | casino floor, cashier, slots, blackjack, roulette |\\n318\\t| `42-photo.js` | photo mode and album |\\n319\\t| `50-title.js` | boot steps, title, main menu, How to Play, About & Credits |\\n320\\t| `51-attract.js` | the attract director |\\n321\\t| `52-exhibition.js` | Beach Match setup and local join |\\n322\\t| `53-dev.js` | the dev panel |\\n323\\t| `54-results.js` | match results, day end, vacation results, credits roll |\\n324\\t| `99-main.js` | building the game, scene registry, hub detection, boot, `game.start` |\\n325\\t\\n326\\t---\\n327\\t\\n328\\t## 4. Systems\\n329\\t\\n330\\t### 4.1 Input, devices, glyphs, prompts (`10-input.js`)\\n331\\t\\n332\\t**4.1.1 Action maps.** Each scene sets an `input` preset. Every preset includes the engine defaults for `up`, `down`,\\n333\\t`left` and `right` (WASD, arrows, d-pad, left stick) and for `start` and `pause`.\\n334\\t\\n335\\t| Preset | Action | Keyboard | Mouse | Pad (standard mapping) |\\n336\\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n337\\t| MATCH | `play`: bump, set, spike, serve (timed) | Space, J | Left | 0 ✕/A |\\n338\\t| | `shot`: tip/cut shot, block, jump serve, free ball | E, K | Right | 2 □/X |\\n339\\t| | `dive` | Left Shift, L | — | 1 ○/B |\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714\",\"uuid\":\"9cc3137d-7847-4aad-b588-f41af7d6d38f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:35:54.410Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md\",\"content\":\"- **Tooling:** Node ≥ 20 (24 is installed); Playwright **1.63.0** (the handoff pins it) and Chromium for browser checks;\\n  the handoff's `tools/check.mjs`, `filmstrip.mjs` and `replay.mjs`; Python 3 for the hub harness's local server.\\n- **Rules:** no other runtime libraries and no network at runtime. The hub client only talks to its parent frame.\\n- **Machine note:** `/tmp` was almost full when this was planned. If npm or Playwright fail with ENOSPC, set\\n  `TMPDIR=DEV/.tmp`.\\n\\n**Fetching the sources** (M0):\\n\\n```sh\\ngit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git DEV/.src/my-3d2dge\\ncd DEV/.src/my-3d2dge && git sparse-checkout set --no-cone /dist/handoff/ /src/mocap/mocap.js /src/mocap/readable.js \\\\\\n  /src/mocap/sets/ /src/mocap/catalogs/ /tools/anim-set.mjs /docs/MOCAP.md\\n# (add any file anim-set.mjs imports if it complains)\\ncurl -fsSL -o DEV/vendor/aihub-session.js https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\\nfor f in harness.html bridge.js round.js README.md; do curl -fsSL -o DEV/hub/$f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done\\n```\\n\\n### 3.2 Engine patches\\n\\nAll patches go in `DEV/engine/my-3d2dge.js`. Mark each with `// AOA:`, list it in `DEV/ENGINE-CHANGES.md` with what\\nchanged and why, give it a headless test, and mention it in the About screen's Engine Feedback.\\n\\n1. **PlayStation symbols in the pixel font.** The 5×7 font table `G57` (around line 1322) lacks ✕ ○ □ △, which\\n   `input.label()` returns for PlayStation pads. Add them, plus ◀ ▶ for steppers.\\n2. **Button symbols setting.** Change the standard `glyphs` setting (around line 2999) to `{ group: 'Game', label:\\n   'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation ✕ ○ □ △'], ['xbox',\\n   'Xbox A B X Y']] }`. That way it appears on the Settings screen and defaults to PlayStation, as TASK.md requires.\\n3. **Per-letter dialog voice.** In `Dialog`'s typing (around line 8956, `if (this.voice && …) this.game.audio.sfx(this.voice)`),\\n   when `typeof this.voice === 'function'`, call `this.voice(ch, index, pageText, this)` for **every** newly shown\\n   letter. Do not skip every other letter, and do not call sfx. This drives the Animalese voices (§4.24.3).\\n4. **Audio.**\\n   - (a) Add a third bus `_voxBus` under `_master`, with `audio.voiceVolume` and a standard setting `voices` (Sound\\n     group, slider, default .8). Add `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')`, which returns the GainNode, or null\\n     headless.\\n   - (b) New options for a music track:\\n     - `decay` (seconds): an exponential pluck envelope instead of a held note;\\n     - `filter: 'lowpass'` with `cutoff` (Hz);\\n     - `detune` (cents): a second detuned oscillator;\\n     - `wave`: may name an entry in `audio.instruments`, a registry of PeriodicWave partial tables `{ real: [], imag: [] }`,\\n       so songs can use `steel`, `marimba`, `pluck`, `bell`, `organ` and `pad` (§4.24.1).\\n5. **Humanoid** (the art patch, §4.25.2):\\n   - (a) an `athletic` entry in `BUILDS`;\\n   - (b) `outfit: 'swim'` with `swim: { cut, pattern, colors: { main, accent, trim }, brief }`. Also allow\\n     `o.pattern` on the `shirt` outfit, for Sonny's loud shirt.\\n   - (c) hair styles `twinbuns`, `bun`, `braid`, `bob`, `puff` and `curly`;\\n   - (d) hat styles `sunhat` and `visor`;\\n   - (e) an `extras` hook: `rig.extras = [{ at: 'head' | 'face' | 'neck' | 'hair' | 'wristL' | 'wristR', draw(g, P,\\n     rig, view) }]`. It is called inside `draw` with the projected anchor point and depth-sorted with the head and torso.\\n     Sunglasses, flowers, necklaces, masks, glasses and wristbands use it.\\n   - (f) bare feet: when `colors.boot === colors.skin`, draw simple feet with no boot cuff; also an optional sandal strap\\n     color.\\n   - (g) new held poses: `vready`, `bump`, `set`, `block`, `toss`, `highfive`, `clap`, `facepalm`, `peace`, `lookback`,\\n     `stretch`, `sit`, `sunbathe`. Build them as `cheer`, `cast` and `kneel` are built in `solvePose`: joint targets,\\n     arms solved with `E.ik3`, blended by `poseW`.\\n6. **Session combo.** Add `game.input.reserveCombo = [8, 9]`: while pad button 8 (Create/View) is held, button 9\\n   (Options/Menu) presses reach no action. This is an AI Hub rule.\\n7. **Touch-off mode.** `new E.Game({ touch: 'never' })` hides touch buttons and the touch stick for good and hides the\\n   Touch settings group, but keeps the corner's menu button. Touch-only devices use it (§4.1.5).\\n8. Register the `court` and `servecam` views. Adding them to `E.VIEWS`, or making them in game code with `new E.View`,\\n   are both fine.\\n\\n### 3.3 Folder layout\\n\\n```\\n./PLAN.md                    this plan\\n./<GAME>.html                the deliverable (built; never edited by hand)\\n./exit-interview.json\\nDEV/\\n  package.json               { \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\", \\\"scripts\\\": { \\\"build\\\": \\\"node tools/build.mjs\\\", \\\"test\\\": \\\"node test/run.mjs\\\" },\\n                               \\\"devDependencies\\\": { \\\"playwright\\\": \\\"1.63.0\\\" } }\\n  README-DEV.md              how to build, run and test; conventions\\n  ENGINE-CHANGES.md          every engine patch: what and why\\n  .src/                      sparse clone of the engine repository (reference only; never bundled)\\n  engine/my-3d2dge.js        the patched engine\\n  vendor/aihub-session.js    unmodified hub client\\n  vendor/mocap/readable.js, mocap.js, aoa-clips.js     (the cut clip set, name AOA)\\n  hub/harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md      (tests only; never bundled)\\n  src/*.js                   game modules (§3.6), concatenated in name order\\n  build/game.js              generated: every src file inside one IIFE\\n  build/dev.html             generated: engine, vendor and build/game.js as separate <script src>, for quick looks\\n  tools/build.mjs            builds build/ and the deliverable\\n  tools/rigsheet.mjs         every fighter × suit × facing × view to test-output/rigsheet/*.png (Playwright)\\n  tools/check.mjs, filmstrip.mjs, replay.mjs, asset-sheet.mjs, asset-find.mjs, asset-set.mjs   (copied from the handoff)\\n  test/run.mjs               THE test command (§9)\\n  test/lib/load.mjs, fakehub.mjs, bots.mjs, assert.mjs\\n  test/suites/*.test.mjs\\n  test-output/               screenshots, filmstrips, rig sheets (never bundled)\\n```\\n\\n### 3.4 Build (`node tools/build.mjs`, also `npm run build`)\\n\\n1. Concatenate `src/*.js` in lexical order into `build/game.js`, wrapped as\\n   `(() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge, G = {}; window.AOA = G; /* files */ })();`. Each src file is plain code\\n   that adds to `G`: no import or export.\\n2. Write `build/dev.html`.\\n3. Write the deliverable html. Order matters:\\n   ```html\\n   <!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n   <script>/* vendor/aihub-session.js, verbatim */</script>        <!-- first script, right after meta charset (hub rule) -->\\n   <meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"> … (the tags of §4.23)\\n   <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\">\\n   <title>Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball</title>\\n   <style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}</style>\\n   </head><body>\\n   <!-- the handoff template's #e3-boot splash div, retitled AHEAD OR ALIVE -->\\n   <canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas>\\n   <script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script>\\n   <script>/* vendor/mocap/readable.js + mocap.js + aoa-clips.js */</script>\\n   <script>/* build/game.js */</script>\\n   </body></html>\\n   ```\\n4. Escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\\\/script`. Add no external URL. Print the file size.\\n5. The build never edits the vendor client.\\n\\n### 3.5 Runtime architecture\\n\\n- **One game.**\\n  ```js\\n  G.game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'court', id: 'ahead-or-alive', bg: '#0a2d3d',\\n    menu: hub ? false : { items, settings, quit: 'title' },\\n    autoPause: !hub, corner: !hub, fullscreen: hub ? false : true, touch: touchOnly ? 'never' : 'auto' })\\n  ```\\n  Here `hub = window.AIHub && AIHub.active` is known on the first line, and `items` are the pause actions of §4.2.\\n  Add `G.ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme })` for themed standard screens, toasts and tutorial cards. If the Shell's pause\\n  screen doesn't list the `menu.items`, pass them again as `screens: { pause: { actions } }`. A headless test checks the\\n  pause screen lists them.\\n- **Scenes** (`game.start({ scenes, scene, boot })`): `title`, `menu`, `attract`, `charselect`, `cutscene` (runs story\\n  scripts), `map`, `location` (every walkable place, entered with `{ loc }`), `match`, `poolhop`, `shop`, `wardrobe`,\\n  `journal`, `album`, `casino` (cashier, slots, blackjack and roulette as sub-states), `dayend`, `results`, `credits`,\\n  `about`, `howto`, `exhibition` (setup and join), `hub` (AI Hub card and match). Gameplay scenes are `pausable: true`;\\n  title, menu, attract, about, credits and the hub scene are not.\\n- **Overlays.** `G.overlay` is a stack for the dev panel, photo mode, toasts, the touch-only notice and the attract\\n  watcher. Wrap every scene with `G.wrapScene(scene)`: its `update` first calls `G.overlay.update(dt)`, which returns\\n  true when an overlay took the input, and its `draw` ends with `G.overlay.draw(r)`.\\n- **State.** `G.state` is the vacation save object (§4.19), or null outside a vacation. `G.session` is the\\n  exhibition/hub match config. `G.unlocks` lives in `E.store('aoa-unlocks')`.\\n- **Tuning.** `G.T` is the live object every system reads every step. It is built from `G.TUNING` defaults (§4.22.2),\\n  with dev overrides from `E.store('aoa-dev-tuning')`.\\n- **Randomness.** Gameplay never calls `Math.random`; use `G.rng(stream)`:\\n  - `world`: schedules, moods, weather and stock (seeded per save);\\n  - `match`: AI rolls, net cords (seeded per match);\\n  - `casino`;\\n  - `cosmetic`: crowd, particles, voices (never affects state).\\n  In a hub shared world the host seeds `match` from `AIHub.rng('match')`. A test greps `src/` for `Math.random(`.\\n- **Event bus.** `G.bus.on/off/emit` carries `point`, `touch`, `fault`, `matchEnd`, `gift`, `affinity`, `purchase`,\\n  `slotEnd`, `dayEnd`, `photo` and `story`. Commentary, stats, tests and the attract director listen to it.\\n- **Debug handle.** `game.debug = { snapshot(), tools }` (§9.2). The dev panel's buttons call the same `tools`.\\n\\n### 3.6 Source modules (`DEV/src/`)\\n\\n| File | Holds |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `00-core.js` | G namespace, constants, rng streams, event bus, scene wrapper, overlay stack, helpers (`G.fmtMoney` → `S$12,500`) |\\n| `01-tuning.js` | `G.TUNING` (every slider: default, min, max, step, group, label, unit) and difficulty presets |\\n| `02-data-cast.js` | fighters, hosts and staff: looks, stats, tastes, likes, voice profiles, schedules, celebration clips |\\n| `03-data-items.js` | swimsuits, accessories, gifts, shops and stock rotation |\\n| `04-data-world.js` | location maps (rows, legends, props, spots, interactables), island map, calendar, weather, events |\\n| `05-data-text.js` | all dialogue as `E.Story` nodes, commentary lines, UI strings, How to Play and About texts |\\n| `06-data-music.js` | songs (step notation), jingles, instrument tables |\\n| `10-input.js` | action maps per context, devices, glyph icons, prompt drawing, the touch-only gate, mouse helpers |\\n| `11-ui.js` | the 10-foot canvas UI kit (§4.2) |\\n| `12-audio.js` | SFX defines, music control and layers, ambience loops, the Animalese voice synth |\\n| `13-rigs.js` | the rig factory (cast + suit + accessories), extras drawers, portraits |\\n| `14-world-art.js` | resort `E.SHAPES` and `E.MATERIALS`, backdrops and lighting by time of day, water, effects helpers |\\n| `15-anim.js` | move timelines, the arm-IK overlay, celebrations and emotes, mocap glue |\\n| `20-ball.js` | closed-form ball flight, launches, aiming, prediction, net and ground events |\\n| `21-rules.js` | the referee: touches, faults, scoring, serve rotation, match end, stats |\\n| `22-players.js` | player entity: movement, actions, the timing judge, the human controller |\\n| `23-ai.js` | volleyball AI: assignment, positioning, decisions, error model, chemistry, spectacle mode |\\n| `24-match.js` | the Match: phases, cameras, HUD, crowd, commentary, celebrations, replay, results |\\n| `25-netplay.js` | AI Hub shared-world host and client sync, the card, reporting |\\n| `30-vacation.js` | calendar, slots, weather, schedules, moods, affinity, partners, money, events, saves |\\n| `31-map.js` | the island map scene |\\n| `32-location.js` | the walkable location scene, NPC spots, talk menu, interactables |\\n| `33-shop.js` | shops, wardrobe, gift bag, journal |\\n| `34-story.js` | `E.Story` wiring, cutscene scripts, portraits and voices, prologue, party, endings |\\n| `40-poolhop.js` | Pool Hop |\\n| `41-casino.js` | casino floor, cashier, slots, blackjack, roulette |\\n| `42-photo.js` | photo mode and album |\\n| `50-title.js` | boot steps, title, main menu, How to Play, About & Credits |\\n| `51-attract.js` | the attract director |\\n| `52-exhibition.js` | Beach Match setup and local join |\\n| `53-dev.js` | the dev panel |\\n| `54-results.js` | match results, day end, vacation results, credits roll |\\n| `99-main.js` | building the game, scene registry, hub detection, boot, `game.start` |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Systems\\n\\n### 4.1 Input, devices, glyphs, prompts (`10-input.js`)\\n\\n**4.1.1 Action maps.** Each scene sets an `input` preset. Every preset includes the engine defaults for `up`, `down`,\\n`left` and `right` (WASD, arrows, d-pad, left stick) and for `start` and `pause`.\\n\\n| Preset | Action | Keyboard | Mouse | Pad (standard mapping) |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| MATCH | `play`: bump, set, spike, serve (timed) | Space, J | Left | 0 ✕/A |\\n| | `shot`: tip/cut shot, block, jump serve, free ball | E, K | Right | 2 □/X |\\n| | `dive` | Left Shift, L | — | 1 ○/B |\",\"numLines\":200,\"startLine\":140,\"totalLines\":2180}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01GuJWvM6HGdJ1fbf9rF34fW\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714\",\"uuid\":\"d2e96f6f-15f7-4597-9e5a-089e0bde37d3\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174807__x5c5240/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2092,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2092,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3550,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"27b4c0f6-d164-4b15-853c-19a59c9a05f1\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3700,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"24aa4230-6866-4249-8969-3a1726ee6c3d\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3800,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"9837ce2a-fd99-46af-ac90-2dd80118f1f4\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3950,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"95b3335a-ae7d-4cc2-b118-3494e404404b\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183009__xe162c9/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":290,"oldLines":3,"newStart":290,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh2fc9mw1UUJPivFqtTw\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now the M0 spike page: a custom per-pixel floor, a Backdrop sky, rigs at depths 60–900, and a rig-height measurement.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":6658,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":213419,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":6658},\"output_tokens\":4,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a0704575-f16b-44ea-a24d-907e9c278025\",\"uuid\":\"4dfe5965-6635-4d09-89b5-ee78207b2c1f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:35:33.335Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh2fbutFcSNa1qoiHJBS\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh2fc9mw1UUJPivFqtTw\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01777bAHWfcVcfBzqT3ZeNnb\",\"name\":\"Write\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183009__xe162c9/work/OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183009/dev/spike.html\",\"content\":\"<!doctype html>\\n<html><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\"><title>spike</title>\\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated}</style></head>\\n<body><canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas>\\n<script src=\\\"../engine/my-3d2dge.js\\\"></script>\\n<script src=\\\"../src/00-core.js\\\"></script>\\n<script src=\\\"../src/10-view3d.js\\\"></script>\\n<script>\\n(() => {\\nconst E = My3D2dge, WP = globalThis.WP;\\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: [480, 270] });\\nconst m7 = new E.Mode7({ floor: () => [0, 0, 0], size: [2, 2], sky: new E.Backdrop({ sky: ['#1d1a3a', '#7a3f6e', '#e88a6a', '#f6c48c'], sun: { x: .7, y: .62, r: 18, color: '#ffd6a0' }, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains', color: '#5a3a5e', y: .58, height: .12, parallax: .1 }, { kind: 'sea', color: '#8a5a7a', y: .66 }] }), fog: { color: '#e0a07c', near: 320, far: 1600 } });\\n// own floor: per pixel\\nconst grass = new Uint32Array(256 * 256);\\nfor (let y = 0; y < 256; y++) for (let x = 0; x < 256; x++) { const c = E.tex.grass(x, y, {}); grass[y * 256 + x] = (255 << 24) | (c[2] << 16) | (c[1] << 8) | c[0]; }\\nlet img = null, buf = null;\\nm7.drawFloor = function (g, vp) {\\n  const P = this._P, top = Math.max(vp.y, Math.ceil(P.cy - P.f * P.sp / P.cp)), bot = vp.y + vp.h; if (bot <= top) return;\\n  const w = vp.w, h = bot - top;\\n  if (!buf || buf.width !== w || buf.height !== h) { buf = E.mkCanvas(w, h); img = buf.getContext('2d').createImageData(w, h); }\\n  const out = new Uint32Array(img.data.buffer);\\n  for (let row = 0; row < h; row++) {\\n    const D = this.rowDepth(top + row + .5); if (!D) continue;\\n    const s = (D * P.cp + P.h * P.sp) / P.f, l0 = (vp.x + .5 - P.cx) * s, ux = P.rx * s, uy = P.ry * s, base = row * w;\\n    let wx = P.x + P.fx * D + P.rx * l0, wy = P.y + P.fy * D + P.ry * l0;\\n    const dep = WP.Y0 - wy;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < w; i++, wx += ux, wy += uy) {\\n      const tx = wx & 255, ty = wy & 255; let c = grass[ty * 256 + tx];\\n      const dd = WP.Y0 - wy; if (dd > 70 && dd < 110) c = 0xff3a5a7a;\\n      out[base + i] = c;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  buf.getContext('2d').putImageData(img, 0, 0); g.drawImage(buf, vp.x, top);\\n  const fog = this.o.fog, fc = E.hex(fog.color), n = fog.near, far = fog.far;\\n  for (let by = top; by < bot; by++) { const D = this.rowDepth(by + .5), a = D ? clamp((D - n) / (far - n), 0, 1) : 1; if (a > .01) { g.fillStyle = `rgba(${fc[0]},${fc[1]},${fc[2]},${a.toFixed(3)})`; g.fillRect(vp.x, by, vp.w, 1); } }\\n};\\nconst clamp = E.clamp;\\nconst rigs = [60, 120, 200, 400, 600, 900].map((d, i) => ({ d, rig: new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.3, weapon: 'gun', hat: 'cap', outfit: 'shirt', colors: { cloth: '#b89a62', pants: '#8a7048', hat: '#7a6038' } }), x: 100 + i * 50 }));\\nconst cam = { x: 200, y: WP.Y0, h: 28, angle: -Math.PI / 2, pitch: 6, fov: 60 };\\nconst res = {};\\ngame.debug = { snapshot: () => res };\\ngame.start({ update(dt) { cam.x += dt * 16; for (const r of rigs) r.rig.update(dt, { x: r.x, y: WP.Y0 - r.d, z: 0, facing: Math.PI / 2, point: true }); },\\n  draw(r) {\\n    m7.cam = cam;\\n    for (const q of rigs) m7.rig(q.rig, cam.x - 150 + rigs.indexOf(q) * 60, WP.Y0 - q.d, 0);\\n    m7.shape('barrel', cam.x + 60, WP.Y0 - 80, 0);\\n    m7.shape('tree', cam.x + 120, WP.Y0 - 300, 0);\\n    m7.draw(r);\\n    r.overlay(g => {\\n      // calibrate: draw a rig at view scale 1 to an offscreen canvas and measure\\n      if (!res.done) {\\n        const c = E.mkCanvas(200, 200), cg = E.ctx2d(c);\\n        const presets = { r13: { size: 1.3, weapon: 'gun', hat: 'cap' }, b155: { size: 1.55, build: 'bulky', weapon: 'gun' }, h135: { size: 1.35, hat: 'cap', outfit: 'coat' } };\\n        for (const k in presets) {\\n          const rig = new E.Humanoid(presets[k]); for (const pose of [null, 'kneel', 'crouch']) {\\n            rig.update(1, { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, facing: Math.PI / 2, pose: pose || undefined }); for (let i = 0; i < 60; i++) rig.update(1 / 60, { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, facing: Math.PI / 2, pose: pose || undefined });\\n            cg.clearRect(0, 0, 200, 200); rig.draw(cg, 100, 150, m7.view(1));\\n            const d = cg.getImageData(0, 0, 200, 200).data; let x0 = 999, x1 = -1, y0 = 999, y1 = -1;\\n            for (let y = 0; y < 200; y++) for (let x = 0; x < 200; x++) if (d[(y * 200 + x) * 4 + 3] > 0) { x0 = Math.min(x0, x); x1 = Math.max(x1, x); y0 = Math.min(y0, y); y1 = Math.max(y1, y); }\\n            res[k + ':' + (pose || 'stand')] = { top: 150 - y0, bot: y1 - 150, w: x1 - x0 + 1, l: 100 - x0, rr: x1 - 100 };\\n          }\\n        }\\n        res.done = true;\\n      }\\n    });\\n  } });\\n})();\\n</script></body></html>\\n\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":6658,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":213419,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":6658},\"output_tokens\":4,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a0704575-f16b-44ea-a24d-907e9c278025\",\"uuid\":\"bfee5d07-7c30-4dc2-8189-af9812feb4d3\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:35:52.463Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh2fbutFcSNa1qoiHJBS\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01777bAHWfcVcfBzqT3ZeNnb\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183009__xe162c9/work/OperationWolfpack-OperationWolf-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183009/dev/spike.html\",\"cont