{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GrDnhKPHaYvC42MxfGeBSo","type":"tool_result","content":"688\t### 4.13 Messages, Examine, Journal, notes and hints\n689\t\n690\t- **The log.** The three newest lines at the bottom left, fading after 8 s; the full history is in Journal → Log.\n691\t- **Examine** (R3, X or middle click) describes what is in front in the source's voice, for example:\n692\t  - \"A wall of slick stone. One stone sits proud of the rest.\"\n693\t  - \"The Drain Rat looks badly hurt.\"\n694\t  - \"A Rusty Dagger and a Rock lie here.\"\n695\t- **The Journal** (from the Party and Map screens or the pause menu) has four tabs:\n696\t  - **Quests**: the main thread, the NPCs and Veil.\n697\t  - **Notes**: every inscription and note read, readable again.\n698\t  - **Deeds**: found out of 3.\n699\t  - **Log**.\n700\t- **Hints** (Settings → Hints, on by default) are first-time tips that use the player's own glyphs, for example \"Rats! Press □ to strike with everyone who's ready.\", plus each puzzle's escalation.\n701\t\n702\t### 4.14 Automap\n703\t\n704\t- **What it records.** `E.Fog` per floor, with a sight radius of 4 in the dungeon. A cell counts as seen when it is visible; walls are drawn next to seen floor.\n705\t- **The screen** (§5.3) shows:\n706\t  - walls, and doors in their states;\n707\t  - stairs, plates (once seen pressed or stood on), alcoves, inscriptions (a quill), teleporters (once used), the spinner (once noticed);\n708\t  - NPCs, the party arrow, and monster dots for a Ranger's Tracking.\n709\t- **A minimap** in the top-right is *optional*. The default HUD has only the compass, to keep the 10-foot view clean.\n710\t\n711\t### 4.15 Saves\n712\t\n713\t- **Where.** The engine's `game.saves`: 3 slots plus the autosave.\n714\t  - Save and Load sit in Camp and in the pause menu (when out of combat, `saves.canSave`).\n715\t  - The autosave runs on every floor arrival and after the boss.\n716\t- **The title.** Continue loads `latest()`.\n717\t- **Hub sessions.** The client gives the page in-memory storage, so add no code. Hide Save and Load in a session.\n718\t\n719\t### 4.16 Settings (the engine's, plus a *Game* group)\n720\t\n721\t- **The engine's own:** volume, music, effects, mute, reduce motion, shake and flashes, pixel scaling, screen filter, frame rate, the 3D Display settings (cards or puppets, resolution, shadows, filter) and Controls (rebinding, dead zone, vibration, **Button symbols: PlayStation / Xbox**).\n722\t- **Ours** (`game.settings.define`, group 'Game'):\n723\t\n724\t  | Setting | Options | Default |\n725\t  |---|---|---|\n726\t  | Difficulty | Easy / Normal / Hard | Normal |\n727\t  | Time in menus | Pause / Slow / Real time | Slow |\n728\t  | Step animation | Smooth / Quick / Instant | Smooth |\n729\t  | Head bob | on / off | on |\n730\t  | Hints | on / off | on |\n731\t  | Level up | At once / On rest | At once |\n732\t  | Voices volume | slider | 0.8 |\n733\t\n734\t---\n735\t\n736\t## 5. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller-first\n737\t\n738\t### 5.1 Principles\n739\t\n740\t- **Resolution.** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true`. The HUD is laid out for **320×240 (4:3) up to about 427×240 (16:9)** in game pixels and anchored to `r.W` and `r.H`.\n741\t  - At 1080p one game pixel is about 4.5 screen pixels, so the 5×7 font reads at about 31 px from the sofa.\n742\t  - Body text is the normal 5×7 font; headings use `scale: 2`; nothing interactive uses the tiny 3×5 font.\n743\t- **Few, big things.** At most about 12 focusable things per screen region. Every screen shows ○ Back at the bottom right. Cut density before you shrink anything.\n744\t- **One look: \"lockwork brass.\"**\n745\t  - Panels: `bg ['#1c1813', '#0e0c0a']`, border `#b8924a`, focus `#ffd36a` (double border plus a slow pulse), text `#f0e6d0`.\n746\t  - Stat colours: HP `#e0463c`, spell slots `#4a8aff`, food `#c8a040`.\n747\t  - Rivets: 2×2 dots `#e8c878` in the panel corners.\n748\t  - Title text: `E.font.title` with `colors ['#fff6d8', '#ffd36a', '#c8923a', '#6a4a1a']` and `depthColor '#2a1a08'`.\n749\t- **Keyboard and mouse are native, not stand-ins.** The same screens, with hover moving the focus, click acting, drag and drop in the Party screen, the mouse wheel scrolling lists and the Hand following the cursor (§5.4).\n750\t- **Prompts always follow `input.lastDevice`** (§5.5).\n751\t\n752\t### 5.2 The play HUD (over the full-screen 3D view)\n753\t\n754\t| Element | Where (game pixels) | Content |\n755\t|---|---|---|\n756\t| Compass | top centre, 64×16 | \"W  **N**  E\", with the facing letter at scale 2. It changes instantly on spinners: the only clue. |\n757\t| Floor toast | top left | the floor's name for 3 s on arrival |\n758\t| Party bar | bottom, `H−50` to `H−2` | one card per member in formation order. Row groups are 4 px apart, with tiny labels FRONT, MID and BACK above them. |\n759\t| Card (about 66×46) | — | live portrait 30×30 (`drawPortrait`, wince when hurt, grey when Down, bones when Dead); the name (cut to 7 letters); HP bar and `hp/max`; a 2-px food strip under the portrait; **two hand slots** 15×15 with the item icon, a cooldown wipe (dark, sweeping), a \"ready\" glint and MISS or damage pops; status icons in a row of 6×6 (poison drop, chain, Zz, shield, bowl) |\n760\t| Selected card | — | brass double frame; the L2 and R2 glyph badges under its hand slots |\n761\t| Log | above the bar, left | 3 lines, newest at the bottom, with a shadow |\n762\t| Prompts | above the bar, right | up to 4 `[glyph] Verb`, e.g. `✕ Pull lever · □ Strike · △ Party · Create Map` |\n763\t| Hand | above the bar, centre | held item icon and its name (unless the mouse cursor carries it) |\n764\t| Hit chevrons | screen edges | red chevrons on the left, right or bottom edge for 0.6 s on flank or rear hits; a red vignette on front-row hits |\n765\t| Mouse helpers | top right under the engine corner | small icons for Map, Camp, Party and Journal, mouse only; hidden for the pad |\n766\t| Boss bar | under the compass | THE BOLT-HOLDER, 200×6, with 3 lock pips (turned or locked) |\n767\t| Race HUD | top left | timer `02:13.4`, checkpoint label, crowns, and in a session the standings in seat colours |\n768\t\n769\tKeep clear of `game.cornerArea()`, the engine's top-right menu button.\n770\t\n771\t### 5.3 Screens\n772\t\n773\tEvery screen is drawn over the dimmed 3D view, takes focus navigation (§5.4) and shows its prompts.\n774\t\n775\t- **Party (△, I).**\n776\t  - **Top:** member tabs, one 32-px portrait each (L1 and R1 switch).\n777\t  - **Left:** the paperdoll, a large live rig portrait framed by 20×20 slots: Head, Neck, Body, Arms, Main, Off, Ring, Ring, Feet, Quiver.\n778\t  - **Centre:** the backpack, 4×3 slots of 22×22.\n779\t  - **Right:** details: a 32×32 icon, the name, a type line, stats (damage, speed, Defense, classes) and the description (§7.7 tone).\n780\t  - **Bottom:** `HP 11/11 · Defense 14 · Lv 2 Fighter · XP 140/250 · Food ███░`.\n781\t  - **Actions:** ✕ takes or places (it carries the item into the Hand, or swaps), □ Use, △ Drop at your feet, R2 Sheet. ○ returns a carried item, then closes the screen.\n782\t  - **The Sheet tab** shows the stats and their modifiers, class abilities, resistances and the spellbook or the prayers. Dismiss (NPCs) is here, behind a confirm.\n783\t- **Cast.** Opened by a caster's book or symbol hand.\n784\t  - A centred panel of about 260×150, with level tabs L1, L2, L3 (shoulders switch them).\n785\t  - Rows read \"Spark Dart ×2\", with a description and the target type.\n786\t  - ✕ casts. A `member` target then moves the highlight across the cards (◀ ▶, ✕). A `line`, `front`, `door` or `party` spell fires at once. ○ cancels.\n787\t- **Camp (L3, C).** The view darkens and a small campfire light glows in the cell. Tiles in 2 rows of 5 (§4.9).\n788\t  - **Rest** shows a rest panel: the hours counting, HP ticking up on the cards and ○ Stop.\n789\t  - **Memorize** and **Pray**: known spells on the left (grouped by level, with descriptions) and slots on the right. ✕ on a spell fills the next free slot of its level, ✕ on a slot empties it, △ \"Same as before\".\n790\t  - **Scribe**: scrolls in the party's packs that the mage doesn't know; ✕ learns one.\n791\t  - **Formation**: the 2×3 places; ✕ twice swaps two members.\n792\t  - **Eat**: a confirm, then a summary of who ate what.\n793\t  - **Save** and **Load** open the engine's slot screens (`saves.show`).\n794\t  - **Settings** opens `game.menu('settings')`.\n795\t- **Map (Create, M).**\n796\t  - A parchment-coloured panel with the floor's explored cells at 8 to 10 px per cell, and a legend row at the bottom.\n797\t  - L1 and R1 switch between visited floors; the d-pad or stick pans a map larger than the screen; ○ closes.\n798\t  - Dev *reveal* shows everything.\n799\t- **Journal (J, or the tab from Party or Map).** Quests, Notes, Deeds and Log. Notes open the **Reader**, a parchment page with the note's text at the normal size, paged with the d-pad.\n800\t- **Dialogue.** `E.Dialog` at the bottom: portrait on the left, name in brass and 3 lines a page. ✕ finishes the line, then turns the page; ○ fast-forwards; choices are a vertical list.\n801\t- **Title, creation, About and Credits, game over, ending, floor card and touch notice:** §7.3, §11, §5.7.\n802\t\n803\t### 5.4 Focus navigation and the mouse\n804\t\n805\t- **One focus system** (`61-ui-kit.js`) for every screen.\n806\t  - Each screen registers its widgets as rects with an id, an action and optional explicit neighbours.\n807\t  - The d-pad and the left stick (menus use the engine's `up/down/left/right`, which include the stick) move to the nearest widget in that direction, by geometry; explicit neighbours override.\n808\t  - Holding a direction repeats (`input.repeat`, 0.35 s, then 0.1 s).\n809\t- **The mouse.**\n810\t  - Moving the pointer over a widget focuses it; a left click acts as ✕; a right click on a slot acts as □; the wheel scrolls lists.\n811\t  - Party screen drag and drop: mouse-down carries the item, mouse-up places it.\n812\t- **Mouse in the 3D view.** Each frame, project the interactables in front with `world.project`: the front wall's feature, the items in the front and own cells, doors, the monsters in front and alcoves. Each gets a screen hotspot.\n813\t  - Hovering one outlines it (a soft brass rim drawn with the pen around the thing) and shows a tooltip, e.g. \"Lever — click to pull\".\n814\t  - A left click on a hotspot uses it. With an item in the Hand, a left click on the lower view puts it down and a left click on the upper view throws it, as in the source.\n815\t  - A right click anywhere in the view is **Party Strike**.\n816\t- **Party cards.** A click on a hand slot uses that hand (the source's core gesture); a click on a portrait selects; a right click on a portrait opens that member in the Party screen.\n817\t\n818\t### 5.5 Prompts and glyphs\n819\t\n820\t- **One painter, `glyph(g, x, y, action)`**, draws a badge for the action's binding on the last device:\n821\t\n822\t  | Device | Badge |\n823\t  |---|---|\n824\t  | Pad, PlayStation (default) | ✕ blue, ○ red, □ pink, △ green, drawn as shapes on a dark disc; L1, R1, L2, R2, L3, R3, Options and Create as rounded labels; D-pad and stick icons |\n825\t  | Pad, Xbox (Settings → Controls → Button symbols) | A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow letters; LB, RB, LT, RT, View, Menu |\n826\t  | Keyboard | a keycap with the bound key (`input.codeLabel`) |\n827\t  | Mouse | a mouse icon with the left or right button lit |\n828\t\n829\t  Never print raw codes. Build every prompt string from `input.label(action)` through the painter, so rebinding just works.\n830\t- **When the prompts change.** They switch the moment `lastDevice` changes: a pad button or a stick past the dead zone, a key, or a mouse move of more than 4 px or a click.\n831\t\n832\t### 5.6 Input map (all rebindable except the menu actions)\n833\t\n834\t| Action | Gamepad (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n835\t|---|---|---|---|\n836\t| Step forward / back | Left stick ↑ ↓, D-pad ↑ ↓ | W / S, ↑ / ↓, Numpad 8 / 5 or 2 | — |\n837\t| Strafe left / right | Left stick ← → | A / D, Numpad 4 / 6 | — |\n838\t| Turn left / right | D-pad ← →, right stick ← → (a flick, repeating every 0.35 s while held) | Q / E, ← / →, Numpad 7 / 9 | — |\n839\t| Use / interact / take / place / stow | ✕ (tap) | F | left click on a thing in the view |\n840\t| Put the Hand's item down | ✕ (hold 0.4 s) | H | left click on the lower view |\n841\t| Throw the Hand's item | ○ | G | left click on the upper view |\n842\t| Party Strike | □ | Space | right click in the view |\n843\t| Select member previous / next | L1 / R1 | Tab / Shift+Tab, or 1–6 | click a portrait |\n844\t| Selected member's main / off hand | R2 / L2 | 1–6 main hand (and select); Shift+1–6 off hand | click a hand slot |\n845\t| Party screen | △ | I | portrait right click, HUD icon |\n846\t| Camp | L3 | C | HUD icon |\n847\t| Examine ahead | R3 | X | middle click |\n848\t| Automap | Create (acts on release; ignored when Options was pressed while Create was held) | M | HUD icon |\n849\t| Journal | (from the Party or Map tabs, or the pause menu) | J | HUD icon |\n850\t| Pause menu | Options | Esc, P | the engine's corner button |\n851\t| Menus | D-pad / stick, ✕ confirm, ○ back, L1 / R1 tabs | arrows, Enter, Backspace or Esc | hover, click, wheel |\n852\t\n853\t**Implementation notes.**\n854\t- Define your own play actions (`fwd, back, strafeL, strafeR, turnL, turnR, use, strike, selPrev, selNext, handMain, handOff, party, camp, examine, map, journal, throw, putDown`) in the play scene's `input` map, as the kit did.\n855\t- **Don't use the engine's merged `left/right` in play**: they merge the d-pad and the stick, and here they mean different things.\n856\t  - Read the left stick from `input.padAxes[0]` and `[1]`, with the dead zone and a 0.5 threshold, for move and strafe.\n857\t  - Read the right stick X from `padAxes[2]`, as a flick with re-arm, for turning.\n858\t  - The d-pad codes are `Pad12` to `Pad15`.\n859\t- **Hub rule.** While Create (`Pad8`) is held, ignore Options (`Pad9`), and don't toggle the map on Create's release if Options went down in between.\n860\t- **Idle detection** (attract mode): any action pressed, any `input.held` code, a stick past 0.3, a pointer move over 4 px or a click.\n861\t\n862\t### 5.7 Touch-only devices\n863\t\n864\t- **Detection.** `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` with no `(hover: hover)`, and no keyboard or gamepad input seen yet. On such devices `input.touchEnabled = false`: no touch buttons and no stick.\n865\t- **The title** shows a panel: \"**Controller or keyboard required.** Connect a controller or a keyboard to play.\" The engine's top-right menu button stays and opens Settings.\n866\t- **The attract mode runs** after the same 10 s idle. A touch exits it to the title, which shows the notice again.\n867\t- **The notice hides** the moment a key or a pad button arrives, and play works normally from then on.\n868\t\n869\t---\n870\t\n871\t## 6. Presentation: art, animation and audio\n872\t\n873\t### 6.1 Art direction\n874\t\n875\t- **The base is the engine's native 3D look,** the one the spike showed: code-drawn textures, `world.res = 'pixels'` (chunky low-res pixels), toon light, outlines on, characters as **cards** (`world.look = 'card'`: the rigs drawn as pixel art from the camera's own angle) and fog for the source's distance falloff.\n876\t- **Lighting.** `torchShadows: 2`, `torchLights: 6`, the party's lantern as a `world.light` at the eyes, and `glowLights: 4` for spells.\n877\t- **New art** wherever the source's feel needs it: wall features, doors, floor items, the creatures in §6.3, the boss, the brass UI, item icons and the stages for the title and the cutscenes."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40","uuid":"04513f44-0edd-465a-a7d6-d60ba831f817","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:46:58.547Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 4.13 Messages, Examine, Journal, notes and hints\n\n- **The log.** The three newest lines at the bottom left, fading after 8 s; the full history is in Journal → Log.\n- **Examine** (R3, X or middle click) describes what is in front in the source's voice, for example:\n  - \"A wall of slick stone. One stone sits proud of the rest.\"\n  - \"The Drain Rat looks badly hurt.\"\n  - \"A Rusty Dagger and a Rock lie here.\"\n- **The Journal** (from the Party and Map screens or the pause menu) has four tabs:\n  - **Quests**: the main thread, the NPCs and Veil.\n  - **Notes**: every inscription and note read, readable again.\n  - **Deeds**: found out of 3.\n  - **Log**.\n- **Hints** (Settings → Hints, on by default) are first-time tips that use the player's own glyphs, for example \"Rats! Press □ to strike with everyone who's ready.\", plus each puzzle's escalation.\n\n### 4.14 Automap\n\n- **What it records.** `E.Fog` per floor, with a sight radius of 4 in the dungeon. A cell counts as seen when it is visible; walls are drawn next to seen floor.\n- **The screen** (§5.3) shows:\n  - walls, and doors in their states;\n  - stairs, plates (once seen pressed or stood on), alcoves, inscriptions (a quill), teleporters (once used), the spinner (once noticed);\n  - NPCs, the party arrow, and monster dots for a Ranger's Tracking.\n- **A minimap** in the top-right is *optional*. The default HUD has only the compass, to keep the 10-foot view clean.\n\n### 4.15 Saves\n\n- **Where.** The engine's `game.saves`: 3 slots plus the autosave.\n  - Save and Load sit in Camp and in the pause menu (when out of combat, `saves.canSave`).\n  - The autosave runs on every floor arrival and after the boss.\n- **The title.** Continue loads `latest()`.\n- **Hub sessions.** The client gives the page in-memory storage, so add no code. Hide Save and Load in a session.\n\n### 4.16 Settings (the engine's, plus a *Game* group)\n\n- **The engine's own:** volume, music, effects, mute, reduce motion, shake and flashes, pixel scaling, screen filter, frame rate, the 3D Display settings (cards or puppets, resolution, shadows, filter) and Controls (rebinding, dead zone, vibration, **Button symbols: PlayStation / Xbox**).\n- **Ours** (`game.settings.define`, group 'Game'):\n\n  | Setting | Options | Default |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | Difficulty | Easy / Normal / Hard | Normal |\n  | Time in menus | Pause / Slow / Real time | Slow |\n  | Step animation | Smooth / Quick / Instant | Smooth |\n  | Head bob | on / off | on |\n  | Hints | on / off | on |\n  | Level up | At once / On rest | At once |\n  | Voices volume | slider | 0.8 |\n\n---\n\n## 5. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller-first\n\n### 5.1 Principles\n\n- **Resolution.** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true`. The HUD is laid out for **320×240 (4:3) up to about 427×240 (16:9)** in game pixels and anchored to `r.W` and `r.H`.\n  - At 1080p one game pixel is about 4.5 screen pixels, so the 5×7 font reads at about 31 px from the sofa.\n  - Body text is the normal 5×7 font; headings use `scale: 2`; nothing interactive uses the tiny 3×5 font.\n- **Few, big things.** At most about 12 focusable things per screen region. Every screen shows ○ Back at the bottom right. Cut density before you shrink anything.\n- **One look: \"lockwork brass.\"**\n  - Panels: `bg ['#1c1813', '#0e0c0a']`, border `#b8924a`, focus `#ffd36a` (double border plus a slow pulse), text `#f0e6d0`.\n  - Stat colours: HP `#e0463c`, spell slots `#4a8aff`, food `#c8a040`.\n  - Rivets: 2×2 dots `#e8c878` in the panel corners.\n  - Title text: `E.font.title` with `colors ['#fff6d8', '#ffd36a', '#c8923a', '#6a4a1a']` and `depthColor '#2a1a08'`.\n- **Keyboard and mouse are native, not stand-ins.** The same screens, with hover moving the focus, click acting, drag and drop in the Party screen, the mouse wheel scrolling lists and the Hand following the cursor (§5.4).\n- **Prompts always follow `input.lastDevice`** (§5.5).\n\n### 5.2 The play HUD (over the full-screen 3D view)\n\n| Element | Where (game pixels) | Content |\n|---|---|---|\n| Compass | top centre, 64×16 | \"W  **N**  E\", with the facing letter at scale 2. It changes instantly on spinners: the only clue. |\n| Floor toast | top left | the floor's name for 3 s on arrival |\n| Party bar | bottom, `H−50` to `H−2` | one card per member in formation order. Row groups are 4 px apart, with tiny labels FRONT, MID and BACK above them. |\n| Card (about 66×46) | — | live portrait 30×30 (`drawPortrait`, wince when hurt, grey when Down, bones when Dead); the name (cut to 7 letters); HP bar and `hp/max`; a 2-px food strip under the portrait; **two hand slots** 15×15 with the item icon, a cooldown wipe (dark, sweeping), a \"ready\" glint and MISS or damage pops; status icons in a row of 6×6 (poison drop, chain, Zz, shield, bowl) |\n| Selected card | — | brass double frame; the L2 and R2 glyph badges under its hand slots |\n| Log | above the bar, left | 3 lines, newest at the bottom, with a shadow |\n| Prompts | above the bar, right | up to 4 `[glyph] Verb`, e.g. `✕ Pull lever · □ Strike · △ Party · Create Map` |\n| Hand | above the bar, centre | held item icon and its name (unless the mouse cursor carries it) |\n| Hit chevrons | screen edges | red chevrons on the left, right or bottom edge for 0.6 s on flank or rear hits; a red vignette on front-row hits |\n| Mouse helpers | top right under the engine corner | small icons for Map, Camp, Party and Journal, mouse only; hidden for the pad |\n| Boss bar | under the compass | THE BOLT-HOLDER, 200×6, with 3 lock pips (turned or locked) |\n| Race HUD | top left | timer `02:13.4`, checkpoint label, crowns, and in a session the standings in seat colours |\n\nKeep clear of `game.cornerArea()`, the engine's top-right menu button.\n\n### 5.3 Screens\n\nEvery screen is drawn over the dimmed 3D view, takes focus navigation (§5.4) and shows its prompts.\n\n- **Party (△, I).**\n  - **Top:** member tabs, one 32-px portrait each (L1 and R1 switch).\n  - **Left:** the paperdoll, a large live rig portrait framed by 20×20 slots: Head, Neck, Body, Arms, Main, Off, Ring, Ring, Feet, Quiver.\n  - **Centre:** the backpack, 4×3 slots of 22×22.\n  - **Right:** details: a 32×32 icon, the name, a type line, stats (damage, speed, Defense, classes) and the description (§7.7 tone).\n  - **Bottom:** `HP 11/11 · Defense 14 · Lv 2 Fighter · XP 140/250 · Food ███░`.\n  - **Actions:** ✕ takes or places (it carries the item into the Hand, or swaps), □ Use, △ Drop at your feet, R2 Sheet. ○ returns a carried item, then closes the screen.\n  - **The Sheet tab** shows the stats and their modifiers, class abilities, resistances and the spellbook or the prayers. Dismiss (NPCs) is here, behind a confirm.\n- **Cast.** Opened by a caster's book or symbol hand.\n  - A centred panel of about 260×150, with level tabs L1, L2, L3 (shoulders switch them).\n  - Rows read \"Spark Dart ×2\", with a description and the target type.\n  - ✕ casts. A `member` target then moves the highlight across the cards (◀ ▶, ✕). A `line`, `front`, `door` or `party` spell fires at once. ○ cancels.\n- **Camp (L3, C).** The view darkens and a small campfire light glows in the cell. Tiles in 2 rows of 5 (§4.9).\n  - **Rest** shows a rest panel: the hours counting, HP ticking up on the cards and ○ Stop.\n  - **Memorize** and **Pray**: known spells on the left (grouped by level, with descriptions) and slots on the right. ✕ on a spell fills the next free slot of its level, ✕ on a slot empties it, △ \"Same as before\".\n  - **Scribe**: scrolls in the party's packs that the mage doesn't know; ✕ learns one.\n  - **Formation**: the 2×3 places; ✕ twice swaps two members.\n  - **Eat**: a confirm, then a summary of who ate what.\n  - **Save** and **Load** open the engine's slot screens (`saves.show`).\n  - **Settings** opens `game.menu('settings')`.\n- **Map (Create, M).**\n  - A parchment-coloured panel with the floor's explored cells at 8 to 10 px per cell, and a legend row at the bottom.\n  - L1 and R1 switch between visited floors; the d-pad or stick pans a map larger than the screen; ○ closes.\n  - Dev *reveal* shows everything.\n- **Journal (J, or the tab from Party or Map).** Quests, Notes, Deeds and Log. Notes open the **Reader**, a parchment page with the note's text at the normal size, paged with the d-pad.\n- **Dialogue.** `E.Dialog` at the bottom: portrait on the left, name in brass and 3 lines a page. ✕ finishes the line, then turns the page; ○ fast-forwards; choices are a vertical list.\n- **Title, creation, About and Credits, game over, ending, floor card and touch notice:** §7.3, §11, §5.7.\n\n### 5.4 Focus navigation and the mouse\n\n- **One focus system** (`61-ui-kit.js`) for every screen.\n  - Each screen registers its widgets as rects with an id, an action and optional explicit neighbours.\n  - The d-pad and the left stick (menus use the engine's `up/down/left/right`, which include the stick) move to the nearest widget in that direction, by geometry; explicit neighbours override.\n  - Holding a direction repeats (`input.repeat`, 0.35 s, then 0.1 s).\n- **The mouse.**\n  - Moving the pointer over a widget focuses it; a left click acts as ✕; a right click on a slot acts as □; the wheel scrolls lists.\n  - Party screen drag and drop: mouse-down carries the item, mouse-up places it.\n- **Mouse in the 3D view.** Each frame, project the interactables in front with `world.project`: the front wall's feature, the items in the front and own cells, doors, the monsters in front and alcoves. Each gets a screen hotspot.\n  - Hovering one outlines it (a soft brass rim drawn with the pen around the thing) and shows a tooltip, e.g. \"Lever — click to pull\".\n  - A left click on a hotspot uses it. With an item in the Hand, a left click on the lower view puts it down and a left click on the upper view throws it, as in the source.\n  - A right click anywhere in the view is **Party Strike**.\n- **Party cards.** A click on a hand slot uses that hand (the source's core gesture); a click on a portrait selects; a right click on a portrait opens that member in the Party screen.\n\n### 5.5 Prompts and glyphs\n\n- **One painter, `glyph(g, x, y, action)`**, draws a badge for the action's binding on the last device:\n\n  | Device | Badge |\n  |---|---|\n  | Pad, PlayStation (default) | ✕ blue, ○ red, □ pink, △ green, drawn as shapes on a dark disc; L1, R1, L2, R2, L3, R3, Options and Create as rounded labels; D-pad and stick icons |\n  | Pad, Xbox (Settings → Controls → Button symbols) | A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow letters; LB, RB, LT, RT, View, Menu |\n  | Keyboard | a keycap with the bound key (`input.codeLabel`) |\n  | Mouse | a mouse icon with the left or right button lit |\n\n  Never print raw codes. Build every prompt string from `input.label(action)` through the painter, so rebinding just works.\n- **When the prompts change.** They switch the moment `lastDevice` changes: a pad button or a stick past the dead zone, a key, or a mouse move of more than 4 px or a click.\n\n### 5.6 Input map (all rebindable except the menu actions)\n\n| Action | Gamepad (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Step forward / back | Left stick ↑ ↓, D-pad ↑ ↓ | W / S, ↑ / ↓, Numpad 8 / 5 or 2 | — |\n| Strafe left / right | Left stick ← → | A / D, Numpad 4 / 6 | — |\n| Turn left / right | D-pad ← →, right stick ← → (a flick, repeating every 0.35 s while held) | Q / E, ← / →, Numpad 7 / 9 | — |\n| Use / interact / take / place / stow | ✕ (tap) | F | left click on a thing in the view |\n| Put the Hand's item down | ✕ (hold 0.4 s) | H | left click on the lower view |\n| Throw the Hand's item | ○ | G | left click on the upper view |\n| Party Strike | □ | Space | right click in the view |\n| Select member previous / next | L1 / R1 | Tab / Shift+Tab, or 1–6 | click a portrait |\n| Selected member's main / off hand | R2 / L2 | 1–6 main hand (and select); Shift+1–6 off hand | click a hand slot |\n| Party screen | △ | I | portrait right click, HUD icon |\n| Camp | L3 | C | HUD icon |\n| Examine ahead | R3 | X | middle click |\n| Automap | Create (acts on release; ignored when Options was pressed while Create was held) | M | HUD icon |\n| Journal | (from the Party or Map tabs, or the pause menu) | J | HUD icon |\n| Pause menu | Options | Esc, P | the engine's corner button |\n| Menus | D-pad / stick, ✕ confirm, ○ back, L1 / R1 tabs | arrows, Enter, Backspace or Esc | hover, click, wheel |\n\n**Implementation notes.**\n- Define your own play actions (`fwd, back, strafeL, strafeR, turnL, turnR, use, strike, selPrev, selNext, handMain, handOff, party, camp, examine, map, journal, throw, putDown`) in the play scene's `input` map, as the kit did.\n- **Don't use the engine's merged `left/right` in play**: they merge the d-pad and the stick, and here they mean different things.\n  - Read the left stick from `input.padAxes[0]` and `[1]`, with the dead zone and a 0.5 threshold, for move and strafe.\n  - Read the right stick X from `padAxes[2]`, as a flick with re-arm, for turning.\n  - The d-pad codes are `Pad12` to `Pad15`.\n- **Hub rule.** While Create (`Pad8`) is held, ignore Options (`Pad9`), and don't toggle the map on Create's release if Options went down in between.\n- **Idle detection** (attract mode): any action pressed, any `input.held` code, a stick past 0.3, a pointer move over 4 px or a click.\n\n### 5.7 Touch-only devices\n\n- **Detection.** `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` with no `(hover: hover)`, and no keyboard or gamepad input seen yet. On such devices `input.touchEnabled = false`: no touch buttons and no stick.\n- **The title** shows a panel: \"**Controller or keyboard required.** Connect a controller or a keyboard to play.\" The engine's top-right menu button stays and opens Settings.\n- **The attract mode runs** after the same 10 s idle. A touch exits it to the title, which shows the notice again.\n- **The notice hides** the moment a key or a pad button arrives, and play works normally from then on.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Presentation: art, animation and audio\n\n### 6.1 Art direction\n\n- **The base is the engine's native 3D look,** the one the spike showed: code-drawn textures, `world.res = 'pixels'` (chunky low-res pixels), toon light, outlines on, characters as **cards** (`world.look = 'card'`: the rigs drawn as pixel art from the camera's own angle) and fog for the source's distance falloff.\n- **Lighting.** `torchShadows: 2`, `torchLights: 6`, the party's lantern as a `world.light` at the eyes, and `glowLights: 4` for spells.\n- **New art** wherever the source's feel needs it: wall features, doors, floor items, the creatures in §6.3, the boss, the brass UI, item icons and the stages for the title and the cutscenes.","numLines":190,"startLine":688,"totalLines":2131}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GrDnhKPHaYvC42MxfGeBSo","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
