{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3YQe96T9E1zRsbRf6b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013kjf32HXyfE4dDQLBwjMQa","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work/PLAN.md","offset":877,"limit":90},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7160,"cache_read_input_tokens":537485,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7160},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40","uuid":"0dcf3917-b94f-4d7f-961a-2d9b9004ab36","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:47:07.611Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3YQKJMxjKwE5yAwZpC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013kjf32HXyfE4dDQLBwjMQa":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work/PLAN.md","offset":877,"limit":90}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013kjf32HXyfE4dDQLBwjMQa","type":"tool_result","content":"877\t- **New art** wherever the source's feel needs it: wall features, doors, floor items, the creatures in §6.3, the boss, the brass UI, item icons and the stages for the title and the cutscenes.\n878\t- **Props.** For generic set dressing (bones, barrels, crates, chains, cobwebs, banners, candles, tables), search the store first with `node tools/asset-find.mjs \"bones\"`, using `kaykit-dungeon-remastered`, `kenney-mini-dungeon` and `kenney-graveyard`. Cut a set with `tools/asset-set.mjs`, load it with `E.addAssets`, and place props with `world.shape(id, …)` or `{ shape }` in the legend.\n879\t\n880\t| Floor | Ground (`level.ground`, `colors`) | Walls (`side`, `color`) | Fog | Ambient `[sky, ground, power]` | Signature dressing |\n881\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n882\t| 1 The Hasp Drains | flagstone `#3e4a44 / #2a332f / #55615a`; a floor colour function paints dark-green **water channels** (6 units wide) down the Rat Channel and Cistern cells | brick `#4a5048` | `#06080a`, 24 → 150 | `#4a5a5a, #1a201e, 2.6` | floor drains (grates), dripping pipes (pen tubes), slime streaks, rusty chains, rat bones, sluice wheels |\n883\t| 2 The Tumbler Halls | tiles `#5a4a3a / #3e3228 / #7a6450` | block `#6a5a48` | `#0a0806`, 40 → 220 | `#7a6048, #2a2018, 3.0` | turning **wall gears** (pen rings of teeth, slowly rotating), anvils, workbenches, cogs on the floor, forge glow (orange lights) in the Workshop |\n884\t| 3 The Gloam Deeps | plain `#2a2434 / #1a1622 / #3a3248` | block `#2e2838` | `#040306`, 20 → 130 | `#3a3a5a, #141220, 2.2` | carved **eye reliefs** on walls (pen), shut-eye banners, bone piles, pale blue candles in the Chapel (lights) |\n885\t| 4 The Eye's Vault | tiles `#3a3e46`; the arena floor colour function adds faint cyan rune lines | block `#30343c` | `#020204`, 30 → 200 | `#2a3040, #0c0e14, 2.0` | the boss's amber light, cyan lightning flashes, the 3 Great Locks' rune lights going out as they turn |\n886\t\n887\t- **Item icons.** Make about 60 of them as `E.sprite` strings, designed at 12×12 and drawn at ×1 on the cards and ×2 in the Party screen. Shade them with `E.tones`.\n888\t- **Item models.** Each floor item also gets a tiny **3D model drawn with the pen**, lying flat at its quadrant spot:\n889\t  - blade (sword, dagger): a thin box with a cross-guard;\n890\t  - axe or mace: a head on a haft;\n891\t  - crossbow; bolts or arrows: thin tubes;\n892\t  - potion: a ball and a neck, in its colour;\n893\t  - scroll: a tube; book: a box;\n894\t  - key: a ring plus a shaft with teeth, in the key's colour;\n895\t  - rock: a grey lump of balls; ration: a wrapped box;\n896\t  - gear: a ring of boxes; ward: a toothed disc.\n897\t\n898\t### 6.2 The 3D presenter (`40–44`)\n899\t\n900\t- **Building a floor.**\n901\t  - Map each cell to 2×2 level tiles (`#` → `##`, open → `..`). A torch wall feature turns the tile on its open side into `t`, the kit's NICHE trick.\n902\t  - Make `new E.World3D(game, { level, look: 'card', res: 'pixels', torchLights: 6, torchShadows: 2, torchPower: 18, ambient, fog, sky: fogColour, camera: { mode: 'fixed' }, overlay: { fov: 60 }, onDraw })`.\n903\t  - Create all of the floor's lights at build time (lantern, candles, forge glows, the boss), as the engine requires.\n904\t  - Build every floor's world at boot and `prepare()` it, so a floor change never compiles a shader mid-game. On a floor change, swap the active world.\n905\t- **Each frame,** from the sim state:\n906\t  - **Camera:** `world.camera.fixed = { x, y, z: EYE + bob, yaw, pitch: −0.04, fov: 74 }`, from the party's tween (the kit's `place()`). A bump adds the lurch, a hit adds `game.shake`, a pit fall drops z by 40 and fades.\n907\t  - **Doors and gates:** `world.thing('door', …, { w: 32, h: 46, swing })`; set `t.open` toward the sim's state and call `world.setSolid` when it opens.\n908\t  - **Secret walls** (and **illusory walls**): a movable wall block that is **indistinguishable from the level's walls**. Try `world.box({ fixed: true, side: <the floor's side style>, color })` first; if it doesn't match, add a `wallBlock` helper to the 3D engine that reuses the level's wall material (risk 3, §13). A secret block sinks into the floor when opened; an illusory one never moves (the party's step through it is masked by the dissolve).\n909\t  - **Wall features:** custom `E.World3D.THINGS`, drawn with the pen on the wall face (local +y out of the wall, as the kit's `wallLever`).\n910\t\n911\t    | THING | How to draw it |\n912\t    |---|---|\n913\t    | `wallLever` | the kit's |\n914\t    | `wallButton` | a square stone and a brass boss that presses in |\n915\t    | `catch` | a slightly proud stone with a crack, or a brass rivet plate; glints under Seeing |\n916\t    | `alcove` | a dark recessed box that draws its items inside |\n917\t    | `keyhole` | per key shape: iron round, warded cross, gear toothed, bone skull, ward discs |\n918\t    | `plaque` | a stone tablet with dark glyph dashes |\n919\t    | `grate`, `pipe`, `chain`, `gearWall` (rotating), `eyeRelief` | decor |\n920\t    | `candle` | a holder, a wax stick and a flame glow when lit, paired with its light |\n921\t    | `greatLock` | a big wheel with rune glow, spun over 2 s |\n922\t    | `undergate` | a great door with 3 keyholes and 7 bolt bars that slide when a ward goes in |\n923\t    | `cage` | bars |\n924\t    | `shrine` | a ring of tiny rat statues |\n925\t    | `clockFace` | a dial with 4 gear sockets and hands that move once the clock is whole |\n926\t    | `altarSlab` | a floor slab |\n927\t    | `stairs` | the kit's `stair` (down), plus `stairUp` |\n928\t    | `pitEdge` | a dark hole with a lip; a bridge slab when bridged |\n929\t    | `plate` | the kit's |\n930\t    | `teleporterField` | a soft swirl glow, only when not silent |\n931\t\n932\t  - **Floor items:** pen models at the quadrant spots of the visible cells (`onDraw`).\n933\t  - **Monsters:** cards (`world.mob` with `rig`, `blob` or `orb`) are steered toward their slot's position with `vx`/`vy` as the kit does (`fly: true` for fliers). Their `anim` comes from the sim: attack phase, hurt flash, `die` pose, sink. Pen-drawn creatures are drawn in `onDraw` from their sim state and a local animation clock (§6.3).\n934\t  - **Projectiles and FX:** `world.glow` for bolts and orbs, pen bars for lightning, `game.particles` for sparks, embers, smoke and damage `text`, and `world.arc` for floor telegraphs (Bolt Rain).\n935\t  - **First-person overlay:** with `world.overlay.pen`, draw the striking member's weapon swinging across its side of the view: left for places 1, 3 and 5, right for 2, 4 and 6. The crossbow rises and kicks; a caster's hand glows in the spell's colour.\n936\t  - **Hover outlines and name tags:** project with `world.project`, then draw them in the HUD.\n937\t- **NullView** implements the same interface (`enter(floor)`, `frame(r)`, `event(e)`, `pick(sx, sy)`) as no-ops for Node.\n938\t\n939\t### 6.3 Creature recipes\n940\t\n941\tThe sizes follow the engine's guidance (heroes `size` 1.2 to 1.4, bosses larger). Every rig gets a real palette.\n942\t\n943\t| Creature | Build | Recipe | Animation notes |\n944\t|---|---|---|---|\n945\t| Drain Rat | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 3.6, ears: 'cat', tail: true, feet: true, mouth: 'fangs', colors: { base: '#6a5a50', dk: '#3e342e', lt: '#9a8a7a', eye: '#ff6a4a' } }` | fast squash scurry; the wind-up is a rear-back squash |\n946\t| Bloat Leech | pen | 5 balls (r 4 → 2.5) along a sine curve on the floor, `#b89a9a` with `#7a5a5a` rings; a mouth ring of 6 small balls; a wet glint | the body undulates; it lunges out 6 units on the strike |\n947\t| Latchkin | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: .85, build: 'chibi', hunch: .5, hood: true, outfit: 'tunic', bladeLen: 5, eyeGlow: '#ffd24a', colors: { skin: '#7a8a5a', hair: '#4a3a2a', cloth: '#6a4a32', pants: '#3a2e22', metal: '#9a9aa8' } }`, plus a pen ring of keys at the belt | the `thrust` move; it stays in a crouch-run while fleeing |\n948\t| Drain Ooze | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 8, face: 'front', mouth: true, colors: { base: '#5a8a3a', dk: '#2e5a22', lt: '#9ad06a', spec: '#e8ffd0' } }` | a slow wobble; it slams by squashing down; it splashes green particles |\n949\t| Rat Knot | pen | 6 rat-body balls in a ring with ear cones, tails as tubes knotted at the middle | the ring wobbles and turns; two bites a strike |\n950\t| Snick, the Latch-Boss | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.0, build: 'bulky', hunch: .3, hat: { style: 'crown', color: '#c8a040' }, armor: true, outfit: 'coat', bladeLen: 9, eyeGlow: '#ffd24a', colors: { skin: '#7a8a5a', cloth: '#5a3a2a', plate: '#a08040' } }`, plus a pen cape of hanging keys | the `overhead` move; it rattles its keys at 50% when it calls for help |\n951\t| Tinker Skeleton | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.2, build: 'skeleton', outfit: 'coat', bladeLen: 7, colors: { bone: '#d8cfb4', cloth: '#5a4030', metal: '#8a8a90' } }`, plus a pen hammer head on the blade | the `overhead` and `slash` moves; it collapses into bones on death |\n952\t| Rustling | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 4.2, horns: true, feet: true, mouth: true, colors: { base: '#b8642a', dk: '#7a3a18', lt: '#e8a060' } }` | the horns twitch; it throws rust-flake particles when it hits |\n953\t| Brass Spider | pen | abdomen ball r 7 and cephalothorax r 4.5 in `#b8923a`; 8 legs of 2 tubes each with procedural tetrapod gait (sine phase lifts); 4 red eye glows | legs step; it lunges on the strike; it falls apart into parts on death |\n954\t| Clockwork Sentinel | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.6, build: 'bulky', armor: true, hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#8a6a3a' }, bladeLen: 14, eyeGlow: '#ff8a3a', colors: { cloth: '#6a4a2a', plate: '#b08a4a', metal: '#c8a868', skin: '#5a4a3a' } }`, plus a pen wind-up key turning on its back | the `twohand` move with a 0.8 s wind-up; the key spins faster during it |\n955\t| Lidless Hound | pen | a quadruped (adapt the 3D horror kit's dogs, `src/starter3d/40-horror.js`): pale `#c8b8b0`, smooth eyeless head, long jaw | run, leap and bite |\n956\t| Gloam Seer | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', outfit: 'robe', hood: true, weapon: 'staff', eyeGlow: '#8ae0ff', colors: { cloth: '#d8d0e8', hair: '#3a2a4a', skin: '#b8b0c8', trim: '#6a4a9a' } }`, plus an eye-sigil glow over the staff | the `cast` pose while charging a Locking Bolt (cyan glow growing) |\n957\t| Gloam Warden | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.35, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#2a2434' }, weapon: 'staff', eyeGlow: '#e8e8ff', colors: { cloth: '#2a2434', plate: '#4a4458', metal: '#9a98a8', skin: '#b8b0c8' } }`, plus a pen halberd blade on the staff | the `thrust` move (reaches two cells) |\n958\t| Gazer | card orb plus pen | an orb `{ color: '#e8a040', r: 4 }`; pen iris (a flattened ball `#3a8a6a`), pupil, two lid slabs, 3 fin cones | blinks; the pupil tracks the party; it glows before Spark Gaze |\n959\t| Lockjaw Golem | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.9, build: 'bulky', armor: true, weapon: null, eyeGlow: '#7ad8ff', colors: { cloth: '#3a3e46', plate: '#5a606a', skin: '#4a4e56' } }`, plus a pen **padlock head** (box body and shackle tube) instead of a hat | the `haymaker` move; heavy footstep shakes |\n960\t| **The Bolt-Holder** | pen | an eye ball r 14 (sclera `#e8e0c8` with red vein bars); a flattened amber iris r 7 (`#e8a030`) facing the party; a black pupil r 3.5 that dilates; upper and lower lid slabs that blink and narrow for the Gaze; **7 radial iron bolts** (bars 22 long and 2.5 thick, with 5×5×3 heads) that slide out 2 per Great Lock (the 7th, the keystone, never moves); cyan lightning arcs (jagged pen bars) between neighbouring bolt heads; a ±3 bob; an amber `world.light`; red tint and crack lines in phase 3 | it must not read as a beholder: no eyestalks, no mouth, no tentacles. It reads as a caged iron lantern-eye. |\n961\t| Ghosts (race) | card, `E.Humanoid` | a hooded cloak in the player's seat colour, `fade 0.45`, a lantern glow in the seat colour, and the hub name as a HUD tag | they glide between the cells they report |\n962\t\n963\t**People** (portraits and cutscenes):\n964\t- the party (§7.9);\n965\t- Keywarden Imelda Strake: heroic, band crown, coat, navy and silver;\n966\t- Magister Abel Lintel: robe, pointed hat, long white hair;"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40","uuid":"af33d787-4895-4c39-bafa-def792de0f81","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:47:07.619Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work/PLAN.md","content":"- **New art** wherever the source's feel needs it: wall features, doors, floor items, the creatures in §6.3, the boss, the brass UI, item icons and the stages for the title and the cutscenes.\n- **Props.** For generic set dressing (bones, barrels, crates, chains, cobwebs, banners, candles, tables), search the store first with `node tools/asset-find.mjs \"bones\"`, using `kaykit-dungeon-remastered`, `kenney-mini-dungeon` and `kenney-graveyard`. Cut a set with `tools/asset-set.mjs`, load it with `E.addAssets`, and place props with `world.shape(id, …)` or `{ shape }` in the legend.\n\n| Floor | Ground (`level.ground`, `colors`) | Walls (`side`, `color`) | Fog | Ambient `[sky, ground, power]` | Signature dressing |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 The Hasp Drains | flagstone `#3e4a44 / #2a332f / #55615a`; a floor colour function paints dark-green **water channels** (6 units wide) down the Rat Channel and Cistern cells | brick `#4a5048` | `#06080a`, 24 → 150 | `#4a5a5a, #1a201e, 2.6` | floor drains (grates), dripping pipes (pen tubes), slime streaks, rusty chains, rat bones, sluice wheels |\n| 2 The Tumbler Halls | tiles `#5a4a3a / #3e3228 / #7a6450` | block `#6a5a48` | `#0a0806`, 40 → 220 | `#7a6048, #2a2018, 3.0` | turning **wall gears** (pen rings of teeth, slowly rotating), anvils, workbenches, cogs on the floor, forge glow (orange lights) in the Workshop |\n| 3 The Gloam Deeps | plain `#2a2434 / #1a1622 / #3a3248` | block `#2e2838` | `#040306`, 20 → 130 | `#3a3a5a, #141220, 2.2` | carved **eye reliefs** on walls (pen), shut-eye banners, bone piles, pale blue candles in the Chapel (lights) |\n| 4 The Eye's Vault | tiles `#3a3e46`; the arena floor colour function adds faint cyan rune lines | block `#30343c` | `#020204`, 30 → 200 | `#2a3040, #0c0e14, 2.0` | the boss's amber light, cyan lightning flashes, the 3 Great Locks' rune lights going out as they turn |\n\n- **Item icons.** Make about 60 of them as `E.sprite` strings, designed at 12×12 and drawn at ×1 on the cards and ×2 in the Party screen. Shade them with `E.tones`.\n- **Item models.** Each floor item also gets a tiny **3D model drawn with the pen**, lying flat at its quadrant spot:\n  - blade (sword, dagger): a thin box with a cross-guard;\n  - axe or mace: a head on a haft;\n  - crossbow; bolts or arrows: thin tubes;\n  - potion: a ball and a neck, in its colour;\n  - scroll: a tube; book: a box;\n  - key: a ring plus a shaft with teeth, in the key's colour;\n  - rock: a grey lump of balls; ration: a wrapped box;\n  - gear: a ring of boxes; ward: a toothed disc.\n\n### 6.2 The 3D presenter (`40–44`)\n\n- **Building a floor.**\n  - Map each cell to 2×2 level tiles (`#` → `##`, open → `..`). A torch wall feature turns the tile on its open side into `t`, the kit's NICHE trick.\n  - Make `new E.World3D(game, { level, look: 'card', res: 'pixels', torchLights: 6, torchShadows: 2, torchPower: 18, ambient, fog, sky: fogColour, camera: { mode: 'fixed' }, overlay: { fov: 60 }, onDraw })`.\n  - Create all of the floor's lights at build time (lantern, candles, forge glows, the boss), as the engine requires.\n  - Build every floor's world at boot and `prepare()` it, so a floor change never compiles a shader mid-game. On a floor change, swap the active world.\n- **Each frame,** from the sim state:\n  - **Camera:** `world.camera.fixed = { x, y, z: EYE + bob, yaw, pitch: −0.04, fov: 74 }`, from the party's tween (the kit's `place()`). A bump adds the lurch, a hit adds `game.shake`, a pit fall drops z by 40 and fades.\n  - **Doors and gates:** `world.thing('door', …, { w: 32, h: 46, swing })`; set `t.open` toward the sim's state and call `world.setSolid` when it opens.\n  - **Secret walls** (and **illusory walls**): a movable wall block that is **indistinguishable from the level's walls**. Try `world.box({ fixed: true, side: <the floor's side style>, color })` first; if it doesn't match, add a `wallBlock` helper to the 3D engine that reuses the level's wall material (risk 3, §13). A secret block sinks into the floor when opened; an illusory one never moves (the party's step through it is masked by the dissolve).\n  - **Wall features:** custom `E.World3D.THINGS`, drawn with the pen on the wall face (local +y out of the wall, as the kit's `wallLever`).\n\n    | THING | How to draw it |\n    |---|---|\n    | `wallLever` | the kit's |\n    | `wallButton` | a square stone and a brass boss that presses in |\n    | `catch` | a slightly proud stone with a crack, or a brass rivet plate; glints under Seeing |\n    | `alcove` | a dark recessed box that draws its items inside |\n    | `keyhole` | per key shape: iron round, warded cross, gear toothed, bone skull, ward discs |\n    | `plaque` | a stone tablet with dark glyph dashes |\n    | `grate`, `pipe`, `chain`, `gearWall` (rotating), `eyeRelief` | decor |\n    | `candle` | a holder, a wax stick and a flame glow when lit, paired with its light |\n    | `greatLock` | a big wheel with rune glow, spun over 2 s |\n    | `undergate` | a great door with 3 keyholes and 7 bolt bars that slide when a ward goes in |\n    | `cage` | bars |\n    | `shrine` | a ring of tiny rat statues |\n    | `clockFace` | a dial with 4 gear sockets and hands that move once the clock is whole |\n    | `altarSlab` | a floor slab |\n    | `stairs` | the kit's `stair` (down), plus `stairUp` |\n    | `pitEdge` | a dark hole with a lip; a bridge slab when bridged |\n    | `plate` | the kit's |\n    | `teleporterField` | a soft swirl glow, only when not silent |\n\n  - **Floor items:** pen models at the quadrant spots of the visible cells (`onDraw`).\n  - **Monsters:** cards (`world.mob` with `rig`, `blob` or `orb`) are steered toward their slot's position with `vx`/`vy` as the kit does (`fly: true` for fliers). Their `anim` comes from the sim: attack phase, hurt flash, `die` pose, sink. Pen-drawn creatures are drawn in `onDraw` from their sim state and a local animation clock (§6.3).\n  - **Projectiles and FX:** `world.glow` for bolts and orbs, pen bars for lightning, `game.particles` for sparks, embers, smoke and damage `text`, and `world.arc` for floor telegraphs (Bolt Rain).\n  - **First-person overlay:** with `world.overlay.pen`, draw the striking member's weapon swinging across its side of the view: left for places 1, 3 and 5, right for 2, 4 and 6. The crossbow rises and kicks; a caster's hand glows in the spell's colour.\n  - **Hover outlines and name tags:** project with `world.project`, then draw them in the HUD.\n- **NullView** implements the same interface (`enter(floor)`, `frame(r)`, `event(e)`, `pick(sx, sy)`) as no-ops for Node.\n\n### 6.3 Creature recipes\n\nThe sizes follow the engine's guidance (heroes `size` 1.2 to 1.4, bosses larger). Every rig gets a real palette.\n\n| Creature | Build | Recipe | Animation notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Drain Rat | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 3.6, ears: 'cat', tail: true, feet: true, mouth: 'fangs', colors: { base: '#6a5a50', dk: '#3e342e', lt: '#9a8a7a', eye: '#ff6a4a' } }` | fast squash scurry; the wind-up is a rear-back squash |\n| Bloat Leech | pen | 5 balls (r 4 → 2.5) along a sine curve on the floor, `#b89a9a` with `#7a5a5a` rings; a mouth ring of 6 small balls; a wet glint | the body undulates; it lunges out 6 units on the strike |\n| Latchkin | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: .85, build: 'chibi', hunch: .5, hood: true, outfit: 'tunic', bladeLen: 5, eyeGlow: '#ffd24a', colors: { skin: '#7a8a5a', hair: '#4a3a2a', cloth: '#6a4a32', pants: '#3a2e22', metal: '#9a9aa8' } }`, plus a pen ring of keys at the belt | the `thrust` move; it stays in a crouch-run while fleeing |\n| Drain Ooze | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 8, face: 'front', mouth: true, colors: { base: '#5a8a3a', dk: '#2e5a22', lt: '#9ad06a', spec: '#e8ffd0' } }` | a slow wobble; it slams by squashing down; it splashes green particles |\n| Rat Knot | pen | 6 rat-body balls in a ring with ear cones, tails as tubes knotted at the middle | the ring wobbles and turns; two bites a strike |\n| Snick, the Latch-Boss | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.0, build: 'bulky', hunch: .3, hat: { style: 'crown', color: '#c8a040' }, armor: true, outfit: 'coat', bladeLen: 9, eyeGlow: '#ffd24a', colors: { skin: '#7a8a5a', cloth: '#5a3a2a', plate: '#a08040' } }`, plus a pen cape of hanging keys | the `overhead` move; it rattles its keys at 50% when it calls for help |\n| Tinker Skeleton | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.2, build: 'skeleton', outfit: 'coat', bladeLen: 7, colors: { bone: '#d8cfb4', cloth: '#5a4030', metal: '#8a8a90' } }`, plus a pen hammer head on the blade | the `overhead` and `slash` moves; it collapses into bones on death |\n| Rustling | card, `E.Blob` | `{ R: 4.2, horns: true, feet: true, mouth: true, colors: { base: '#b8642a', dk: '#7a3a18', lt: '#e8a060' } }` | the horns twitch; it throws rust-flake particles when it hits |\n| Brass Spider | pen | abdomen ball r 7 and cephalothorax r 4.5 in `#b8923a`; 8 legs of 2 tubes each with procedural tetrapod gait (sine phase lifts); 4 red eye glows | legs step; it lunges on the strike; it falls apart into parts on death |\n| Clockwork Sentinel | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.6, build: 'bulky', armor: true, hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#8a6a3a' }, bladeLen: 14, eyeGlow: '#ff8a3a', colors: { cloth: '#6a4a2a', plate: '#b08a4a', metal: '#c8a868', skin: '#5a4a3a' } }`, plus a pen wind-up key turning on its back | the `twohand` move with a 0.8 s wind-up; the key spins faster during it |\n| Lidless Hound | pen | a quadruped (adapt the 3D horror kit's dogs, `src/starter3d/40-horror.js`): pale `#c8b8b0`, smooth eyeless head, long jaw | run, leap and bite |\n| Gloam Seer | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', outfit: 'robe', hood: true, weapon: 'staff', eyeGlow: '#8ae0ff', colors: { cloth: '#d8d0e8', hair: '#3a2a4a', skin: '#b8b0c8', trim: '#6a4a9a' } }`, plus an eye-sigil glow over the staff | the `cast` pose while charging a Locking Bolt (cyan glow growing) |\n| Gloam Warden | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.35, build: 'heroic', armor: true, hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#2a2434' }, weapon: 'staff', eyeGlow: '#e8e8ff', colors: { cloth: '#2a2434', plate: '#4a4458', metal: '#9a98a8', skin: '#b8b0c8' } }`, plus a pen halberd blade on the staff | the `thrust` move (reaches two cells) |\n| Gazer | card orb plus pen | an orb `{ color: '#e8a040', r: 4 }`; pen iris (a flattened ball `#3a8a6a`), pupil, two lid slabs, 3 fin cones | blinks; the pupil tracks the party; it glows before Spark Gaze |\n| Lockjaw Golem | card, `E.Humanoid` | `{ size: 1.9, build: 'bulky', armor: true, weapon: null, eyeGlow: '#7ad8ff', colors: { cloth: '#3a3e46', plate: '#5a606a', skin: '#4a4e56' } }`, plus a pen **padlock head** (box body and shackle tube) instead of a hat | the `haymaker` move; heavy footstep shakes |\n| **The Bolt-Holder** | pen | an eye ball r 14 (sclera `#e8e0c8` with red vein bars); a flattened amber iris r 7 (`#e8a030`) facing the party; a black pupil r 3.5 that dilates; upper and lower lid slabs that blink and narrow for the Gaze; **7 radial iron bolts** (bars 22 long and 2.5 thick, with 5×5×3 heads) that slide out 2 per Great Lock (the 7th, the keystone, never moves); cyan lightning arcs (jagged pen bars) between neighbouring bolt heads; a ±3 bob; an amber `world.light`; red tint and crack lines in phase 3 | it must not read as a beholder: no eyestalks, no mouth, no tentacles. It reads as a caged iron lantern-eye. |\n| Ghosts (race) | card, `E.Humanoid` | a hooded cloak in the player's seat colour, `fade 0.45`, a lantern glow in the seat colour, and the hub name as a HUD tag | they glide between the cells they report |\n\n**People** (portraits and cutscenes):\n- the party (§7.9);\n- Keywarden Imelda Strake: heroic, band crown, coat, navy and silver;\n- Magister Abel Lintel: robe, pointed hat, long white hair;","numLines":90,"startLine":877,"totalLines":2131}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013kjf32HXyfE4dDQLBwjMQa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
