{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QRhfTJKa5dz8LutRSvPBBZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1996\t## 14. Testing\n1997\t\n1998\t### 14.1 The one command\n1999\t\n2000\t`node tests/run.mjs [suite …] [--fast]`, run from the dev folder.\n2001\t\n2002\t- It runs every suite in §14.3 by default; `--fast` skips the browser suites, and naming suites runs only those.\n2003\t- **It prints only failures** (`FAIL <suite>: <check>: <detail>`) and **one final line**: `412 passed, 0 failed · 11 suites · 38.4 s`.\n2004\t- The exit code is 1 on any failure. Rerun it only after changing the code a suite covers.\n2005\t\n2006\t### 14.2 The Node harness (as in `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs`)\n2007\t\n2008\t- Load `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, then every `src/` file in ORDER, into a `vm` context.\n2009\t- **Stand-ins:**\n2010\t  - `window` (the context itself), `addEventListener() {}`, `location { hash: '', search: '' }`;\n2011\t  - `matchMedia(q) → { matches: q === flags.coarse, addEventListener() {} }`;\n2012\t  - a Map-backed `localStorage`;\n2013\t  - `navigator { getGamepads: () => [] }`;\n2014\t  - `performance`;\n2015\t  - an `AIHub` stub that is inactive by default.\n2016\t- `E.World3D` is absent, so the game uses `NullView` and skips the 3D boot steps.\n2017\t- **Driving it.** `game.advance(seconds)` (exact 1/120 s steps); `game.input.tap(action)`, `hold(action, on)` and `press(code)` (pad and key codes); `input.feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y)` for the mouse.\n2018\t- **`game.debug`** is the handle the tests read:\n2019\t\n2020\t  | Member | What it does |\n2021\t  |---|---|\n2022\t  | `snapshot()` | scene, floor, cell, dir, the party (HP, food, statuses, cooldowns), nearby monsters, flags, the Hand, the open UI screen and its focus id |\n2023\t  | `state()` | the full sim state |\n2024\t  | `hash()` | the state's hash |\n2025\t  | `cmd(c)` | injects a command |\n2026\t  | `warp(floor, x, y, dir)` | moves the party |\n2027\t  | `give(id)` | adds an item |\n2028\t  | `cheats` | the cheat toggles |\n2029\t  | `bot` | the walkthrough runner |\n2030\t  | `layout(screen, W, H)` | every widget's rect, for the overflow test |\n2031\t\n2032\t### 14.3 Suites and what they check\n2033\t\n2034\t| Suite | Covers |\n2035\t|---|---|\n2036\t| `lint` | Every map is rectangular and walled. Every legend character is known. Every wall feature stands on an open cell facing a wall. Every wire's ids, every item, monster, spell and text id, and every lock and key pair exist. Stairs pair up. **The walkthrough reachability and sealed checks** for every floor and branch (the planning script's logic, §7.4). There is no unused text id, and no `src/` sim file breaks the layer rule. |\n2037\t| `movement` | steps, turns, strafes, the buffer and repeat; bumps on walls, doors and monsters; the timing of arrival effects; the head-bob setting; stairs and floor cards |\n2038\t| `features` | each door, gate, lock (key used up, picking, warded refusal), magic seal (spell, scroll, wand), secret wall, illusion, plate (hold, latch, toggle; party, item and monster weight; small monsters don't count), dart trap (and disarm), pit, bridge, trapdoor and landing, teleporter (silent; the loop count and hint; the switch), spinner (seeded), lever, button and its window, catch, alcove (accepts, returns), candles in sequence and the wrong order, Great Locks |\n2039\t| `items` | equip rules (class, two-handed, quiver stacks); pack moves; the Hand (take from the front or own cell, stow, put down, throw range and landing, a throw onto a plate, into a pit, hitting a monster); use (eat, drink, read, scribe); rust; stolen items returned when the thief dies |\n2040\t| `combat` | to-hit and damage with a fixed seed (expected values over 10,000 rolls within bands); crits; cooldowns and the DEX scaling; rows and reach; missiles and ammo recovery; Party Strike choosing the right hands; flank and rear targeting; telegraph dodges (a step during the wind-up makes it miss); re-engaging; statuses ticking and curing |\n2041\t| `monsters` | waking by sight and noise; hunting with A* and flanking around a full cell; keepAway and ranged Seers; fleeing and stealing Latchkins; fliers over pits; cell capacity by size; drops; the boss's phases, locks, relock, absorbing lightning, summons and its attacks' telegraphs and dodges |\n2042\t| `magic` | every spell's effect and target; slot tables; memorizing and praying persisting; rest refills; scroll casting; wands' charges; the Robe's extra slot |\n2043\t| `camp` | refusal near enemies; heal per hour; cleric auto-Mend; interruptions (seeded; safe rooms; the wanderer budget); food drain and starving; Eat; level-up timing (at once or on rest) |\n2044\t| `progress` | XP split and multipliers; thresholds; HP and slots on level-up; deeds; Down and Dead rules; Raise (spell, scroll, shrine); game over; NPCs joining, the full-party path for Veil, dismissing |\n2045\t| `save` | save at a sample point on each floor, then load: the same `hash()`; the version field; a bad save is refused gracefully |\n2046\t| `determinism` | the same seed and command script give the same hash twice, and the same again after a save and load mid-script |\n2047\t| `ui` | title → New Game → Quick Start → skip intro → play. Every screen opens and closes; focus moves by d-pad and by mouse hover; carry and place in the Party screen; Cast targeting; Camp → Rest, Memorize, Formation; Map; Journal; dialogue choices. **Prompts follow the last device** (`label()` and the badges for keyboard, pad and mouse). The **Xbox setting turns ✕ into A**. The pause menu has Dev Mode, which disappears in a session. Text overflow at 320×240 and 427×240. |\n2048\t| `dev` | each slider changes its system (e.g. Monster HP × 2 doubles a spawned rat's HP); Reset restores every default; every cheat works; Warp to every waypoint; spawning; storage persists |\n2049\t| `attract` | 10 s idle on the title starts it, 9.9 s does not; each vignette runs to its end with no errors; any key, button, stick or pointer input exits within one step to the title; it doesn't write saves or settings; on the touch flag the notice shows and the attract mode still runs |\n2050\t| `babble` | `plan()` is deterministic; vowels pick their formants; punctuation sets pauses and contours; profiles differ |\n2051\t| `hub` (Node) | the stub becomes active: the title is skipped; `connect` gets `ghost` and `[1, 4]`; `ready()` is called once with no input; the card answers ready and more; play starts at `time() ≥ 0`; sends stay at 10 Hz or less, unreliable; progress about every second; `result` once on the finish (a time), a wipe or `time-up` (a score); fake messages make ghosts; `leave` removes one; `end` stops input and sound; no Save or Dev Mode in session menus; Options is ignored while Create is held |\n2052\t| **`playthrough`** | §14.4 |\n2053\t| `browser` (Playwright) | §14.5 |\n2054\t| `harness` (Playwright) | §14.5 |\n2055\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40","uuid":"b968f2ee-2a69-4e82-ae0c-efe6c3f91872","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:49:33.613Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 14. Testing\n\n### 14.1 The one command\n\n`node tests/run.mjs [suite …] [--fast]`, run from the dev folder.\n\n- It runs every suite in §14.3 by default; `--fast` skips the browser suites, and naming suites runs only those.\n- **It prints only failures** (`FAIL <suite>: <check>: <detail>`) and **one final line**: `412 passed, 0 failed · 11 suites · 38.4 s`.\n- The exit code is 1 on any failure. Rerun it only after changing the code a suite covers.\n\n### 14.2 The Node harness (as in `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs`)\n\n- Load `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, then every `src/` file in ORDER, into a `vm` context.\n- **Stand-ins:**\n  - `window` (the context itself), `addEventListener() {}`, `location { hash: '', search: '' }`;\n  - `matchMedia(q) → { matches: q === flags.coarse, addEventListener() {} }`;\n  - a Map-backed `localStorage`;\n  - `navigator { getGamepads: () => [] }`;\n  - `performance`;\n  - an `AIHub` stub that is inactive by default.\n- `E.World3D` is absent, so the game uses `NullView` and skips the 3D boot steps.\n- **Driving it.** `game.advance(seconds)` (exact 1/120 s steps); `game.input.tap(action)`, `hold(action, on)` and `press(code)` (pad and key codes); `input.feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y)` for the mouse.\n- **`game.debug`** is the handle the tests read:\n\n  | Member | What it does |\n  |---|---|\n  | `snapshot()` | scene, floor, cell, dir, the party (HP, food, statuses, cooldowns), nearby monsters, flags, the Hand, the open UI screen and its focus id |\n  | `state()` | the full sim state |\n  | `hash()` | the state's hash |\n  | `cmd(c)` | injects a command |\n  | `warp(floor, x, y, dir)` | moves the party |\n  | `give(id)` | adds an item |\n  | `cheats` | the cheat toggles |\n  | `bot` | the walkthrough runner |\n  | `layout(screen, W, H)` | every widget's rect, for the overflow test |\n\n### 14.3 Suites and what they check\n\n| Suite | Covers |\n|---|---|\n| `lint` | Every map is rectangular and walled. Every legend character is known. Every wall feature stands on an open cell facing a wall. Every wire's ids, every item, monster, spell and text id, and every lock and key pair exist. Stairs pair up. **The walkthrough reachability and sealed checks** for every floor and branch (the planning script's logic, §7.4). There is no unused text id, and no `src/` sim file breaks the layer rule. |\n| `movement` | steps, turns, strafes, the buffer and repeat; bumps on walls, doors and monsters; the timing of arrival effects; the head-bob setting; stairs and floor cards |\n| `features` | each door, gate, lock (key used up, picking, warded refusal), magic seal (spell, scroll, wand), secret wall, illusion, plate (hold, latch, toggle; party, item and monster weight; small monsters don't count), dart trap (and disarm), pit, bridge, trapdoor and landing, teleporter (silent; the loop count and hint; the switch), spinner (seeded), lever, button and its window, catch, alcove (accepts, returns), candles in sequence and the wrong order, Great Locks |\n| `items` | equip rules (class, two-handed, quiver stacks); pack moves; the Hand (take from the front or own cell, stow, put down, throw range and landing, a throw onto a plate, into a pit, hitting a monster); use (eat, drink, read, scribe); rust; stolen items returned when the thief dies |\n| `combat` | to-hit and damage with a fixed seed (expected values over 10,000 rolls within bands); crits; cooldowns and the DEX scaling; rows and reach; missiles and ammo recovery; Party Strike choosing the right hands; flank and rear targeting; telegraph dodges (a step during the wind-up makes it miss); re-engaging; statuses ticking and curing |\n| `monsters` | waking by sight and noise; hunting with A* and flanking around a full cell; keepAway and ranged Seers; fleeing and stealing Latchkins; fliers over pits; cell capacity by size; drops; the boss's phases, locks, relock, absorbing lightning, summons and its attacks' telegraphs and dodges |\n| `magic` | every spell's effect and target; slot tables; memorizing and praying persisting; rest refills; scroll casting; wands' charges; the Robe's extra slot |\n| `camp` | refusal near enemies; heal per hour; cleric auto-Mend; interruptions (seeded; safe rooms; the wanderer budget); food drain and starving; Eat; level-up timing (at once or on rest) |\n| `progress` | XP split and multipliers; thresholds; HP and slots on level-up; deeds; Down and Dead rules; Raise (spell, scroll, shrine); game over; NPCs joining, the full-party path for Veil, dismissing |\n| `save` | save at a sample point on each floor, then load: the same `hash()`; the version field; a bad save is refused gracefully |\n| `determinism` | the same seed and command script give the same hash twice, and the same again after a save and load mid-script |\n| `ui` | title → New Game → Quick Start → skip intro → play. Every screen opens and closes; focus moves by d-pad and by mouse hover; carry and place in the Party screen; Cast targeting; Camp → Rest, Memorize, Formation; Map; Journal; dialogue choices. **Prompts follow the last device** (`label()` and the badges for keyboard, pad and mouse). The **Xbox setting turns ✕ into A**. The pause menu has Dev Mode, which disappears in a session. Text overflow at 320×240 and 427×240. |\n| `dev` | each slider changes its system (e.g. Monster HP × 2 doubles a spawned rat's HP); Reset restores every default; every cheat works; Warp to every waypoint; spawning; storage persists |\n| `attract` | 10 s idle on the title starts it, 9.9 s does not; each vignette runs to its end with no errors; any key, button, stick or pointer input exits within one step to the title; it doesn't write saves or settings; on the touch flag the notice shows and the attract mode still runs |\n| `babble` | `plan()` is deterministic; vowels pick their formants; punctuation sets pauses and contours; profiles differ |\n| `hub` (Node) | the stub becomes active: the title is skipped; `connect` gets `ghost` and `[1, 4]`; `ready()` is called once with no input; the card answers ready and more; play starts at `time() ≥ 0`; sends stay at 10 Hz or less, unreliable; progress about every second; `result` once on the finish (a time), a wipe or `time-up` (a score); fake messages make ghosts; `leave` removes one; `end` stops input and sound; no Save or Dev Mode in session menus; Options is ignored while Create is held |\n| **`playthrough`** | §14.4 |\n| `browser` (Playwright) | §14.5 |\n| `harness` (Playwright) | §14.5 |\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1996,"totalLines":2145}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QRhfTJKa5dz8LutRSvPBBZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
